(4, NULL, 'ECOPRINT: PLASTIC BOTTLE RECYCLING SYSTEM USING REAL-TIME OBJECT DETECTION WITH INCENTIVIZED PRINTING SERVICES AT CSPC ICTU', 'Developing a Reverse Vending Machine (RVM) with incentivized printing services required considerable time in understanding both software and hardware components. To meet this need, the researchers developed EcoPrint: Plastic Bottle Recycling System Using Real-Time Object Detection with Incentivized Printing Services at CSPC ICTU. The system does not only focus on collecting recyclable plastic bottles but also provides users with printing privileges as a reward. When a user inserts a plastic bottle into the machine, they earn EcoPrint Credit Points which can be used to access printing services in the ICTU or other participating offices. The system underwent Black Box Testing to ensure functionality and reliability. Integration, performance, and security testing were all conducted, and results showed that the system met both the client’s and project requirements. The development followed the Scrum Agile Methodology, allowing continuous collaboration, feedback, and adaptation throughout the project. Interviews with ICTU, GSU, and maintenance personnel helped the researchers understand existing recycling challenges and potential concerns in deploying the RVM. EcoPrint uses RFID authentication for machine access and social authentication for the web system. A YOLOv8n model running on Raspberry Pi 4 performs real-time bottle detection and classification, while an ultrasonic sensor measures bottle size to assign corresponding credit value. Credits are transmitted to the database through a REST API. The web system, built using CodeIgniter 4, provides dashboards and printing access for users and administrators. Integration testing used formulated test cases, performance testing was conducted using Apache JMeter, and security testing was performed using OWASP ZAP, with detected vulnerabilities corrected to improve the system. In the conducted test, the system was able to achieve a 0.99 arithmetic mean score in integration, achieved a performance of 2.1 second average response time with huge load of requests, and the tool was only able to detect informational risks during the security testing. With the results obtained the system, it passed all the testing proposed, quality was assured, and deployment was achieved.', 'Kenneth Leonard M. Buquid, Eman S. Escuro, Cindy T. Oscoro', '[0.05583418905735016, 0.7357162237167358, -3.318598747253418, -0.889382004737854, 1.6181957721710205, -0.7023741006851196, -0.009564556181430817, 0.8618379235267639, -0.1343933343887329, 0.23915021121501925, 0.2152787148952484, 0.05803302302956581, 0.9586758613586426, -0.9853380918502808, -0.3579811751842499, -0.27608901262283325, -0.12051209062337875, -1.0728439092636108, -1.2381372451782229, 0.36914676427841187, 0.24264320731163025, -1.1617789268493652, -0.6561945080757141, -0.4238136112689972, 1.690916895866394, 0.5833969116210938, 0.30764493346214294, -0.08859680593013763, 0.3690755367279053, -0.2898615896701813, 0.04989065229892731, -1.002941608428955, -0.268371045589447, -1.3726576566696167, -0.3776771426200866, -0.8778078556060791, 1.5819026231765747, -0.0647071897983551, 0.8635603785514832, 0.833077073097229, -0.5589772462844849, 0.9019147157669068, 0.2162835597991943, -0.4103413224220276, 0.7848321199417114, 0.545933187007904, 0.8542366027832031, 0.5296289920806885, 1.0877000093460083, -0.752900242805481, 0.8686232566833496, -0.4157910943031311, -1.076727032661438, 0.8984109163284302, 0.847776472568512, -0.2759650945663452, -0.576887845993042, 0.4003087282180786, 0.44192978739738464, -1.01417076587677, 0.5687633752822876, 2.515019416809082, -0.8580683469772339, 1.7882295846939087, 0.7116312980651855, 0.04042264446616173, 0.4966234564781189, 0.20780102908611295, 0.830743670463562, -0.7863036394119263, 0.5501179695129395, -0.46375784277915955, 0.3330354690551758, 0.17316633462905884, 0.030689716339111328, 0.2047146260738