(6, NULL, 'WEB-BASED FINANCIAL MANAGEMENT AND CLEARANCE SYSTEM FOR STUDENT ORGANIZATION', 'Manual financial processes with student organizations often lead to delays, inaccurate records, and lack of transparency. To address these challenges, this study developed a Web-Based Financial Management and Clearance System for Student Organization. The system integrates payment monitoring, financial tracking, expense entry, clearance generation, and reporting into a single centralized platform. Through this automation, officers can manage financial data more efficiently, while students receive direct access to their balances, obligations, and clearance status timely. The system was developed using the Scrum Agile methodology, allowing continuous improvement and refinements based on user feedback and functional requirements. Testing results confirmed the overall effectiveness of the system. User Acceptance Testing obtained an overall score of 0.99, indicating that the system meets user expectations and supports efficient workflows. Black Box Testing also verified that the features perform as intended and produce correct outputs. The automation of financial records minimized human error, reduced manual workload, and strengthened accountability in fund management. It also improved data accuracy and promoted transparency in financial reporting, ensuring that all transactions are all well documented and easily traceable for auditing purposes. As the system becomes integrated into organizational activities, its stands as a practical and modern solution that supports transparency, speeds up financial processes, and improves student services within the Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges.', 'APRIL B. ABONITA, MICHAELA M. CEZAR, MARK BRYAN S. LUCAS', '[0.5077416896820068, 1.064427137374878, -3.348827362060547, -0.5356417894363403, 0.6439511775970459, -0.12283281236886978, 1.345454216003418, 0.8462967872619629, 0.7186866998672485, 0.7437778115272522, -0.011012086644768717, -0.12003916