(10, NULL, 'INTEGRATED CAMPUS REPAIR, ICT, AND VEHICLE REQUEST SYSTEM FOR CAMARINES SUR POLYTECHNIC COLLEGES', 'The Integrated Campus Repair, ICT, and Vehicle Request System developed for Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges aims to resolve problems encountered in processing requests manually. These problems include manual processing, errors in requests, and problems in document tracking. Other problems that the system aims to resolve include delays in processing requests, tracking requests, and managing submitting approvals. The system developed is a unified platform that allows users to digitally submit and track requests to all Campus premises. The system is a project developed under Scrum Agile Methodology where researchers designed the system while receiving feedback to adjust the construction to the needs of the user. Final system features include request tracking, automated email notifications, Role-based access control, and a system that collects requests. The system executed features were reviewed with a Unit Testing to inspect subsections of a system. The system\'s Usability and User Acceptance Tests as well as the system Security Tests confirmed that core and additional modules of the system worked. The system allows admins to streamline the way Campus Repair, ICT and Vehicle requests are processed and reduces the time taken to processed, recorded for correction, and responded to requests. From a campus service point of view, the system is a fast, effective, fully digitalized system for campus employees.', 'Mia B. Landagan, Joycel C. Llagas, Carl Lawrence S. Maranion', '[-0.32413285970687866, 0.4216775894165039, -3.19746732711792, -0.608141303062439, 1.613033652305603, -1.0935348272323608, 0.5638355016708374, 1.3318719863891602, 0.2302584946155548, -0.49829310178756714, 0.460687518119812, -0.7541424036026001, 0.9099973440170288, -0.2863882780075073, -0.4052150845527649, 0.023076746612787247, 0.15427923202514648, -0.5307015180587769, -1.729610800743103, 0.88