(12, NULL, 'MULTI - BRANCH SALES AND INVENTORY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR JEANLEX HARDWARE', 'Jeanlex Hardware faces challenges managing sales and inventory across its multiple branches due to manual, paper-based processes that are often time-consuming, inconsistent, and prone to human error. These inefficiencies hinder accurate stock monitoring, real-time sales tracking, and timely decision-making across the organization. To address these issues, the researchers developed the Multi-Branch Sales and Inventory Management System for Jeanlex Hardware, an integrated web-based solution designed to centralize, streamline, and automate sales and inventory operations across all branches. The system was developed using the Agile Scrum methodology, enabling iterative development and continuous refinement based on stakeholder feedback. The primary web application, built with the CodeIgniter PHP framework and a MySQL database, manages core business processes, including product inventory, branch stock transfers, sales monitoring, role-based access, purchase orders, and automated report generation. To ensure accurate, synchronized data across branches, the system uses real-time data handling via API- based communication between branch terminals and the central server. This enables immediate updates on stock levels, sales transactions, and branch activities. For secure access, the system employs role-based authentication and encrypted data transmission. System validation included Black Box Testing to assess functional accuracy, usability, reliability, and performance. In addition, a comprehensive User Acceptance Evaluation was conducted among staff and administrative personnel using a standardized questionnaire model. Results of the evaluation confirmed the system’s effectiveness and readiness for deployment. Performance and security testing results demonstrated stable, responsive, and secure operation under peak transaction loads, ensuring reliable deployment across all branches.', 'S