(15, NULL, 'KAWÁYANHUB: THE ONLINE MARKETPLACE FOR BAMBOO CRAFTS IN PAWILI, BULA', 'KawáyanHub is a web and mobile e-commerce platform designed to modernize the bamboo craft industry in Pawili, Bula by digitizing how artisans manage operations and connect with customers. It addresses issues with manual transactions, limited online visibility, and operational inefficiencies while promoting cultural craftsmanship and expanding market reach. Built using the Agile Scrum method, the system evolved iteratively through user feedback and collaboration to better meet stakeholder needs. Key features include Augmented Reality (AR) previews, 3D product visualization, pre-order scheduling for production planning, and product customization, all aimed at enhancing customer experience and equipping artisans with practical digital tools. The system underwent black-box evaluation—covering requirement-based, compatibility, and stress testing—which verified its reliability, achieving ratings of 0.99 and 0.84, with stress testing averaging a 1.2-second response time. Deployed in a cloud-based hosting environment, KawáyanHub enables bamboo craftsmen to showcase products online, reach more customers, and streamline order and payment processes. The study helped simplify transactions, improve product visibility expand market reach, and enhance customer satisfaction, successfully implementing AR and 3D features through DeepLink for product visualization. Results indicate that the platform can handle typical user operations efficiently and maintain acceptable performance levels under peak traffic. The researchers recommend that future researchers examine additional business process aspects and further reduce 3D model load times. As a digital hub for Pawili’s bamboo artisans, KawáyanHub shows how technology can preserve culture, improve livelihoods, and foster community-driven economic growth.', 'Julius Caesar A. Naag IV, Stephen Andrew C. Noblesala, Vladimir P. Tortoles', '[-0.508241415023803