.0860459804534912, -0.12229378521442412, -0.4445788860321045]', NULL, '2025', 'BSIT', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published'),
(18, NULL, 'SCHOOL MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR LOURDES PROVINCIAL HIGH SCHOOL', 'The increasing demand for digital transformation in educational institutions highlights the need for efficient and reliable administrative systems. Lourdes Provincial High School (LPHS) continues to utilize manual, paper-based processes for enrollment and records management, resulting in inefficiencies and data inaccuracies. This study aimed to design, develop, and evaluate a web-based School Management System (SMS) for LPHS to automate essential administrative and academic processes. The system was developed using the Extreme Programming (XP) software development methodology and implemented using HTML5, CSS, JavaScript, PHP (CodeIgniter 4), and MySQL. System evaluation employed Black Box Testing, including Functional, Performance, Security, and User Acceptance Testing (UAT). The respondents were students, teachers, administrators, and IT experts. UAT results revealed an overall weighted mean of 4.63 for students, 4.82 for teachers, and 5.00 for administrators, all verbally interpreted as Highly Acceptable. The results confirm that the developed system effectively enhances operational efficiency, data accuracy, and accessibility at LPHS. It is therefore recommended that the school fully adopt the system and consider future enhancements to further improve functionality and scalability. The study also serves as a reference for similar public secondary schools seeking to modernize their administrative processes through web-based solutions.', 'Joshua Philip I. De Lima II, Joe Harris D. Hosana, Ian Clark N. Beltran', '[-0.38216081261634827, 0.6208798885345459, -3.699195384979248, -1.557308316230774, -0.13769835233688354, -0.2410006672143936, -0.0015460625290870669, 0.33004432916641235, 0.6257468461990356, 0.2540917992591858, 0.09930898994207382, -0.2421550750732422, 2.8308277130126953, 0.29749488830566406, -0.12189577519893646, 0.033078208565711975, -0.5024260878562927, -1.0002455711364746, -1.402