151978, -0.7806400060653687, -0.559076189994812]', NULL, '2025', 'BSIT', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published'),
(22, NULL, 'PLJOBS: PILI LOCAL JOB MARKET A WEB-BASED PLATFORM FOR CONNECTING LOCAL JOB SEEKERS AND EMPLOYERS', 'Many local government units require effective employment facilitation to connect job seekers with available opportunities. Manual job posting and job matching remain the standard practice in the Public Employment Service Office (PESO) of Pili, Camarines Sur. This traditional approach presents several challenges, including delayed updates, limited job accessibility, and inefficient record management. The study proposed PLJOBS: Pili Local Job Market, a web-based platform designed to centralize job posting and job matching by connecting verified local employers with job seekers in a secure and accessible environment. Using an iterative development approach, the study developed the system and employed a descriptive research method to evaluate its functionality and effectiveness. The developed PLJOBS system underwent Functional, Usability, Compatibility, Stress, and Security Testing using Black Box Testing with defined test cases. Stress testing conducted using Apache JMeter confirmed that the system remained stable under simulated heavy workloads, while security testing using OWASP ZAP revealed no critical vulnerabilities. The study concludes that PLJOBS demonstrates strong potential for improving local employment facilitation, and future work is recommended to enhance usability, strengthen security mechanisms, and integrate AI-based job matching for broader applicability.', 'Rodel C. Sapalaran Jr.', '[-0.5313560366630554, 0.6706003546714783, -3.047114610671997, -0.5410774946212769, 0.795236349105835, -0.4344735145568848, 0.14897753298282623, 0.5753605365753174, 0.4948074519634247, 0.4179226756095886, -0.9631376266479492, -0.34367984533309937, 0.4559091031551361, -0.2188757210969925, -0.21836189925670624, -0.18663281202316284, 0.9379093647003174, -0.7761765718460083, -0.39773064851760864, 0.3116421103477478, 0.2276204526424408, 0.0797942653298378, -0.79193162