(25, NULL, 'PARKMATE: RFID-BASED PARKING MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR CSPC', 'The manual parking monitoring system at Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges (CSPC) presents several operational challenges, including traffic congestion at entry points, inaccurate logbook records, and delayed access to parking data for security audits. These issues reduce the efficiency of security personnel and compromise campus safety. This study aimed to design and develop ParkMate, an RFID-based parking management system that automates vehicle entry and exit logging, improves traffic flow, enhances data accuracy, and supports real-time monitoring for campus parking facilities. The system was developed using RFID technology integrated with a centralized database and an administrative dashboard for the General Services Unit (GSU). System development followed a structured design and implementation process, while functionality and performance were evaluated through system testing and real-time campus demonstrations. Testing results showed a significant reduction in entry and exit processing time compared to the manual system, with logging accuracy reaching 100% during test scenarios. Data retrieval time was reduced from several minutes to near real-time access, and parking slot monitoring achieved full operational reliability during demonstrations. ParkMate successfully addresses the limitations of the existing manual parking system by providing a secure, efficient, and scalable RFID-based solution. The system enhances operational speed, data reliability, and campus security while reducing the workload of security personnel, making it a practical solution for institutional parking management', 'Michael Jay C. Bagacina, Jhana A. Bueno, Jobert C. Niebres, Jeremi E. Saltarin', '[-0.5687159299850464, 0.8155303597450256, -3.173048734664917, 0.10156803578138351, 1.0720081329345703, -0.5188736915588379, 0.6519122123718262, 0.8245359659194946, 0.04851113259792328, -0.32168111205101013, -0.165913194417953