(26, NULL, 'ANITALA: A COMMUNITY-DRIVE N PLANT MAPPING AND GEO-TAGGING WEB APPLICATION FOR HARVEST SELLING AND SHARING', 'AniTala is based on the word Ani (harvest) and Tala (record), and as such is a site where harvests by the community are documented and indexed. This exploration ushered in AniTala: A Community-based Plant Mapping and Geo-Tagging Web Application in Harvest Selling and Sharing, which is a system that would help users map the locations of plants, visualize nearest harvests, and conduct community-based or business sharing or commercial transactions. The system reacts to the limitations of the easily available methodologies, which ease the process of identifying plant harvests in local settings. Using Agile methodology, the research team formulated and developed the platform, including features such as plant geo-tagging, map visualization, user management, and a harvest list. Data gathering was conducted in the Rinconada area, comprising 300 respondents, including 125 farmers, 125 students, 50 agricultural workers, and others. Also, black-box testing strategies were applied to assess system functionality and usability. The results 6.48 and rated it “Highly Accepted” that the AniTala platform is useful to support the mapping of plants and distribution of harvests, allowing customers and users to find out and buy the existing produce in their communities. The platform improves the exposure, creates a partnership with the community, and makes local harvests easy to reach. Future improvements can include the creation of a mobile application, the improvement of plant recognition potential, and an increase in mapping analytics.', 'Djahaira Diana B. Aspa, Ruthiemay T. Esquilador', '[0.6112270951271057, 0.31740739941596985, -3.818183422088623, -0.03657708317041397, 0.35220015048980713, -0.8132080435752869, 0.07660146057605743, 0.1620877981185913, -0.5381133556365967, 0.8510796427726746, 0.9687466025352478, -0.32288187742233276, 3.560749769210815, -0.316868543