(27, NULL, 'ESCHOLAR: A COMPREHENSIVE WEB-BASED SCHOLARSHIP APPLICATION PORTAL CONNECTING GOVERNMENT AND STUDENTS', 'The eScholar Web-Based Scholarship Application Portal is an online portal was created to address the challenges in government scholarship procedure. The main objective of the study is to develop a centralized system that allows students to find scholarships at ease, can submit applications through online, and also allowed them to track their application progress, while on the other hand, administrators and government officials managed the posting management, application assessment and communication that allowed students to be informed. The study used a mixed method approach that combined qualitative interview methods with quantitative survey data and system evaluation results to develop and evaluate the system. The system development used agile methodologies that followed a structure based on data flow diagrams, entity relationship diagrams, and modular functional components. The equivalent partition testing with the use of Puppeteer simulation tool, it showed that all essential system modules worked correctly without discovering any system failures. The User acceptance testing produced a mean rating of 4.51 that showed that the system achieved high levels of usability, simplicity, and usefulness. The evaluation instrument showed high reliability because its Cronbach’s alpha score reached 0.98 which indicates excellent internal consistency. The system maintained a stable performance during stress testing that involved with multiple simulated users at once and security testing proved that the system protected against typical high security threats.', 'Chris Harold S. Brazil, Aemann T. Nueva, Mark Dale Andrie S. Perillo', '[-0.34404799342155457, 0.9782865047454834, -2.8274145126342773, -0.994490385055542, 0.7716547250747681, 0.0772910863161087, 0.26143285632133484, 0.7775176763534546, 1.0284086465835571, 0.7404323816299438, 0.03410246968269348, -0.141832