(28, NULL, 'DESIGNING A POS SYSTEM FOR ENHANCED PRODUCT AND TRANSACTION MANAGEMENT AT DMD FOOD HOUSE IN IRIGA CITY', 'This study presents the design and development of a Point of Sale (POS) System intended to enhance product and transaction management at DMD Food House in Iriga City. The business previously relied on manual processes for ordering, billing, and recording sales, which caused delays, pricing inconsistencies, missing records, and difficulty in monitoring inventory. The proposed web-based POS integrates product and category management, table-based ordering, real-time transaction recording, inventory monitoring, secure user access, and automated receipt and sales report generation. The system was developed using the Extreme Programming (XP) Iterative Software Development Method and was evaluated through Black Box Testing and usability assessment to ensure its functionality, accuracy, and reliability. Results showed that the system significantly improved the speed and accuracy of daily operations, reduced manual workload and transaction errors, and enhanced product stock monitoring. It achieved an overall performance rating of 0.98, indicating that it is fully functional, highly usable, and secure for business use. The system provides a reliable technological solution that supports efficient workflow and better decision-making for DMD Food House. Future enhancements may include mobile compatibility, automated analytics, and integration with digital payment options.', 'Angelyn P. Aleman, Francine Louise N. Libreja, Andrea Nicole Rancapollo', '[-0.6793516874313354, 1.7675330638885498, -3.2759108543395996, -0.6642069816589355, 0.1748398095369339, -1.3225568532943726, 0.3033350110054016, 0.32283708453178406, 0.29045599699020386, -0.7778756618499756, 0.1582869440317154, -0.10055449604988098, 1.4987176656723022, -0.05367988720536232, 0.1011788547039032, 0.0986509919166565, -0.4557056427001953, -0.6117244958877563, -0.9370896816253662, 0.5497403144836426, 0.86832