(29, NULL, 'iBARANGAY: A DIGITAL PLATFORM FOR COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT AND PUBLIC SERVICE MANAGEMENT', 'Barangay San Juan, Bato continues to rely on manual logbooks and paper-based transactions that slow down certificate requests, record keeping, and communication. These issues lead to delays, misplaced files, and limited access to information. To address these gaps, this study developed iBarangay, a web-based information system that centralizes resident profiling, online service requests, incident reporting, and announcement posting. The study aimed to identify problems in the existing manual workflow, design and develop a database-driven system to improve efficiency, evaluate the system using ISO/IEC 25010 quality standards, and validate the system through resident, government, and IT expert assessment. The project used the Agile Extreme Programming model in developing the PHP–MySQL application. System evaluation followed ISO/IEC 25010’s attributes, including functionality, performance efficiency, usability, security, and maintainability. A total of 48 respondents participated: 30 residents, 11 barangay officials, and 7 IT experts. Binary scoring (0 = failed, 1 = passed) and weighted averages were used to analyze the results. Findings show that residents and officials rated functionality and usability with a mean score of 1.00, while IT experts rated performance efficiency, security, and maintainability at 1.00 as well. All sub-characteristics such as modularity, analyzability, time behavior, and confidentiality also scored 1.00, indicating full compliance with the test cases. The study concludes that iBarangay meets its objectives and provides an efficient, user-friendly, and secure solution for barangay operations. Future enhancements may include mobile integration and online payment features.', 'Von Aries P. Bables, Alexander S. Melitante, Christopher T. Pornillos', '[-0.5488134622573853, 0.8489209413528442, -2.8876953125, -0.7305107712745667, 1.2221434116363523, 