(30, NULL, 'WEB-BASED RESORT AND APARTMENT MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR BALANG MARISTELA CORPORATION', 'This research focuses on the development of a Web-Based Resort and Apartment Management System for Balang Maristela Corporation. This aims to improve the efficiency, accuracy, and convenience of managing business operations, customer communications, and reporting compared to manual processes. The project encompasses various functionalities, including user management, booking and reservation systems, payment and billing processing, employee management, notifications, and report generation. However, it has limitations, particularly its reliance on internet connectivity and its applicability being confined to the corporation\'s operations. The study employed agile methodology and mixed-method design for data collection, involving administrators, staff, IT experts, and tenants as respondents. Data was gathered through interviews and questionnaires, analyzed using the arithmetic mean, and interpreted with the Likert Scale. The evaluation included testing the system’s functionality, reliability, compatibility, interaction capability, performance efficiency, and maintainability, in accordance with criteria set in ISO 25010. Findings indicate that the manual processes were plagued by inaccuracy and delays, while the proposed system demonstrated potential to improve real-time information management, garnering a total score of 0.98. Thus, it is concluded that despite its advantages in accessibility and efficiency, the system faces structural instability and significant technical debt, suggesting risks to long-term performance and sustainability.', 'Grazela Khrystal S. Froyalde, Loida B. Gastilo, Jorhi Rainwater S. Rabino', '[-0.2457265853881836, 0.9851405620574952, -3.544299602508545, -0.2293294072151184, -0.3230212330818176, -0.19235152006149292, 0.3358149528503418, -0.4741289019584656, 0.5789081454277039, -0.10710233449935912, -0.6258122324943542, -0.6068180799484253, 1.98066830