(32, NULL, 'EDUCONNECT: A SMART WEB-BASED ACADEMIC MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR STA. JUSTINA NATIONAL HIGH SCHOOL', 'Academic management in secondary schools have to deal with manual and semi-digital processes. These processes lead to inefficiencies, inaccuracies in data, and a lack of communication among stakeholders. This is the case with Sta. Justina National High School (SJNHS), where traditional methods dominate operations. This paper contributes to the field by proposing EduConnect: A Smart Web-Based Academic Management System. EduConnect is designed to automate and streamline the central processes and pent processes of academics and administration. These include enrollment, attendance, grade tracking, scheduling, announcements, and reporting. EduConnect provides role-based access to students, teachers, administrators, and parents. The system is built on a technical stack that includes CodeIgniter 4, PHP, JavaScript, MySQL, HTML 5, and Bootstrap. The system was built using the Agile Software Development Methodology. This is a process that allows for incremental development and refinement based on user feedback. Existing academic workflows were analyzed to identify gaps and difficulty in record keeping, accessibility of information, and communication. EduConnect was assessed using Black Box Testing to meet the requirements of the ISO 25010 software quality model. Use case testing and requirement-based testing scored 0.99 while usability testing was 0.99 and compatibility testing was 1.00 . According to the Nikto Docker security test, EduConnect has proper data and access control along with good security configurations. EduConnect has no critical or high security risks. The third-party findings were also non-impacting. With performance testing using Apache JMeter, the findings show concurrent users, given all 1,809 requests finished with 0 errors, took reasonable time to respond, and recorded 5.20 transactions per second, on average. Overall, EduConnect passed all tests confirming it is operational, user oriented, safe, efficient, and dependable, thereby greatly improving SJNHS’ academic management.', 'Gwyneth L. Buenconsejo, Christian Jay C. Gonzaga, Blessing C. Nachor', '[-0.3063283860683441, 0.5202915072441101, -3.095391750335694, -0.5494371056556702, 0.5388365983963013, -0.3012627363204956, 0.8356411457061768, 0.4734821915626526, 0.87507164478302, 0.9500926733016968, 0.13346663117408752, -0.5100114941596985, 2.2321979999542236, 0.8991171717643738, -0.34209322929382324, -0.9885760545730592, -0.02903849631547928, -0.14612017571926117, -1.5886484384536743, -0.28831911087036133, 0.5368595123291016, -1.2072172164916992, -0.9110252261161804, 0.17502641677856445, 1.5238865613937378, 0.353644460439682, -0.7708001732826233, -0.04930262640118599, -0.29409483075141907, -0.3713495433330536, 1.4039026498794556, -0.18170166015625, 0.1991579383611679, 0.4519687592983246, -0.7400014400482178, -0.47261133790016174, 0.24927304685115817, -0.5815647840499878, -0.4633432924747467, -0.19826224446296692, 0.11107198148965836, -0.4525737166404724, -0.3024601936340332, -1.1269725561141968, 0.26611703634262085, 0.31173956394195557, 0.7892598509788513, -0.3429996967315674, 0.9195969700813292, 0.07793772965669632, 0.5722848773002625, -1.0842002630233765, -0.3808552920818329, 0.746121346950531, 0.6121477484703064, 0.2133471816778183, -0.40295565128326416, 1.527732014656067, -0.15744221210479736, -0.8805117607116699, 2.0228848457336426, 1.6592134237289429, -0.8824434280395508, 0.8692432045936584, 0.6789518594741821, 0.4278281331062317, 0.17039291560649872, 0.7734269499778748, 0.2982943058013916, -0.2008636444807053, 0.12693588435649872, -0.9822335243225098, 0.4130753576755524, -0.3763969242572784, 0.32778283953666687, -0.13914160430431366, 0.29335281252861023, -0.4438621699810028, -0.14091913402080536, 0.6336780190467834, 0.6679149866104126, -0.11189094185829164, 1.2994120121002195, 0.4295728802680969, 1.254818558692932, 0.4707592725753784, -0.779340982437