(38, NULL, 'WAVES: A WEB-BASED WATER LEVEL MONITORING AND EARLY WARNING SYSTEM FOR FLOOD PREPAREDNESS', 'Flooding remains one of the most severe natural hazards in the Philippines, particularly in flood-prone municipalities such as Bula, Camarines Sur. Existing flood monitoring practices rely heavily on manual observation and delayed reporting, limiting timely disaster response. This study presents WAVES: A Web-Based Water Level Monitoring and Early Warning System for Flood Preparedness, a system designed to enhance flood preparedness through real-time environmental monitoring and automated alert dissemination. The system integrates IoT-based sensors that collect water level, rainfall, humidity, and temperature data, which are transmitted and stored in a Firebase Database for instant synchronization. These data are processed through an API and visualized on a web-based dashboard for the Municipal Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Office (MDRRMO). Descriptive analytics are used to present real-time and historical flood trends to support informed decision-making. Automated SMS alerts are triggered when predefined threshold levels are exceeded, providing timely flood warnings and evacuation information to registered residents and barangay officials. System evaluation using black-box testing (functional, integration, and performance testing) and usability testing through the System Usability Scale (SUS) revealed that WAVES is fully functional, reliable, and user-friendly. The results indicate that the system effectively improves situational awareness, response efficiency, and community preparedness for flood events.', 'Dina O. Laresma, Czaerina Nicole Dulfo, John Kenneth S. Pera', '[-0.08537325263023376, -0.06228487938642502, -4.093335151672363, -1.163478970527649, 1.5056660175323486, 0.876357913017273, 0.36104482412338257, 0.0372520349919796, 0.35448768734931946, -1.0337657928466797, -0.11013436317443848, 0.5746974945068359, 1.7877485752105713, 1.2837202548980713,