(40, NULL, 'OLIN: OFFLINE LEARNING INTERFACE – AN OFFLINE-FIRST MOBILE LMS WITH SMART SYNCHRONIZATION AND WEB INTEGRATION FOR CSPC', 'This research introduced the Offline Learning Interface (OLIN), an offline-first mobile learning management system (LMS), developed to mitigate the effects of unreliable internet connectivity on sustained academic access at CSPC. Recognizing that unstable network service directly hinders instruction, the system\'s core objective was to ensure students have guaranteed, uninterrupted access to education via a mobile application, while offering faculty an efficient web platform for course management. The mobile application was designed with an offline-first architecture exclusively for students, utilizing smart synchronization to update data upon connectivity restoration. Conversely, the web application was restricted to instructors for management and oversight. The development methodology followed the Agile Scrum framework. Laravel was used for the web app and React Native with TypeScript was employed for the mobile app. Data management utilized MySQL for the web database and SQLite for local mobile storage. A rigorous black-box testing process was executed involving student end-users, IT experts, and a subject matter expert instructor from the CCS department. The results affirmed high system quality: unit, integration, and security testing all achieved completely functional scores of 1.0. Furthermore, the usability testing attained an excellent and acceptable score of 84.76. The study affirmed that OLIN delivered a viable and robust digital solution, utilizing targeted mobile and web components and intelligent synchronization to overcome connectivity barriers, thereby enhancing the modernization and accessibility of learning delivery at CSPC.', 'Vincent Anthony H. Moreno, Rommel E. Barbonio, Shann Arlly P. Lagdaan', '[-0.955341935157776, 0.8659420609474182, -3.3508009910583496, -1.3552327156066897, 0.6121569871902466, -0.45393010973930