(42, NULL, 'LICOMSIA: CROSS- PLATFORM STUDENT INFORMATION AND ADMISSION SYSTEM FOR LIBON COMMUNITY COLLEGE', 'The demand to introduce high efficiency, accuracy, and accessibility to academic services, LiComSIA was created as a holistic solution to the weaknesses of manual admission and enrollment systems at Libon Community College. It is a cross-platform Student Administration and Admission System that automates and centralizes the most important academic and administrative processes like admission, enrollment, management of grades and handling of academic records. The system decreases paper work, delays in processing and inconsistencies in data and increases the accessibility by students, the faculty and the administrators. LiComSIA was created with the help of state-of-the-art web and mobile technologies and was based on Agile approach to development to allow flexibility and constant enhancement. It has role based access control, secure data manipulation, and real time notification, in order to maintain data privacy and reliability of the system. Students are able to apply, enroll, and access academic information remotely and the faculty and administration are able to access records and reports efficiently. The system was tested in terms of functional, usability, and security. Black Box Testing ensured that all modules worked as per the requirements whereas usability testing with a Likert Scale resulted in high level of user satisfaction over ease of use and interface clarity. Efficient authentication and access control were checked by means of security testing. In general, the findings show that LiComSIA can effectively address the needs of the institutions and users, offering a stable and convenient platform that will facilitate the digital transformation of the Libon Community College.', 'Ricardo F. Osea Jr., Sophia B. Estorninos, Hazel Anne C. Sanorjo', '[-0.4733116626739502, 0.7496339678764343, -2.5111618041992188, -1.3703367710113523, 0.7791628837585449, -0.