(44, NULL, 'SPHERE: CSPC SPACE FACILITY AND EQUIPMENT RENTAL AND EVENT MANAGEMENT SYSTEM', 'This study developed SPHERE: CSPC Space Facility and Equipment Rental and Event Management System, a centralized web-based platform designed to address the inefficiencies of the manual, paper-based booking process used by the Supply and Property Management Office (SPMO) of Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges. The study specifically aimed to identify existing facility and equipment reservation procedures, develop a digital system that automates booking, documentation, and event management, and evaluate the system using Black-Box testing to assess functionality, security, performance, and compatibility. The system was developed through requirements analysis, system design, iterative development, and testing, incorporating features such as real-time availability monitoring, centralized booking management, automated document generation, billing computation, inventory tracking, booking status monitoring, and a QR code–based attendance mechanism. Evaluation results showed that SPHERE met the required quality standards, demonstrating reliable performance, secure data handling, high usability, and cross-device compatibility, while significantly reducing administrative workload and scheduling conflicts and improving transparency and operational efficiency. It is therefore recommended that SPHERE be fully adopted by CSPC and further enhanced through the integration of advanced reporting, expanded attendance analytics, and dynamic facility management to support scalability and continuous institutional digital transformation.', 'Liza Mae B. Cleofe, Katrina G. Luzadas, Jomel G. Tienes', '[-1.4295616149902344, 1.4167890548706057, -3.884935140609741, -0.5124301910400391, -0.2732076644897461, 0.40293508768081665, 1.0107790231704712, 0.615363597869873, 0.4939272105693817, -0.4384561479091644, 0.4401672184467316, -0.17797881364822388, 2.0095438957214355, 0.08108500391244888, 0.4906174838542938,