(46, NULL, 'ARGENT: A WEB-BASED FINANCIAL MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR PHILIPPINE GOOD NEWS INTERNATIONAL', 'The fast advancement of technology has changed the way organizations, including churches, manage financial data. Argent: A Web-based Financial Management System for Philippine Good News International aimed to solve inefficiencies in the PGNI Church\'s financial management, such as mistaken assumptions and delayed reporting. The project\'s primary purpose was to develop a secure and efficient system for automating financial transactions such as budgeting, tithing, offering and fund allocation, incorporating essential features like Cashflow Management, Church Projects and Savings, Reports, Audit Trails, Pledges, Donation and User Access Control, all built on the Laravel framework, PHP v8.2.12, and utilized DOMPDF for generating downloadable financial reports isn PDF format. PayPal Business was integrated as a payment gateway to initially support online subscription-based payments and utilized also a QR- Based donation using GCash and Maya. The Agile Scrum Methodology was used during development to ensure flexibility, adaptability and collaboration. Thorough evaluation utilizing Black box testing revealed high results specifically in functionality garnering 0.832 classified as “Highly Functional”, performance testing yielded 0.952 and classified as “Excellent Performance”, usability testing got an overall mean of 1.643 and classified as “Completely Usable” and security testing garnered the highest score which was 1.00 classified as “Completely Secured”, the results indicate significant developments in financial management through the elimination of manual processes, decreased error rates, and increased transparency.', 'Christine Joy S. Casia, Edison B. Tominio, Missy S. Velitario', '[0.770973801612854, 0.7078151702880859, -3.072991371154785, -0.17661109566688538, 1.0932917594909668, -1.3460359573364258, 0.689104437828064, -0.6949964761734009, 0.3255869150161743, -0.473