(48, NULL, 'GIS- INTEGRATED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR EVANGELICAL CEMETERY IN SANTIAGO, IRIGA CITY', 'The Evangelical Cemetery in Santiago, Iriga City had experienced disadvantages that come along with the traditional way of keeping records, inefficient plot tracking, and limited access to burial information which led to data inaccuracies and service delays. In an attempt to solve the problem, a GIS-Integrated Management System was launched that would be helpful in the modernization of cemetery operations while also taking into consideration the local cultural and religious practices. The aim of the research was to devise, create a web-based system that includes functions for managing burial records, allocating and tracking plots, managing deceased profiles, providing notification services, and visualization of plots based on GIS technology. A black-box testing approach was taken to evaluate the system, wherein different testing methods like functional, integration, security, compatibility, and usability were applied. The total average score of 0.99 was achieved for both functional and integration testing, where integration got the highest rating of 1.00 meaning there was 100% module interaction. Secured, compatible, and usability testing then reported their average scores of 4.50, 4.46, and 4.48, respectively, which were all seen as Highly Functional. It can thus be concluded that the system is able to significantly enhance efficiency, accuracy, data security, and accessibility. Overall, the research work establishes the claim that GIS and web technologies can be easily and effectively combined to create a record management system and service delivery solution that works in a local context.', 'John Rick L. Babila, Maria Lourdes S. Arcilla, John Mark David S. Pajenago', '[0.0943089872598648, 0.936425805091858, -2.8851282596588135, -0.8688305616378784, 0.21949315071105957, 0.10920459032058716, 0.8769974708557129, 0.28982073068618774, 0.07771731168031693, -0.3659038543701