(50, NULL, 'AUGMENTED REALITY MOBILE APPLICATION FOR DIGITAL PRESERVATION AND 3D VISUALIZATION FOR THE CSPC CENTER FOR RINCONADA CULTURE AND THE ARTS', 'The study introduced an innovative Augmented Reality (AR) mobile application and a web-based Content Management System (CMS) designed to preserve and showcase the cultural heritage of the Rinconada region for the CSPC Center for Rinconada Culture and the Arts (CRCA). Developed as a strategic response to the loss of the physical \"Museo Rinconada\" and the ongoing risk of artifact deterioration, the dual-system approach utilizes markerless AR technology to allow the public to visualize interactive 3D models of digitized artifacts within their own physical environments. While the administrative CMS empowers CRCA personnel to manage artifact metadata and secure digital assets, the mobile platform democratizes access to cultural education, overcoming previous geographical and physical limitations. Built using the Agile Extreme Programming (XP) methodology and validated through comprehensive Black Box Testing, the system achieved a functional testing average of 0.97 (Highly Functional) and UI/UX ratings of 1.00 (Excellent) for the CMS and 0.93 (Good) for the mobile app. Additionally, compatibility testing reached averages of 1.00 and 0.91 respectively, while the System Usability Scale (SUS) yielded an overall average of 4.35, interpreted as Acceptable. Ultimately, this digital repository transforms static historical objects into dynamic assets, ensuring the long-term preservation of Rinconada culture while offering a scalable foundation for future enhancements, such as iOS compatibility and integrated community news features.', 'Rondale Rae B. Bufete, Justin Larry R. Dimaiwat, John Lawrence N. Oliveros', '[-0.12684419751167297, 0.8152292966842651, -3.20212459564209, -1.309802770614624, -0.02719329297542572, -0.11250999569892885, 1.6890246868133545, 0.1871059238910675, 0.9358478784561156, 0.12883253395557404, 0.6459213495