(51, NULL, 'CBSTrac: A Web-Based Alumni Tracking System for Central Bicol State University of Agriculture', 'Fragmented alumni records, low participation, and the lack of automated reporting are among the current problems that the Alumni Office of Central Bicol State University of Agriculture (CBSUA) face. This paper introduces CBSTrac, a web-based alumni tracking system for the Central Bicol State University of Agriculture in response to the identified problems. The system includes key features such as alumni onboarding with masterlist cross-checking, profile management, tracer survey, QR code event attendance, job posting using APIs for scraping and fetching, donation tracking, internal messaging, and analytics-based reporting. The researchers found that CBSTrac has the potential to create a centralized place for all alumni employment, involvement and participation information in a near real-time environment with ease of access, organization and analysis. From the results of our black box testing, CBSTrac was rated highly. The Functionality score was (3.77), Usability (3.83), Compatibility Score (3.77), Security Score (3.87), and Performance Score (3.77) giving the overall score of (3.80) which was interpreted as Excellent. The results demonstrated that the CBSTrac is . The findings from this study supported that CBSTrac met its purpose by providing a secure and efficient means of using data, improving the accuracy of data, automating many administrative processes, and enhancing alumni participation and tracking. Additionally, this study lays the foundation for future enhancements that may also explore the implementation of advanced predictive modeling and machine learning to forecast employment trends and further align the university curriculum with evolving industry needs.', 'Dominic Martin A. Escuro, Michael Angelo S. Manzano, Fiona Ll. Rombano', '[-0.140367329120636, -0.1254594624042511, -3.728061199188232, -0.4807925820350647, 0.12563467025756836, -0.00005656