(52, NULL, 'E-GUIDANCE: AN ONLINE APPOINTMENT AND INFORMATION SYSTEM FOR THE CENTER FOR GUIDANCE SERVICES', 'The E-Guidance System aims to modernize the operations at the Center for Guidance Services of Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges (CSPC) by transitioning from manual processes to a digital platform. The problem was that the old system used paper forms, which caused lost records, scheduling errors, and a heavy workload for staff. To fix this, the team built \"E-Guidance,\" a website meant to make booking appointments easy and information more accessible. Used the Agile method to develop the software and tested it with 62 people, including students and staff. The methodology involved Black-Box Testing and surveys to check if the system was easy to use and safe. The numerical results were excellent, showing a perfect 100% success rate in functionality and a 5.0 mean score for user satisfaction. These scores prove the system is \"Highly Functional\" and \"Highly Usable.\" In conclusion, the new system successfully replaced the slow manual steps with a fast, digital process. It keeps student data safe and organized, following strict security rules. The researchers recommend using the system right away to help students better. Future updates should include text message alerts and better data tools to help school leaders make good decisions. This change makes the guidance services modern, reliable, and much faster for everyone at CSPC.', 'Richie B. Bagacina, Princess Hyancinth I. Belza, John Errol N. Borela', '[-1.2109439373016355, 0.6785601377487183, -3.4351418018341064, -0.7935143709182739, 0.5791449546813965, -0.027820708230137825, 1.6004440784454346, 0.6940540075302124, 0.4821850061416626, -0.015843195840716362, 0.5786511898040771, 0.053453750908374786, 1.2284889221191406, 0.5444533228874207, -0.07131414115428925, 0.7160837054252625, 0.6034257411956787, -0.8443464636802673, -1.175929069519043, 0.12912949919700625, 0.5216507315635681, -0.4630583226680755, -0.66429