(54, NULL, 'APPOINTMENT SCHEDULING SYSTEM WITH SMS NOTIFICATION FOR MUNICIPAL AGRICULTURE OFFICE OF BATO', 'Technology has become the go to solution for the modern problems including long queues and controlling the arrival flow of appointees. In fact, private organizations use technology to provide services and fast transaction. But it\'s not only private sectors that are continually trying to transform, but public organizations have also come to acknowledge the importance of automation. Thus, the researchers were inspired to create an appointment for the Municipal Agriculture Office client in the Municipality of Bato. Therefore, this study aims to develop an Appointment Scheduling System with SMS Notification for the Municipal Agriculture Office of Bato in managing appointments, employee availability tracking, and disseminating information. The study used an iterative model as a software development methodology which involves a functional model and allows the researchers to quickly adapt to the constantly changing requirements in every iteration until the system is completely developed. The respondents of this study were limited to the staff of the Municipal Agriculture Office of Bato. The data were obtained using interviews and test cases and were evaluated using the arithmetic mean. The interpretation of data reveals that there are problems in organizing appointments, tracking the availability of employees present in the office, and information dissemination. Furthermore, the developed appointment scheduling system has implemented and automated the manual processes in the existing operations. Thus, the performance evaluation of the system accounts to moderately functional which is ready for deployment. With this, the implementation of Appointment Scheduling System for Municipal Agriculture Office of Bato is highly recommended.', 'WAYNE BENEDICT V. IRAOLA, JOHN CARLO C. DIGAY, GENEIL B. BONDOC, BERNARD BRENNAN N. REGASPI', '[-0.5386528968811035, 0.4767994284629822