(56, NULL, 'BIOMETRIC ATTENDANCE MONITORING WITH PAYROLL SYSTEM IN STO. DOMINGO INSTITUTE', 'Learning new things and accepting them have an impact on the ability to continually innovate for success and progress. One of the developments and advances in the switch from a manual to an automated system. With this, the researchers developed a system that reliable system for using biometrics to track attendance, calculating of salary, and scheduling for Sto. Domingo Institute staff members. Generally, the study intends to create a reliable and user- friendly solution for monitoring attendance, automatic computation of salary, and implement a secure issuance of payslip for the staff of Sto. Domingo Institute. The study used Iterative Software Development Methodology that aims to provide a solution to the client’s problem to make an efficient system and reach the user requirements. Furthermore, this methodology would be the researcher’s instrument as a guide to having a well organize and systematic system development and faster process which avoid a more risk exposure of the system. The respondents were the staffs of Sto. Domingo Institute. In gathering the data, test cases were used to verify the expected functionality of a feature to determine whether or not various features of the system are functioning. The level of performance using Black Box Testing, the developed system was rated by 0.98 in terms of User Acceptance Testing, for Performance Testing it was rated by 0.98, and for Usability Testing, it was also rated 0.96 which is also Highly Functional. Therefore, it’s reasonable to implement the Biometric Attendance Monitoring with Payroll System in Sto. Domingo Institute.', 'Jhemar C. Beato, Jon Kenneth P.Sain, Carmela B. Mata, John Rey S. Ramos, Jimmy A. Tomabdo Jr.', '[0.08897214382886887, 0.8769793510437012, -4.1605024337768555, -0.2048659473657608, -0.29648730158805847, -0.4977756142616272, 1.8023626804351809, -0.7177309989929199, 0.09898052364587784, 0.7528424263