(58, NULL, 'CEBU CALL CENTER ACADEMY INC., (IRIGA BRANCH) INTEGRATED SYSTEM: ADMINISTRATION MANAGEMENT', 'The automation of manual processes in managing documents and other transactions is an excellent tool for an institution. It can reduce the number of printed documents and manage data or information more easily. With these, the study was conducted to develop a system that automates the management of administration at Cebu Call Center Academy Inc., Iriga Branch. Generally, this study determined the problems encountered in the existing manual process and developed a system that enhances the manual process at Cebu Call Center Academy Inc., Iriga Branch. The study utilized a mixed-methods research design and a DevOps model. Data were obtained using an interview guide, questionnaire, and test cases. The respondents were one (1) administrative officer and four (4) trainers from the institution. The result shows that the problems encountered in the existing process are a lack of workforce due to limited manpower, a time-consuming process of locating documents, a tedious process, and a lack of data integrity. Hence, the researchers developed an administration management system with the limited modules of Human Resources, Inventory, Program Guidelines and Job Linkages. The developed system was tested by the developers, eight (8) IT experts, and the end-users. It was tested based on fuzz, integration, and user acceptance testing. As a result, the developed system was completely functional and highly acceptable, which means that it is ready for deployment, all modules are functioning, and free of mistakes and errors. Therefore, it is reasonable to implement the Cebu Call Center Academy Inc., Integrated System: Administration Management.', 'JOHN VINCENT SC. CAMILA, ROSE ANN O. JOVEN, MILDRED E. PERAJA, DON JAY S. RALUTA', '[-0.1858043372631073, 0.4607120156288147, -2.78338623046875, -0.6117969155311584, 0.005452534183859825, -0.6181191802024841, 0.25811654329299927, -0.83710