(64, NULL, 'PROFILING AND RECORD MANAGEMENT OF BCIEERD – AN ENHANCED WEB PORTAL', 'BCIEERD web portal is where events and other research development in the consortium are first disseminated and planned, but it also contains the limited functionalities, least quantity of the dissemination of information and profiling of each member. The Profiling and Record Management of BCIEERD is a web-based platform that aims to enhance the BCIEERD web portal. This web portal can reduce the probability of encountering problems such as time-consuming of reaching all members to be notify of upcoming events or the delayed of dissemination of information. Its primary purpose is to enhance existing administrative operations, such as profiling and record management of each members of the said consortium. The Extreme Programming Lifecycle methodology is used in the study. With the use of purposive sampling for identifying the respondents and Mixed-Method research design to gather quantitative and qualitative data to analyze the results of the study. The respondent of this study were the secretariat of the BCIEERD wherein it consisted of 2 respondents. The questionnaire is used for data gathering. The data gathered were analyzed and interpreted using Arithmetic Mean, level of functionality using test cases. Analysis of the data showed that the developed system was rated with 0.843 which comparable to 84.3% when interpreted verbally as completely functional. The researchers concluded that the development of the “Profiling and Record Management of BCIEERD – An Enhanced Web Portal” can reduced the probability of encountering problems in the area of information dissemination, document storage, collation of submitted proposals, membership profiling, and messaging and chatting.', 'Jim Justine D. Abanes, Samuel Nathan D. Nico B. Caguiron, Joshua R. Obaña', '[0.0634608268737793, 0.9815799593925476, -3.6443393230438232, -1.060625076293945, 1.1535273790359497, -1.365922451019287, 0.4270623922348022