(65, NULL, 'RFID-BASED INTEGRATED COMPUTER LABORATORY EQUIPMENT MANAGEMENT SYSTEM', 'The College of Computer Studies under Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges seeks to employ an easy automation of recording, inventory and monitoring of Computer Laboratory Equipment as much as possible to aid the existing manual process on Computer Laboratories. Based on the findings the following are the problems encountered on manual recording, inventory, monitoring and tracking of borrowed equipment; The data of borrowed equipment is not being recorded, record book is unorganized, recording of Equipment is time consuming and an un-organized list of equipment. With these, this study is conducted to develop a system that will automate the recording, inventory, monitoring and tracking of borrowed equipment to which it was the basis on the development of the RFID-Based Integrated Computer Laboratory Equipment Management System. Generally, this study used a Descriptive-Quantitati ve form of research to determine the problems in the existing manual process on Computer Laboratory. The respondents of this study were the Computer Laboratory Staff, student and other computer laboratory related personnel under College of Computer Studies. In gathering data, researcher made questionnaires, used for the survey and observation. The data gathered were analyze and interpreted using Weighted Mean. The analysis of the data showed that the developed system was highly acceptable in terms of functional suitability, performance efficiency, compatibility, usability, reliability, security, maintainability, and portability. Furthermore, the analysis showed that the performance of the developed RFID-Based system was highly acceptable. Therefore, it is reasonable to implement the RFID-Based Integrated Computer Laboratory Equipment Management System.', 'John Ervin T. Bernales, Audrey C. Bonita, Jeo D. Guanzon, Patrick Jay M. Guanzon, Kevin Rusel L. Solera', '[-0.4711636304855346, 0.8854169845581055, -2.810454