(66, NULL, 'SALES MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR ZUÑIGA’S GRAVEL AND SAND TRADING', 'Manual document filing is not an easy task and contributes to man-made errors and difficulties for an effective document management. That is why even small businesses are now implementing automation in day-to-day business operation The Sales Management System developed for Zuñiga’s Gravel and Sand Trading aims to automate the manual operations in the record section, transaction area, computation of sales and inventory area of Zuñiga\'s Gravel and Sand Trading in order to speed up the process and to improve productivity. Extreme Programming is used as software development methodology in this study. Total Enumeration is used to identify the respondents and Mixed- Method research design in gathering both quantitative and qualitative data. As for system evaluation, functional and performance testing through black-box approach is conducted. Functional testing is conducted by letting five (5) IT experts test the system following the formulated test cases. Meanwhile, JMeter is used to test the system performance. The data gathered were analyzed and interpreted using Arithmetic Mean and Standard Deviation. The results of data gathering shows that the existing problems in manual process of Zuñiga’s Gravel and Sand Trading in terms of manual business process are difficulty to manage, time-consuming, high-cost paper maintenance, inaccurate and miscalculation, and unsellable products. In terms of the results of functional testing, the system is completely functional with an average result of 1. In terms of user acceptance testing, the system obtained an all passed from the client and end users. The system also met the performance criterion for performance testing by focusing on the standard deviation and average results generated from JMeter. Due to the problems encountered by the business, the researchers concluded and recommended that the development of Sales Management System be adopted to reduce the possibility of encountering problems.', 'NEIL C. BABILA, VINA MAE B. OCCIANO, PAOLO O. LLAGAS, JEORGIE P. SALCEDO, SHEILA MAY P. ZUÑIGA', '[0.6424953937530518, 0.857061505317688, -3.7488272190093994, -0.621904730796814, 0.0589682012796402, -0.38387465476989746, 1.1718180179595947, -0.4384436011314392, -0.1318603157997131, 0.15053153038024902, 0.32911962270736694, -0.5489405989646912, 2.135326862335205, 0.02225704863667488, 0.27758944034576416, -0.1413467824459076, -0.014259738847613336, -0.4649868905544281, -0.36930662393569946, 0.3806830644607544, 1.1471956968307495, -0.4215342402458191, -0.7612385749816895, -0.963792324066162, 1.4783883094787598, -0.6539100408554077, -0.16215768456459043, -0.0735824853181839, 0.7581886649131775, -0.5404036641120911, 0.3669869601726532, -0.06208329275250435, -0.9192739129066468, -0.1458207666873932, -1.0962762832641602, -1.0913352966308594, 0.7060148119926453, -0.17663359642028809, 0.3832458257675171, -0.2208215594291687, -0.22505375742912292, -0.8438154458999634, -0.2374284565448761, -0.1991288661956787, 1.3083648681640625, -0.18281282484531405, 1.426316499710083, 0.9413452744483948, 0.604641854763031, 0.14597633481025696, 0.7799651622772217, -1.827681064605713, 0.26093703508377075, 0.8276174664497375, 0.4239051043987274, -0.1616886556148529, -0.12608090043067932, 0.5651100873947144, -0.1466989368200302, -0.8513424396514893, 1.228697419166565, 1.3244802951812744, 0.013323203660547732, 0.7587510347366333, 0.4734944701194763, -0.4997939169406891, 0.04115980118513107, 0.2603759765625, 0.2282160222530365, -0.5609326362609863, 0.902340292930603, 0.3466505706310272, -0.08451462537050247, -0.5709960460662842, -0.5083784461021423, 0.27708396315574646, -0.7655872106552124, -0.1388452649116516, -0.6769908666610718, 0.6895583271980286, -0.17553839087486267, 0.19174867868423465, 1.1857726573944092, 0.6610862016677856, 0.8833702206611633, -0.6566183567047119, 0.5531336665153503, -0.10138794779777528, -0.27153751254081726, 0.6256604194641113, 