(67, NULL, 'TRANSACTION MANAGEMENT SYSTEM WITH QR CODE IN BARANGAY SAN FRANCISCO BULA CAMARINES SUR', 'Transaction Management System was created to modernize barangay management from a conventional standpoint. Generally, the main objective of the study was to enhance current administrative processes such as requesting document, making complaints, and producing accurate reports. The objective of this study is to identify the problems encountered in the processes of the system in terms of barangay transaction management system, to design and develop a system with the features stated in the barangay transaction management system and evaluate the system using block box testing using the following methods. This study applied the software development methodology known as Extreme Programming (XP) to agile development processes. It also used purposive sampling and random sampling to select the 50 respondents.', 'JUAN D. BISENIO, JOHN FRANCIS L. IRENO, EMIL JON B. PENA, JONIE A. VERANO', '[-0.05090893059968949, 1.019669532775879, -2.9132080078125, -0.7301328182220459, 1.087354063987732, -1.2823147773742676, 0.3919196128845215, -0.4385219216346741, 0.3383522629737854, -0.4871845841407776, -0.09813273698091508, -0.44971734285354614, 2.0656988620758057, 0.4098926782608032, -0.15611441433429718, -1.8461546897888184, -0.2196288704872131, -0.30314749479293823, -1.3275821208953855, 1.1686639785766602, 0.6781783699989319, -0.007548809051513672, -0.6230534315109253, -1.3422584533691406, 1.778247952461243, 0.3437648415565491, 0.31097114086151123, -0.13694944977760315, -0.362618625164032, -0.4200372695922851, 0.8810308575630188, -0.5462651252746582, -0.33020687103271484, -0.61114901304245, -0.7500892281532288, -0.6849938035011292, 0.428422749042511, -0.4737938642501831, 0.5337842106819153, -0.2559554874897003, -0.6444326043128967, -0.3646091818809509, -0.4740840494632721, -0.504664421081543, 0.6466507315635681, 0.09848914295434952, 1.8965128660202024, 0.046468090265989304, 0.5901018977