(68, NULL, 'WEB-BASED EVENT SCHEDULING SYSTEM FOR CAMARINES SUR POLYTECHNIC COLLEGES', 'The modernization of setting up event schedules, distributing and recording attendance, and disseminating announcements are a must nowadays. Having a more organized, accurate, and faster dissemination of upcoming events, unexpected announcements, and the distribution of attendance is such a relief to all employees of a particular institution. With these, this study was conducted to develop a web- based event scheduling system that can systematically organize the events, generate the attendance record, and manage the announcements of academic administrators and personnel of Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges. The study used a mixed-methods research design that combines parts of quantitative and qualitative research to contextualize the data. The researchers used a purposive sampling technique to identify the specific respondents. The gathered data was analyzed and interpreted through the use of test cases with an acceptable range of functionality. The agile-iterative method was utilized throughout the study. The researchers perform the non-observation participant for the developed system through functional testing. The overall function of the system during the first iteration was moderately functional. In the second iteration after the modification of the system, it resulted in a highly functional system that already meets the requirements and modules that were expected to be developed. Therefore, it is recommended to implement and deploy the web-based event scheduling system for Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges.', 'MOHAMAD SALEM BELMONTE, VIRNA M. BUENA, AIREZ D. BUSTAMANTE, PETER ROEN A. LLESOL, CHRISTIAN E. QUELONIO', '[-0.18894211947917935, 1.1194334030151367, -3.655584335327149, -0.7383992075920105, 0.1102893128991127, -0.4822584092617035, 0.5234204530715942, -0.020418021827936172, 0.6015835404396057, -0.432050883769989, 0.21160441637039185, -0.41602975130081177, 2.31527423