(69, NULL, 'WEB-BASED RECORD MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR PRIVATE LENDING TRANSACTIONS', 'Private money lenders usually make use of manual methods in recording and managing their lending transactions. It is not because they wanted to but because there are just not enough automated alternatives that may help them with their methods. In connection to this, this study generally aimed to develop a record management system for private money lending that would help in various processes present in private money lending. Beforehand, the researchers aimed to determine the problems the private money lenders encounter in their regular routine. It helped with the determination of the functional requirements that the system must inherit. After that, the researchers aimed to develop the supposed record management system. The researchers expected the system to be a generic system which a lot of different private money lenders may use. Further, the researchers aimed to manually test the system for security which focused on securing the system against SQL injections, XSS attacks, and password cracking. The study covers only the record management involved within a private money lending business. However, it does not include the online distribution of money. Further, the study includes the automated versions for documentation of private money lending transactions, mathematical computations, and regular monitoring, which the researchers determined the private money lenders have had problems with. Although the researchers determined that the private money lenders didn’t have problems with archiving, tracking transactions, and validating agreements, the researchers still made the system encompassing these modules since these are generally important in private money lending. This research utilized the mixed-method approach. The respondents of this study are the private money lenders in Rinconada, Camarines Sur. The researchers made use of an interview instrument in the data collection which was analyzed thematically. After the collection of data, the researchers developed the system. The system made use of checklist instrument in testing the system’s security. The data collected in the security analysis was analyzed using a frequency percentage and weighted mean. On the side of system development, the researcher systematically followed the phases of Scrum methodology to achieve a quality system.', 'Hernanie V. Morales, Mhark Teddy Ll. Oliva, Jericho C. Peñones, Kervin Karl M. Trinidad', '[0.4859530031681061, 0.8914623260498047, -3.456761360168457, -0.7736506462097168, 0.4049416184425354, -1.5086472034454346, 0.17613127827644348, 0.12453553080558775, 0.46314528584480286, 0.9132516384124756, -0.44714492559432983, 0.13160401582717896, 0.5235163569450378, -0.3315541744232178, 0.0017910059541463852, -0.9127302169799804, -0.16565796732902527, -0.5296326875686646, -1.0511183738708496, 0.7160860896110535, -0.4853362441062927, -0.363201916217804, -0.8259904384613037, 0.749457836151123, 1.5427274703979492, -0.5921310186386108, -0.3506637513637543, -0.8645820617675781, 0.7653707265853882, 0.11342194676399232, 0.22924451529979703, -0.291851282119751, -0.27524375915527344, -0.6161841750144958, -1.2975578308105469, -1.813868522644043, 0.4390032887458801, 0.06402070075273514, 0.4033028483390808, -0.17531421780586243, -0.29871511459350586, 0.33216384053230286, -0.8359857201576233, -0.6391682624816895, 1.241560697555542, 0.40552306175231934, 1.053918957710266, 0.24370181560516355, 1.5902457237243652, 0.6669020056724548, 1.2272968292236328, -0.9682505130767822, 0.6257364153862, 0.7482233047485352, 0.5507514476776123, -0.35136687755584717, -0.7411757111549377, 0.7016465663909912, 0.528515636920929, -1.2101539373397827, 2.325873613357544, 1.0538222789764404, -0.3061595559120178, 1.3357594013214111, 0.4628690779209137, -0.5831909775733948, 0.4503525495529175, 0.5892972946166992, 0.7370774149894714, -0.10599398612976074, 0.7804059386253357, 0.9765482544898988, 0.433190226554870