(70, NULL, 'WEB-BASED STUDENT INFORMATIN SYSTEM FOR PEREPTUAL HELP NATIONAL HIGH SCHOOL, IRIGA CITY', 'Improving technology does not imply adopting the latest trend; rather, it requires an understanding of how new technology works and how it might benefit people. This study was conducted to develop a system that speeds up the work of staff at Perpetual Help National High School with documents, files, and records, as well as the management of data storage. The researchers used mixed-methods research, which includes both qualitative and quantitative data, and extreme programming methodology to guide and ensure the success of the project. The respondents were the teachers, administrators, and senior high school students of Perpetual Help National High School. In the gathering of data, interviews with open-ended questions were used. Furthermore, the developed system was evaluated through black box checklists and questionnaires. The data gathered was analyzed and interpreted using a percentage, obtaining an overall rating of 95% functionality for requirement-based testing and an overall rating of 92% functionality for used- case testing. The developed web-based student information system, therefore, gained a highly functional rating based on black box testing in terms of use case testing and requirement- based testing. Moreover, the overall average of 3.72 revealed that the respondents were very satisfied with the proposed system based on ISO-25010 using a weighted mean. As a result, the Web-Based Student Information System for Perpetual Help National High School was recommended for implementation.', 'ARLENE E. ALBANIA, NICOLE A. BUENA, LYKA M. PORTUGAL, AUDREY LALAINE P. LOQUIAS, JONAS B. RIVERA', '[-0.4918856620788574, 0.7225122451782227, -2.621328830718994, -0.43217793107032776, 0.8072354793548584, 0.231884241104126, 0.487210750579834, 0.5916796922683716, 0.06600051373243332, 0.1845557391643524, 0.5477983951568604, 0.28387734293937683, 1.5749030113220217, 0.6878882646