(71, NULL, 'WEB-BASED RICE FARMERS MANAGEMENT SYSTEM OF BARANGAY SAN ISIDRO BUHI CAMARINES SUR', 'In today’s environment, everyone is trying to engage and contribute innovative ideas in terms of technology to assess different problems encountered by the people and trying to take part in the continuous growing field of technology. With these, this study was conducted to develop a system that will monitor activities in farming and manage vital documents of farmers of barangay San Isidro Buhi, Camarines Sur. Generally, this study determined the performance the developed information management system that support the Rice farmers of Barangay San Isidro, Buhi in the monitoring and management of important records. The study used the Iterative Model and was successfully done guided by the different phases on this model of system development. The respondents of this study were the farmers and official of Barangay San Isidro, Buhi, Camarines Sur. In gathering the data, interview with open and closed ended questions and researcher made checklist and questionnaires were used. The data gathered were analyzed and interpreted using Weighted Mean and percentage. With an overall rating of highly functional in terms of Functionality the developed Web Based Rice Farmers Management System therefore meets the functional requirements based on Black Box testing in terms of Use Case Testing and Requirement- Based Testing. The overall interpretation revealed that the developed system is acceptable to the respondents. As a result, implementing the Web-Based Rice Farmers Management System of Barangay San Isidro, Buhi, Camarines Sur is acceptable.', 'MA. ERIKA N. BATAC, IAN FITZSKIRT R. DEMADARA, NIÑO R. JUAN, HAROLD KYLE H. NAGALES, ROSABELLE S. SAN MIGUEL', '[0.11992526799440384, 0.6029921770095825, -3.759549140930176, 0.2810280919075012, 0.5497937202453613, -0.06421326100826263, -0.27125927805900574, -1.1831014156341553, -0.2740074694156647, -0.4030084609985352, 0.7794038653373718, -0.5739