(72, NULL, 'BATO FARMLAND GEOLOCATION AND MAPPING SYSTEM', 'The \"Bato Farmland Geolocation and Mapping System\" is a functional and user-friendly system when it comes to management and land mapping. This addresses the issues associated with manual recording and tracking of registered and insured farmers specifically in the Municipality of Bato. The system, which was specifically built for the Municipal Agriculture Office of Bato, aims to enhance efficiency, and reduce errors in farmers\' registration and tracking of farmland. It is primarily aimed at the office admin and staff that provides real-time monitoring and tracking of every farmland of registered farmers. The system provides accurate data on the location of the land area that serves as a guide to staff during the field visit for data collection. To ensure the level of functionality of the system, the system undergoes several test methods using black-box testing, where the use case and requirement-based testing were applied. The geolocation and mapping solution, developed in response to recognized concerns with manual tracking, of the registered farm and eliminates the need for manual data entry, offering a more efficient digital interface for users. The results of use case testing show a high degree of functionality, with an average mean of 0.98 (Highly Functional). Requirements-based testing confirms its efficacy, with a mean score of 0.98 (Highly Functional). The system\'s performance and alignment with objectives are supported by Local Government of Bato, input from administrators, and staff. “Bato Farmland Geolocation and Mapping System \" is set to transform municipal agricultural office administration by offering efficiency, accuracy and user-friendly system.', 'Junel R. Joven, Julius M. Zaballa, Fernando P. Pasadilla', '[0.023680690675973892, 0.3588101863861084, -3.7141523361206055, 0.0707940086722374, 0.6050807237625122, 0.4644705653190613, 0.5223944187164307, 0.256372332572937, -0.1574470698833465