(73, NULL, 'WEB-BASED REGISTRAR OFFICE TRANSACTION APPOINTMENT SYSTEM FOR CAMARINES SUR POLYTECHNIC COLLEGES: THE IMPLEMENTATION OF POST-DESIGN STAGES', 'The post-design phases of the Web-Based Registrar\'s Office Transaction Appointment System for Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges have been carried out, encompassing the project\'s development and evaluation stages. The system, developed by researchers utilizing Extreme Programming (XP), has been designed with the objective of improving operational efficiency at the registrar\'s office. This is achieved by minimizing client wait times and enhancing customer satisfaction through the implementation of an online appointment scheduling feature. The system facilitates the transmission of automatic communications to both students and workers, encompassing various types of messages such as confirmations, reminders, and updates. The system produces reports regarding patterns and durations of appointment scheduling. The development process encompassed the identification of difficulties and demands in the planning phase, which was subsequently followed by a design phase wherein features were meticulously conceived and subjected to comprehensive testing. The researchers employed a questionnaire and interview guide as data collection instruments to ascertain the requirements and obstacles faced by clients. The proposed system is anticipated to yield advantages for the Registrar\'s Office personnel, administrators, and clients by offering an effective means of documenting information and expediting transactions. The study\'s efficacy is evident by the favorable outcomes of the survey, wherein participants assessed the system\'s operational capabilities and efficacy.', 'Ivan Jefferson O. Calleja, Zarina Kate D. Lagatic, Kaye Angela L. Sabenorio', '[-0.9604695439338684, 1.4883623123168943, -3.3151931762695312, -0.8206690549850464, 0.2524271011352539, -1.0302677154541016, 0.990453600883484, 1.6766413450241089, 0.4657592177391052, 