(75, NULL, 'RESEARCH PROJECT INFORMATION MANAGEMENT AND TRACKING SYSTEM', 'Through Research Project Information Management, the researchers come up with the idea to lessen the work in the AI Research Center for Community Development, or AIRCoDe, by managing and tracking the research project and its progress. Hence, this study aimed to develop a web-based system entitled “Research Project Information Management and Tracking System”, (RPIMTS) that help faculties and researchers in managing each research projects. The RPIMTS is paperless-based management system in which the researchers who are willing to propose new research can find it easier to apply their research. Applying for exploratory research, this study considered the data provided by the director, staff, researchers, and reviewers in the AIRCoDe. The researchers used stratified sampling techniques to gather data. The Blackbox testing for AIRCoDe’s system results reveal low vulnerability risk, excellent performance, and full functionality, with no detected errors. of the system. The researcher used the Extreme Programming (XP) phases for the development of the system, and by doing so, they created a great RPIMTS. By exploring the functionalities of the AIRCoDe, the researchers created a process flow that serves as a guide for every user that will use the system. After the development of the system, it undergoes testing, such as Use Case Testing, Performance Testing, and Security Testing, to show its level of functionality for use case testing, its level of vulnerability for security testing, and its level of response for performance testing. By those tests, it gives the results of passing those tests. The findings of this study may serve as a fundamental basis for the researchers to use the system in managing and tracking the research project and its progress.', 'China T. Bea, Louie B. Molina, Jessemri A. Tabayag', '[0.1286674290895462, 0.6997094750404358, -3.342677593231201, -0.3935354053974152, 0.6960035562