(76, NULL, 'Development of Digital Marketplace', 'Traditional grocery stores face numerous challenges in today\'s dynamic retail environment, including limited convenience and the need to adapt to changing customer preferences. This study aims to address these challenges by developing a Digital Marketplace. A third-party web application that seamlessly integrates diverse grocery outlets into a unified platform with multiple grocery options under one checkout outlet, this provides crucial support to traditional stores, enhancing visibility, attracting new customers, and streamlining operations. The research employs a mixed-method approach, gathering data from merchants, riders, IT experts, and customers through interviews and surveys. Extreme Programming is used as software development methodology in this study, utilizing PHP and MySQL for software development and Windows 10 or 11 for the operating system. The researchers used front-end technologies like HTML, Bootstrap 5, and JavaScript. Functional testing reveals challenges in the traditional store processes, emphasizing the need for a digital solution. The Digital Marketplace achieves a high level of functionality in user acceptance testing, reaching a perfect score of 1.0 in subsequent tests. In further tests, system receives an impeccable score of 1.0, indicating a high degree of functionality I security testing. Findings highlight challenges in sales calculations, inventory tracking, logistics, document storage, report generation, and customer communication. Recommendations include adapting the Digital Marketplace features for optimal performance. landscape.', 'JAKE B. AGNAS, JOEBE V. CASTAÑEDA, ELSIE B. DANCALAN', '[-1.17899751663208, 1.248808741569519, -3.3295345306396484, -0.6299901008605957, 0.7827754020690918, -0.5451290011405945, 0.708335280418396, 0.24874648451805115, 0.4061925709247589, 0.022496048361063004, 0.6818444132804871, -0.9210854768753052, 1.559375286102295, 0.14009997248649597, -0.052561692893