(79, NULL, 'CSPC Student Event Calendar System Version 3.0', 'In today\'s society, technology plays a crucial role in communication, information storage, and learning, facilitating access to essential information and aiding in educational endeavors. This capstone project aimed to develop and implement a CSPC Student Event Calendar Version 3.0 for the students of the Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges. The objectives were to identify the functionality limitations of the Android-based CSPC Calendar System Version 2.0, develop an improved version, and evaluate Version 3.0 using black box techniques like use case testing and requirement-based testing. The study employed a mixed- method research design, with 387 students, 33 CSPC Organization Officers, and 6 SASO staff as target respondents. Findings revealed functional limitations of CSPC Calendar v2.0, notably its lack of integration with other devices and unreliable distribution of announcements, hindering seamless interaction in different technological environments and communication efficiency at events. Version 3.0 addressed these issues by utilizing Extreme Programming and technologies like Dart, Flutter, and Firebase, enhancing account review, database security, feedback features, and announcements capability. Black Box Testing demonstrated high system capability, with scores of 0.93 in Use Case Testing and 0.99 in Requirement-based Testing, indicating improved user experience, security, and participation. These findings underscore the importance of addressing system vulnerabilities and implementing upgrades to meet the diverse needs of the CSPC community effectively. In conclusion, the upgrade to v3.0 successfully addressed performance limitations seen in v2.0, notably enhancing account verification, database security, and announcement features.', 'Cylene A. Busadre, Charlyn Joyce T. Sedutan, Ronnie G. Yaguel jr.', '[-0.7926068902015686, 0.7580887079238892, -3.29012131690979, -0.4857469201087952, 0.64245116710662