(83, NULL, 'WEB-BASED STUDENT-FACULTY PORTAL FOR MASOLI HIGH SCHOOL', 'Nowadays, knowing that technologies have shaped educational advancement the way humans act today, the developer of a web-based student-faculty portal for Masoli High School is presented. It addresses the problems and limitations that now exist with manual enrollment, class scheduling, grading, and document requests. It aims to recognize the current obstacles and develop and execute an all-encompassing web-based resolution. To assess the system\'s functionality, the study used black box testing, which includes user acceptance testing, stress testing, and security testing. After conducting a comprehensive examination, the researcher found out the problems and difficulties in manual procedures, which led to the development of an online student-faculty portal. That focuses on grading systems, document requests, class scheduling, and enrollment. The information obtained through questionnaires and interviews was used by the researchers during development to build an online platform that provides a better substitute for the existing manual and paper-based procedures. To make sure it worked, the system was tested through a black box testing process. Arithmetic mean of 0.94, the User Acceptance Testing findings demonstrated a high degree of functionality and broad satisfaction among administrators, teachers, students, and IT experts.', 'Joshua A. Layderos, Demet B. Espiritu, Christina F. Gonowon', '[-0.8079032301902771, 0.946499526500702, -3.350736379623413, -0.6516788601875305, 1.126955270767212, 0.5166000723838806, 1.326704740524292, 0.8086658120155334, 0.3030228018760681, 0.4715830087661743, 0.31887325644493103, 0.034688662737607956, 2.447917222976685, 0.8521077036857605, -0.020112354308366776, -0.5892484784126282, 0.4506718814373016, -0.7414150238037109, -1.3380035161972046, -0.1804116517305374, 0.4406166672706604, -0.3962242901325226, -0.9167200922966005, -1.0707356929779053, 1.5999504327774048, 0.37