(86, NULL, 'A Novel Approach of Integrating Face Unlock Technologies for a Web-Integrated Smart Door Lock Management System in CSPC-CCS Open Laboratory', 'This paper presented a facial recognition-based smart door lock management system for the CSPC-CCS Open Laboratory, which integrated IoT (Internet-of-Things) technologies and facial recognition to strengthen access control and management. The system took advan- tage of RFID for attendance records and facial recognition for door openings, featuring lab scheduling-based door openings, monitoring of attendance, inventory management includ- ing borrowing support, access records, and unscheduled door opening operations. Extreme Programming methodology and a mixed-method research strategy were used, along with the technique of Purposive Sampling, where participants were chosen and the sample size calculated through Slovin’s formula and Total Enumeration. Moreover, this study revealed that functional testing achieved 0.77 score. Non-functionality testing included load testing that passed at 50–150 threads, stress testing that partially passed at 200–300 threads but failed above 300 threads resulted to 1.0 score for performance testing, and user acceptance testing that passed at 0.75 score. Compatibility testing passed at 0.75 score, and secu- rity testing passed at 0.96 score. Tested by IT professionals, academic staff, students, and laboratory administrators, the system was considered efficient and widely accepted. The research emphasized the ability of IoT-based systems to enhance laboratory accessibility and management.', 'JOHN PAUL O. BARDENAS, MA. TERESA R. PAPA, MARIMAR H. RIVERA', '[-0.8490239977836609, 1.1271235942840576, -3.112276554107666, -0.2860260009765625, 0.8862829208374023, -0.6009117364883423, 1.5542480945587158, 0.32396167516708374, 0.8947946429252625, -0.1498037576675415, -0.09341084957122804, 0.1388634443283081, 1.5814757347106934, 0.3763384521007538, 0.2492607533931732, 0.3563830554485321, 0.50565248