(89, NULL, 'BJMP (Bureau of Jail Management and Penology) Record Management System with Electronic Head Counting', 'In today\'s landscape, technology is pivotal, reshaping how we interact, work, and navigate our world. A streamlined Record Management System is vital for organized, accessible, and meticulous record-keeping, promoting accountability and informed decision-making. This study focuses on automating record management for Persons Deprived of Liberty (PDLs), ensuring accurate tracking. Using a Mixed-method approach, Iriga City District Jails Officers were interviewed for data collection, which underwent arithmetic mean analysis. Black box testing showed use case and requirement-based testing achieving a Completely Functional level with a 100 overall average. The application significantly addresses challenges in manual recording and counting of PDLs, justifying the BJMP Record Management System with Electronic Head Counting implementation. This system revolutionizes inmate record-keeping, ensuring accuracy and efficiency. It streamlines data entry, facilitates seamless retrieval and analysis, aiding decision-making and resource allocation. This technological advancement enhances correctional facility operations, showcasing BJMP\'s commitment to modernizing record management, fostering transparency, accountability, and optimal resource utilization.', 'Angelito M. Arsenal Jr., Mary Grace R. Dilla, Lawrence G. Ramos', '[0.44590306282043457, 0.986174702644348, -2.8523268699645996, -0.5611737966537476, 0.7463497519493103, -1.2015018463134766, 0.7933651208877563, 0.493228942155838, -0.012290693819522858, 0.3402676582336426, -0.2730463445186615, -0.11051511764526369, 0.9154984951019288, 0.010167360305786133, 0.259817510843277, -1.5887079238891602, 0.5425693988800049, -0.956234574317932, -0.6594693660736084, -0.04775936156511307, 0.856670618057251, -0.23655995726585388, -1.12769877910614, -0.2941678762435913, 0.9758611917495728, 0.7116053700447083, 0.357672780752182,