(98, NULL, 'BIOLOCK: Fingerprint and PIN Lock Access Control and Attendance Logging in IT Laboratory 2', 'The Biolock system was developed in order to cope up with the growing need for modern security solutions in educational institutions, particularly IT Laboratory 2, the current door lock system used in IT Laboratory 2 are outdated and inefficient when it comes to attendance logging and it posed significant challenges. These problems pertain to the vulnerability of manual systems to unauthorized access and inaccuracy in attendance tracking, leading to security risks. The project aims to integrate fingerprint recognition and PIN-based access control to enhance security and automate attendance logging, reducing error and improving accuracy. In conclusion, the Biolock system provides a certain step toward modernizing campus security and attendance management, demonstrating the potential for further refinements to maximize its performance and reliability.', 'Noel Andrew Mendoza, Kyla Mae O. Baldago, Sheena T. Martinez, Angel F. Obia', '[0.2485710084438324, 1.1682798862457275, -3.193906784057617, -0.137229785323143, 1.0941643714904783, -0.36596736311912537, 1.618006706237793, 0.8634846806526184, 0.5757579803466797, 0.08291440457105637, -0.32350704073905945, -0.3200390636920929, 1.1184965372085571, 0.1449407935142517, 0.7615318298339844, -0.2822940945625305, 0.5988411903381348, -0.9414318799972534, -0.11799833923578262, -1.2348984479904177, 0.8529224395751953, -0.2995440363883972, -1.082566499710083, 0.12560701370239258, 1.8152611255645752, 1.2268452644348145, 1.4719752073287964, -0.11549817025661469, -0.3416738510131836, 0.6528009176254272, 0.5290824770927429, -1.063053846359253, 0.2155047357082367, -0.7126861810684204, 0.2769523859024048, -2.0573983192443848, -0.8093384504318237, 0.08601874113082886, -0.5937120914459229, 0.9787768125534058, 0.6221252679824829, 0.6620685458183289, 0.28854018449783325, -0.8541867733001709, 0.22848136723041537, 0.711205005645752, 0.83283