(100, NULL, 'Mobile Application Based Library Book Reservation In CSPC Library', 'This study focuses on the implementation of a Mobile Application Based Library Book Reservation system, aimed at enhancing the efficiency and convenience of book reservation processes for students. The introduction of this innovative solution addresses concerns regarding borrowing schedules and returns, offering significant benefits to users. Utilizing technologies such as JavaScript, HTML, CSS, PHP Laravel, and Vue.js, coupled with IDEs like Android Studio and Visual Studio Code, the development process ensures a user-friendly design and seamless functionality. The system’s intuitive interface, designed with end-users in mind, provides navigation convenience and accessibility. Features such as real- time availability status of books, personalized recommendations, and push notifications enhance the overall user experience. Integration with APIs and database management systems ensures smooth communication with the library\'s database. Secure coding practices and encryption techniques safeguard user data. The system\'s functionality was rated highly by respondents using Black box testing, with an average of 0.94 for Use Case Testing and Requirement-Based testing with the average of 0.78. The result indicated an overall agreement of 0.86. Overall, this study emphasizes creating a user-friendly platform that optimizes the library experience for students, enhancing overall satisfaction and convenience.', 'David Karl Yuan M. Cuerdo, Cyrene M. Navarro, Andrei Joshua M. Sael', '[-1.3007439374923706, 1.5997025966644287, -2.7425990104675293, -1.2377183437347412, 0.5567152500152588, -0.2787371873855591, 0.4134695529937744, 0.7259161472320557, -0.2738589644432068, 0.1593218445777893, 0.2591554820537567, -0.5081014633178711, 1.5814597606658936, 0.7112581729888916, -0.019673068076372147, -0.4022608995437622, 0.19649186730384827, -0.9674698114395142, -0.19117695093154907, -0.08534736931324005, -0.018