),
(102, NULL, 'A COMPREHENSIVE IMPLEMENTATION OF A SMART DOOR LOCK SYS- TEM WITH ACCESS LOG AND REALTIME NOTIFICATIONS AT NAS LABO- RATORY', 'The proposed Smart Door Lock System for the NAS Laboratory at the College of Com- puter Studies (CCS) replaces the traditional key-based system with biometric fingerprint authentication, access logging, and real-time SMS notifications. Developed using the Ra-tional Unified Process (RUP) iterative model, the system addresses inefficiencies identified through surveys and interviews, including incomplete manual logbook entries, delays, and heightened security risks associated with physical key management. Key features such as automated entry tracking, faculty scheduling, and real-time notifications were integrated to enhance security and operational efficiency. System testing across two iterations validated the system’s functionality, security, and reliability. In Iteration 1, the system achieved a perfect functionality score of 1.00 for admins and staff, 0.96 for faculty, and 0.91 for IT experts, with an overall score of 0.96 classified as Highly Functional. Iteration 2 results showed further improvement, with admins, staff, and faculty scoring 1.00, and IT experts scoring 0.97, yielding an overall functionality score of 0.99. Security testing demonstrated consistent improvements, with scores increasing from 0.95 in Iteration 1 to 0.97 in Itera- tion 2, indicating low-risk severity. Stress testing confirmed the system’s robustness, with a 0.00% error rate under a maximum load of 250 users, ensuring reliable performance in real-world scenarios. The study highlights the system’s effectiveness in addressing access management challenges, emphasizing iterative testing and user feedback for continuous refinement. The findings affirm that the Smart Door Lock System is ready for deploy- ment, offering a secure and efficient solution tailored to the operational needs of the NAS Laboratory.', 'Christine Joy L. Dichoso, Mark Anthony A. Llorin, Ma.Henna Fe B. Sernande', '[-0.7455064058303833, 0.6869140267372131, -2.7205638885498047, -0.2596387565135956, 1.060577630996704, -1.13742995262146, 1.2965216636657717, 1.008370280265808, 0.5968977212905884, -0.7380099892616272, -0.7395948171615601, 0.16545909643173218, 0.7664133310317993, 0.741848349571228, -0.22959378361701965, -0.31833982467651367, 0.6506360769271851, -0.8057645559310913, -0.13639149069786072, -0.32340824604034424, 0.656173586845398, -0.5809820890426636, -1.517298698425293, -0.5383087396621704, 1.3639438152313232, 0.8566458225250244, 0.9767398834228516, 0.5111914873123169, -0.2529544532299042, 0.5120938420295715, 0.9606188535690308, -0.7882561087608337, 0.06620027869939804, -0.5452898740768433, -1.1124353408813477, -1.699470043182373, -0.06075452268123627, -0.7158561944961548, 0.32263678312301636, 0.3744668364524842, 0.3258984684944153, 0.13792768120765686, 0.042159851640462875, -0.496868371963501, 0.17624324560165405, 0.4707198143005371, 0.6693284511566162, -0.8305622339248657, 1.4431885480880735, -0.2090017795562744, -0.12058528512716292, -0.94633948802948, 0.3387402296066284, 0.2557002305984497, 1.2168452739715576, 0.5775642395019531, -0.2518465220928192, 0.35670268535614014, -0.45830023288726807, -0.6659190654754639, 1.9615662097930908, 1.4664268493652344, -0.624045729637146, 1.084313154220581, 0.685121476650238, 0.8043714761734009, 0.33768728375434875, 1.2948393821716309, 0.35311418771743774, -0.8093920946121216, -0.4975453019142151, -1.1371080875396729, -0.07847116142511368, -0.28678128123283386, 0.8515681028366089, 0.7891502380371094, -0.5256720185279846, -0.27715864777565, -0.6608322262763977, 0.6959697008132935, 0.405689537525177, -0.7476686239242554, 1.1858031749725342, 0.63881516456604, 0.6866856813430786, -0.2274007797241211, -1.0674216747283936, -0.5802555084228516, -0.11323389410972597, 0.9960086345672609, 0.8491402864456177, 0.5063295960426331, -0.5284695029258728, -0.13528408110141754, -1.3751554489135742, 1.4110313653945925, 0