(103, NULL, 'TECH-SCAN: Implementing PIN Authentication in RFID-Based Smart Door Lock System for Employee Access in IT Laboratory 1 Using ALOHA-Based Algorithm', 'We create TECH-SCAN smart door lock to overcome conventional lock issues by mixing RFID technology and PIN codes for automatic lab entry. The system records when people enter and leave while improving security measures. Research teams ran system tests and security checks using ag- ile principles combined with mixed-methods research to test the system’s basic function and overall performance. Faculty members, laboratory staff, technology professionals, and student users re- sponded to this project through questionnaires and direct conversations. Test results showed the system operated with 0.96 overall functionality and earned a perfect security score of 1 demon- strating minimal dangers and positive user feedback. Research proved the system enhanced both security measures and access controls by resolving problems with duplicate keys and unapproved entrances. We suggest building better access controls while adding new security systems along- side ways to manage users better plus interactive features for smoother usage. These improvements are proposed to make the system more flexible for future security requirements while maintaining strong reliability over time.', 'JONALYN G. ALVARO, KRISTIAN P. BAS, MARK GLANDESTINE L. MANISCAN', '[-0.7008485198020935, 1.0717631578445437, -3.375558376312256, -0.12543067336082458, 1.502942442893982, -0.18923354148864743, 1.1537270545959473, 0.6454066634178162, 0.4723781645298004, -0.23985812067985535, -0.2264268100261688, 0.0689978376030922, 0.7522197961807251, 0.17313747107982635, 0.4945642650127411, 0.0639364942908287, 0.8699308633804321, -0.998907208442688, 0.08990752696990967, -0.9591273069381714, 0.8850783109664917, -0.4780627489089966, -1.0752660036087036, -0.8495214581489563, 2.1270103454589844, -0.003437880426645279, 0.8010004758834839, 0.5694996118545532, -0.076712