(104, NULL, 'CCS Faculty Lounge Smart Door Lock with Web Based Access Log and Class Sched- ule Viewing System', 'The Smart Door Lock System integrates RFID and fingerprint authentication with a web-based access log and class schedule viewing functionality to enhance security and scheduling efficiency for educational institutions. This system addresses the limitations of traditional access control and scheduling methods, which are prone to unauthorized entry, human error, and inefficient scheduling processes. By ensuring only authorized students, instructors, and admins can access secured areas and view class schedules, the system offers improved reliability and transparency. The access log component allows real-time entry/exit tracking, enhancing monitoring capabilities. The system was developed using the Agile methodology, allowing for iterative development, continuous feedback, and adaptive planning to meet evolving user needs. Data collection involved qualitative and quantitative methods, including interviews and surveys. The system underwent black-box testing to verify functionality, load, stress, and security performance. Surveys were distributed to 290 students, 23 instructors, and 2 IT experts, and 2 admins to assess system usability and effectiveness. The survey responses were analyzed using the Arithmetic Mean to ensure comprehensive feedback. Results showed a 95% function- ality rating, indicating high reliability and performance. The system’s effectiveness was validated through purposive and convenience sampling, ensuring that the solution met all user needs. Testing approaches such as functional, load, stress, and security testing confirmed the system’s dependability and security compliance. **Additionally, the system’s user- friendly interface contributed to its high usability rating, as participants reported ease of navigation. Future improvements may include integrating mobile notifications and AI-based analytics for enhanced security insights.**', 'K