(107, NULL, 'Petcare: Rayna Animal Care Clinic Information System with SMS Notification and Appointment Scheduler', 'Nowadays, most veterinary hospitals adopt high technology, or IT, where the computer has become a way of life, and technology makes things easy and possible. Some pet care clinics still use manual operations in their daily business transactions. However, the number of animals grew as the years rolled by, and various medical cases arose. The manual method of managing animal records, prescriptions, billing, and appointment schedules was no longer practical. There was a need for a lightweight application that would keep track of patients, appointments, diet monitoring, vaccination, and illness. Rayna Animal Care Clinic is a well-known clinic in Iriga, Camarines Sur. Giving veterinary services (i.e., grooming, immunizations, consultation, deworming, etc.) not only in Iriga City but also in the entire Camarines Sur and out of the province beloved pet cats and dogs. Overall, PetCare aims to provide Rayna Animal Care Clinic with a comprehensive and efficient system to manage its daily operations. The data gathered were analyzed and interpreted using Arithmetic Mean. The analysis of the gathered data shows that the problems encountered are time- consuming and limited accessibility, appointment conflicts and overbooking, inefficient reminders, and limited data analysis. Further, the black box testing regarding user acceptance and security testing shows an overall rating of 0.98 and is highly functional. Therefore, the implementation of the Petcare Rayna Animal Care Clinic Information System with SMS Notification and Appointment Scheduler was recommended to enhance the Animal Care Clinic designed to improve the quality of care for patients, increase efficiency, and enhance customer satisfaction.', 'Jan Art T. Brazal, Princess Camille O. Febres, Karl Mikel B. Pecson', '[-0.3364793658256531, 0.3062891960144043, -3.4019598960876465, -0.8131085634231567, 0.85684990