(112, NULL, 'A SENTIMENT ANALYSIS ON CSPC STUDENTS EXPERIENCES DURING COVID-19 PANDEMIC', 'The COVID-19 pandemic forced the closure of a large number of higher education in- stitutions resulting in an unprecedented in-crease in online learning. With the continued growth online education, monitoring CSPC Students thoughts and opinions about the academic performances during the pandemic using the en-hanced model may lead to useful information that can help lessen the students\' struggles when it comes to online learning and may be useful to the teachin staffs in developing an intervention to smoothen the students\' learnin process. Thus, this study endeavors to shed lights on CSPC Students sentiments about their academi using Sentiment Analysis. This study used a machine learning ap-proach to analyz the students\' sentiments based on feedback from online Google forms The results show that, o the three models tested (Naive Bayes, SVM, and Logistic Regression) the Support Vector Machine has the highest accuracy rate of 92.69%, followed by NB and LR, which have 78.84% and 91.75% respectively.', 'Romel M. Tayer, Jenyrose T. Gastilo, Princess Kaye D. Purisimas, Sarah Jane D. Agarin', '[0.22166556119918823, 0.291370689868927, -3.452425003051758, -0.5647175908088684, 0.9196902513504028, 0.796644926071167, 1.072458028793335, 0.4499374032020569, 0.8274809122085571, 0.9668604135513306, 0.42725908756256104, 0.3173799216747284, 1.8991916179656985, 0.5717310905456543, -0.18478387594223025, -0.538224995136261, -0.41474705934524536, 0.26198744773864746, -1.6539859771728516, 0.05514591187238693, -1.080179214477539, -0.8539990186691284, -0.46147969365119934, -0.45717328786849976, 1.4859058856964111, 0.9066805839538574, -1.5219080448150637, -0.30249086022377014, -0.5275322794914246, 0.310544490814209, -0.008554097265005112, -0.6574972867965698, -0.6410810351371765, -0.6747729778289795, -0.4919895529747009, -0.4092244505882263, -0.20786318182945251, -0.2991381883621216, 0.14803263545036