(113, NULL, 'Automated Temperature and Humidity Control for Hydroponic Garden using Fuzzy Logic', 'Hydroponics is a modern farming method where plants are grown in a water-based nutrient solution. In warm areas like the Philippines, growers use digital misting and fans to maintain ideal temperature and humidity. In this study, a fuzzy logic control system was designed, integrated, and tested to maintain the ideal temperature, 18-34 degrees Celsius, and humidity, 50-70 percent, to prevent physiological disorders such as bolting, tip burns, and wilting. During its development, the fuzzy library provided easy use in developing the control system and effectively automated tasks; it also main- tained the ideal temperature. However, using a HAF fan prevented ideal humidity, resulting in some tip burns to the lettuce. The test resulted in a score of 1 which means very effective on the Likert Scale of effectiveness, which indicates that almost 20 percent of the physiological disorder occur out of 30 heads. Therefore, the tem- perature and humidity control system with fuzzy logic effectively automates tasks and actions based on the sensor’s reading. The ideal temperature is maintained and effectively prevents physiological disorders.', 'Kayla Marie C. Abonita, Sheeva Mae Corporal, Joey C. Orante, Hazel V. Reyes, Jay I. Tadeo', '[0.9975969195365906, 0.9597612619400024, -4.118187427520752, -0.24964165687561035, 0.1242084577679634, 0.1388062983751297, 0.531610906124115, 0.1643943041563034, -0.4748847782611847, 0.20580509305000305, 0.6346760988235474, 0.07148200273513794, 1.9071446657180784, 1.308129072189331, -0.08548816293478012, 1.055660367012024, -0.480488657951355, -0.2991246283054352, 0.7184954881668091, -0.07565595954656601, -0.08630762994289398, -0.1886340230703354, -0.6796409487724304, -0.8235965967178345, 0.6611930131912231, 0.4518335461616516, -0.4571059346199035, 0.8578198552131653, 0.4206820726394654, 0.45879268646240234, 0.13678181171417236, -0.1931593120098114, -0