(114, NULL, 'College of Computer Studies Career Recommendation using Decision Tree Aglorithm', 'Anything can evoke a sense of empowerment in the contemporary world. This is evident in many facets of life, including romantic relationships, ordinary purchases, and career decisions. This generation appears to be constantly moving and inclined to making important decisions. This study used machine learning to recom- mend an ICT-related career for CCS third and fourth-year students to help them choose the right career in the future, and to lessen the job-skill mismatch in the Philippines. It gathered data from the students to serve as training data in recommending a career. The researchers collected a total of 70.75% of the total population of third and fourth-year students and graduates of the college. Deci- sion Tree Algorithm was used to create a model to train and test the data in recommending an ICT-related career. After the model was created, the researchers used precision, recall, F1-Score, and ac- curacy to asses the data model’s effectiveness. The model achieved a 0.67 accuracy, 0.69 precision, 0.67 recall, and 0.65 F1-score. The model showed that the model needs additional data to achieve a better performance in recommending a career. After evaluating the model, the results showed that Decision support metrics were helpful in evaluating a recommender type of model.', 'Isaac, Johnmir, Badiola, Jhon Rey, Dinero, Ronald, Monge, Mary Dine, Salona, April', '[-0.8479659557342529, 0.3041863739490509, -2.9210243225097656, -0.35055387020111084, 0.6729888916015625, 0.6780999898910522, 0.5716374516487122, -0.2435004562139511, -0.3444172739982605, 1.376392483711243, -0.6376625895500183, 0.2433977723121643, 2.649688482284546, 0.745893120765686, -0.5184277892112732, 0.15758216381072998, -0.8684349656105042, -0.9496707916259766, -0.12036097049713136, 0.48227810859680176, 0.06448596715927124, -1.1103215217590332, -0.7479777336120605, 0.43731579184532166, 0.24613195657730105, 0