(115, NULL, 'Data Analysis of Nabua COVID-19 Cases using Machine Learning SigPNG: An Implementation of Suzuki’s Algorithm for Vectorizing Webcam Scanned Signatures', 'The practice of storing, organizing, and analyzing data for commer- In this study, the main goal was to utilize Suzuki’s algorithm for the development of the software, coined SigPNG, that eases the process of creating e-signature, specifically for desktop users. Suzuki’s algo- rithm was implemented to scan and find the contours of signatures. The signatures’ contours then were used to create a vectorized im- age of the signature, and in turn, generate a PNG file of that image. Through this study, users are provided with e-signature desktop software using the system in this study, which allows them to sign papers digitally on a desktop computer utilizing the software. This software greatly assists users in signing documents quickly and easily, especially for those who sign numerous documents. This study explored and proved that Suzuki’s algorithm was suitable for signature image processing. This study developed a desktop soft- ware application, the SigPNG, that can scan written signatures and then vectorize and lastly generate a clean and accurate e-signature of the scanned signatures. Additionally, SigPNG was evaluated in this study. The system was determined to be functional and efficient to an acceptable level based on the respondents’ assessments.', 'Jane Irish B. Elevado, Reneveb S. Gabrillo, Darryl Joshua S. Juanillas, Jonalyn L. Orbino, Juluis Cezar L. Landong, Florencio S. Bagayawa, Benson P. Bandoy, Cedric Lawrence S. Pandes, Mark Jumar B. Perez, Christian Gilbert M. Salas', '[0.46248894929885864, 0.4938528835773468, -3.4949018955230713, -0.4103233218193054, -0.3088186979293823, -0.9536909461021424, 0.7194091081619263, 0.6656163334846497, -0.43549397587776184, 0.6040082573890686, -0.24032869935035703, -0.46538764238357544, 2.1134591102600098, 0.4267869293689728, -0.18202394247055056, -0.2589664