(116, NULL, 'Sweet Potato Disease Detection Using Convolutional Neural Network', 'Sweet potatoes are one of the most essential food crops in the Philippines. However, sweet potato farmers experience significant economic losses annually due to the numerous diseases that can harm sweet potato plant. In connection with this, this study aimed to gather and collect datasets of healthy and diseased sweet potato leaves, particularly Brown leaf spot, Cercospora leaf spot, and Sweet Potato Feathery Mottle Virus; build and train a Convolutional Neu-ral Network (VGG16) model for detecting the specified sweet potato leaf diseases; and determine the level of performance of the devel-oped model. The sweet potato leaf images were collected by the researchers through actual capturing using mobile phones. Some images were found online and downloaded through the internet. The constructive research design was implemented to complete the study, starting with the collection of image dataset, followed by the construction of a model, and development of a prototype to test the model. Using the VGG16 architecture, the classification reports revealed that the developed models had an overall performance of 86% and 66% accuracy in models with and without data augmenta-tion, respectively. Thus, it can be concluded that the trained CNN model solved the problem in the classification of images in this study.', 'Suzette B. Hermoso, Amy Z. Balares, Rosally C. Borbe, Christine B. Ballecer, Froilan B. Navida', '[1.1592127084732056, -0.0462101511657238, -3.356992244720459, -0.671629011631012, 0.35539984703063965, -0.44990718364715576, -0.24967604875564575, 0.23598553240299225, -0.17033886909484863, 0.031168203800916672, 0.13527515530586243, 0.6312485933303833, 1.7029156684875488, 0.25599533319473267, -1.1256895065307615, -0.03567760810256004, -1.7358897924423218, -0.28724902868270874, -0.6483394503593445, -0.05455483123660088, 0.4774443507194519, 0.4147898852825165, -0.41164976358413696, -0.02854194492