(118, NULL, 'BAYAD: Coins and Bills Identifier for Visually Impaired Individual using Convolutional Neural Network CONSUMER BUYING BEHAVIOUR OF MOTORCYCLE PARTS AND ACCESSORIES USING DATA MINING', 'In addressing the challenges confronted by visually impaired individuals at levels 1 and 2 of visual disability while indepen-dently managing finances, researchers demonstrated adept-ness. Conventional methods, notably bill folding, proved unreliable, prompting the development of a sophisticated prototype integrating a Convolutional Neural Network. This innovative solution aims to empower visually impaired indi-viduals in autonomously identifying coin and bill values. The primary goal focused on creating and evaluating a cutting-edge Coins and Bill Identifier for the Visually Impaired, uti-lizing a Convolutional Neural Network applied to a compre-hensive currency image dataset. Despite facing challenges such as limited equipment during the training phase, the pro-totype showcased a commendable 73% overall accuracy in effectively classifying various denominations. This promis-ing accuracy not only underscores its potential for real-world scenarios but also accentuates the critical importance of re-source availability, emphasizing its role in optimizing results for the enhanced financial autonomy of visually impaired individuals. With the increasing demand for motorcycles in the Philippines, resulted in a significant growth in the motorcycle parts and accessories industry. It is es- sential to have an understanding of consumer be- havior in this industry to effectively cater to their target market’s needs and preferences. Accord- ing to Gull, data mining techniques are considered more effective in analyzing customer behaviors. Therefore, this study develops a data mining model to analyze consumer buying behavior, evaluate its performance, and provide insights into motorcycle parts and accessories purchase. Data mining tech- niques such as K-means clustering, Association Rule mining, and Random Forest Regression have been selected to analyze consumer buying behav- ior. To ensure the accuracy of the proposed model, the Silhouette Score, Support and Confidence, as well as metrics like MAE, MSE, and R2 are used. K-means clustering and association rule methods were found to be the most suitable, achieving a sil- houette score of 1 and demonstrating 60% support and confidence. In contrast, the regression model was not as fitting for predictions with the avail- able dataset. The study emphasizes the importance of expanding the dataset for improved prediction precision and reliability. Notably, consumers in Nabua prefer maintenance-related items.', 'Princess Charine Rose Q. Portugal, Dave S. Lorzano, John Clifford C. Satorre, John Mark R. Seletaria', '[0.09836718440055849, 0.7864179611206055, -3.281886100769043, -0.4875417351722718, 0.9853925704956056, -0.05650936812162399, 0.48621636629104614, 0.4323816895484924, 0.5558565258979797, 0.5383589267730713, -0.1213991791009903, 0.2580167055130005, 1.9970824718475344, 0.220473513007164, 0.803813099861145, -0.07352602481842041, -1.504324436187744, -0.40377163887023926, -0.23931413888931272, 0.7530131340026855, -1.2348259687423706, 0.6395679116249084, -0.6610729694366455, -0.09518314898014069, 1.6956120729446411, -0.33864104747772217, -0.13850407302379608, -0.2918902039527893, 0.42241132259368896, 0.8307373523712158, 0.6252660751342773, -1.1851332187652588, -0.09305891394615172, -0.4070084989070892, -1.3252102136611938, -0.4681609570980072, 2.1030547618865967, 0.3270338177680969, 1.0290091037750244, 1.6745762825012207, -0.3145096004009247, -0.42812108993530273, -0.1493319272994995, -0.6092629432678223, 1.03587007522583, 0.9642401337623596, 1.8448408842086792, 0.08619208633899689, 1.552309513092041, 0.15329548716545105, 1.6367173194885254, -0.04577239602804184, 0.5201879143714905, 1.1962416172027588, 1.297731876373291, -0.1962020993232727, -0.32006925344467163, 0.43886682391166687, -0.129740208387374