(120, NULL, 'Optimizing CSPC Event Scheduling using a Genetic Algorithm', 'College events pose a scheduling challenge due to their diverse sizes. styles, and contexts. This often leads to conflicts and inefficiencies, disrupting students and staff. This research investigates the feasi bility of using a Genetic Algorithm to optimize event scheduling at Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges. Data on event details like number, duration, and attendees was collected and used to train the algorithm implemented in Python. The Genetic Algorithm\'s perfor-mance was evaluated by analyzing its space and time complexity with varying population and generation sizes. Results showed that larger generations improved scheduling optimization while reduc-ing CPU usage and conflicts. The developed prototype automates scheduling, significantly reducing manual effort. Further research suggests customizing the algorithm for specific event types to cater to their unique requirements.', 'Shaira F. Bautista, Kelsey Eunice T. Besa, Jireh Arjie C. Polvoreza', '[-0.6821666359901428, 2.24348521232605, -3.297651767730713, -0.1548600047826767, 0.6851718425750732, 0.0197613388299942, 0.3778819739818573, 0.14186955988407135, -0.5225680470466614, -0.1248042732477188, 0.1749226152896881, 0.6783578991889954, 1.6334609985351562, 1.0113701820373535, -0.41666632890701294, -0.3996970057487488, 0.2773255705833435, -0.4116092920303345, -1.039105772972107, 1.3217360973358154, 0.8105795383453369, -0.9295641779899596, -0.3219897449016571, 0.4319151043891907, 0.996520459651947, 0.14260798692703247, -0.47329482436180115, 0.48956358432769775, -0.6470818519592285, 0.32493624091148376, -0.06097029522061348, 0.44975394010543823, 0.05881991982460022, -0.974284052848816, -0.6407601833343506, -0.7113748788833618, 0.17079982161521912, -0.6549592018127441, 1.0782148838043213, 0.6644390821456909, 0.2773338854312897, -0.5008917450904846, 0.7018153667449951, -1.2022764682769775, 1.0640294551849363, -0.2792808413505554, 1.347285