(123, NULL, 'Hate Speech and Offensive Language Detection in Facebook using Naive Bayes Algorithm', 'Social media platforms, notably Facebook, stand as pervasive mod- ern tools tainted by the prevalence of hate speech and offensive language—issues that stem from broader societal prejudices. This study addresses these concerns by harnessing the potential of Naive Bayes and Optical Character Recognition (OCR) in content identifi- cation. Researchers conducted a comprehensive analysis, utilizing these methodologies to train a model using a substantial dataset of 10, 010 posts encompassing both English and Tagalog content. Among these, 5, 005 datasets were in Tagalog, while an equivalent number was in English. The resultant evaluation, performed on 20% of the data, showcased encouraging metrics: precision rates at 82% and recall rates at 81%, with corresponding F1-score and accuracy also at 81%. These findings underscore the efficacy of the Naive Bayes Algorithm and OCR in discerning hate speech and offensive language in Facebook posts. However, this study recognizes the imperative for further advancements to refine the model’s accuracy and performance, suggesting the need for ongoing enhancements to tackle the nuanced challenges posed by online content moderation and classification.', 'Benitez, John Carlo A., Quiapo, Karl Angelo C., Urbana, Jessa Mae C.', '[0.48146894574165344, 0.6404246091842651, -3.163858413696289, -0.6707835793495178, 1.6964648962020874, -0.09755676984786989, -0.19364431500434875, 0.4639345407485962, -0.106586754322052, 0.5974961519241333, 0.17098090052604675, 0.7240438461303711, 1.861132860183716, 0.941519260406494, 0.08318740129470825, -0.9578717350959778, -0.5106613636016846, -0.2723763585090637, -0.645234227180481, 0.6640171408653259, -0.48527973890304565, 0.6284154057502747, -0.6009686589241028, -0.7123793363571167, 1.9823243618011477, 0.7715920209884644, -0.124119833111763, -0.17582471668720245, -1.0340946912765503, 0.24689145386219025, 0.1671