(124, NULL, 'Cacao Detection Disease using VGG16 Architecture', 'Cacao is considered as one of the most important crops grown in the Philippines that could provide a potential source of income among large and small scale farmers. The proposed study was created to aid cacao farmers in classifying the cacao disease. The researchers developed a model by training and testing the dataset using VGG16 Architecture. Also the researchers collected 500 cacao image datasets which includes cacao image dataset taken from Kaggle and used preprocessing methods like cropping and resizing the images to develop a model to classify the diseases of cacao. This study used F1 score for evaluation method of accuracy of the model. Researchers conclude that the smaller number of training dataset, the higher the accuracy of the trained model. Also, the algorithm used in the model has the accuracy of 57% and F1 score of 54% to classify the image of the cacao into three classifications to determine its disease.', 'Lean Mae Beloro, Johannes Murillo, Jerald Toledo, Edwin Parreño', '[0.4243445694446564, 1.0509865283966064, -3.8171286582946777, -0.3469676971435547, 0.4255310893058777, -0.7188116908073425, 0.7250612378120422, 0.07517123222351074, -0.5626092553138733, -0.30685168504714966, 1.0184481143951416, 0.21031801402568817, 2.552154541015625, -0.246160089969635, 0.20865489542484283, -0.38914743065834045, -1.1970869302749634, -0.825884222984314, -0.4167674779891968, 1.3244062662124634, 0.05303502455353737, 0.14411383867263794, 0.11253263801336288, 0.0965212732553482, 1.3165100812911987, 0.3964571952819824, -0.7674541473388672, 1.2620012760162354, 0.16235233843326569, 0.4014756679534912, 0.3252303898334503, -1.2864819765090942, -0.16644349694252014, -0.5305331945419312, -0.0974034070968628, -0.1655287742614746, 0.9348571300506592, -0.046426836401224136, 1.1133050918579102, 0.8523581624031067, 0.7001585960388184, -0.4493707716464996, 0.06122700497508049, -0.8539809584617615, -0.2716437578201294, 