(125, NULL, 'Camarines Sur Polytechnic College Library Cosine Similarity in Automated Thesis and Review of Related Literature Using Data Mining', 'Thesis is one of the most important concepts in college expository writing, The researchers developed a prototype which is CSPC Library Cosine Similarity in Automated Thesis and RRL using Data Mining. This study implemented the Cosine Similarity for measuring the similarity of the documents using data mining. The researcher used survey questionnaire to evaluate the prototype, it was evaluated in terms of its usefulness and efficiency. To summarize the evaluated result of the CSPC Library Cosine Similarity in Automated Thesis and RRL using Data Mining; according to the findings of the respondents evaluation both usefulness and efficiency of the prototype got a verbal interpretation of Strongly Agree with an average weighted mean of 4.29 and 4.25 respectively. This re- sult demonstrates that the respondents was strongly agree that the usefulness of the prototype has the capability to fulfill its purpose and that the prototype was easy to navigate, well integrated and consistent. Finally, in terms of efficiency, the prototype has received an Strongly Agree level of acceptability in providing response to the searched words and sentences; in providing the needed and accurate results; and respondents was strongly agree that the pro- totype makes it faster in finding related literature. The prototype performance was tested in terms of usefulness and efflciency and was able to serve its purpose and was simple to understand and', 'Elaila Mae C. Baran, Ella Mae T. Bergado, Judith A. Taduran', '[0.815285325050354, -0.4052290916442871, -2.621004581451416, -1.7374205589294434, 0.6659494638442993, -0.8552025556564331, 0.5945932865142822, -0.039871759712696075, -1.2533674240112305, 0.7274205684661865, 0.2077248692512512, -0.02794588729739189, 2.5173611640930176, -0.04249892383813858, -0.13154810667037964, -0.52381432056427, -0.147783994