(126, NULL, 'Course Recommendation for CSPC Incoming Freshmen using Collaborative Filtering Algorithm', 'Nowadays, there are many courses accessible for students, and it might be difficult for a student to acquire information about such courses and determine which course to take. This study developed a course recommendation for CSPC freshmen students, which can help students in decision making by proposing suitable courses based on their admission exam results. In general, the suggested course was generated using a method known as Collaborative Fil- tering Algorithm. The researchers used the batch 2018-2019 and 2019-2020 entrance test results from the Student Testing and Admission office of CSPC, which included 500 sample data sets in each batch for a total of 1000. The model can instantly generate course suggestions using the technique by obtaining the highest similar- ity score. Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1 Score, MSE, MAE, RMSE, MAPE and R-Squared have been used to evaluate the proposed ap- proach. The model’s overall performance is 73% of accuracy which means is dependable, demonstrating that it is possible to use the developed model in recommending courses to students to assist them in making decisions', 'Myra SB. San Felipe, Joselito S. Batan, Jonel L. Britania, Jamaica T. Rabino, Shania Mae D. Elpedes', '[-0.9229862093925476, -0.14901141822338104, -3.300662040710449, -0.2273426204919815, 1.578487992286682, 0.3942461907863617, 1.3281116485595703, 0.03846337646245957, -0.25821954011917114, 1.32513427734375, 0.4904608130455017, 0.617143452167511, 2.164573907852173, 1.5456327199935913, -1.6960303783416748, -0.608952522277832, -0.2092605382204056, -0.8857383131980896, -1.410175919532776, -0.4254472255706787, -0.44638633728027344, -0.6526482701301575, -0.4460558891296386, 0.1099676638841629, 1.60158109664917, 0.6414111852645874, -1.2635886669158936, -1.0136600732803345, -0.46555542945861816, 0.4341007173061371, 0.5851626396179199, -0.514129638671875, 0.184824779