(127, NULL, 'Crime Rate Prediction and Analysis in Iriga City Using K-Means Algorithm', 'Crime is the largest issue facing the entire world now and one of the greatest threats to humanity. The goal of this study is to develop a model that can be utilized in identifying and predicting the future oc- currence of crime. Data on crimes committed in Iriga City between January 2018 and April 2022 was gathered and used in the study. The model employedtheK-mean salgorithmtouncoveru nderlying crime trends and patterns, detect crime-prone areas, and determine which barangays have the highest crime rate. The Elbow method was implemented to identify the best k value in clustering. The result of the model indicates that crimes involving damage to property and physical injury had the highest rates of occurrence, and of the 36 barangays in Iriga City, San Francisco (Pob.) and San Roque (Pob.) had the highest rates of crime occurrence. It was also discovered that the crime rate has been declining over time. These findings will be very useful to law enforcement and local government units in taking necessary actions to reduce crime and in crafting safety and security policies. Moreover, the developed model can be a spring- board for the future development of more reliable crime prediction and analysis applications.', 'Jodan B. Parel, Kyla Glen Alcantara, Jason S. Ordinario, Nicole Alcantara', '[1.4637086391448977, 0.392846941947937, -3.390454053878784, 0.5775124430656433, 1.5304914712905884, -0.09303440153598784, 1.0642435550689695, 0.6314046382904053, -0.1899686753749847, 0.14681951701641083, -0.11720454692840576, -0.03586098551750183, 1.259459137916565, -0.17775438725948334, -0.5469580888748169, -0.9404762983322144, -0.4864586889743805, -0.03693196177482605, -0.9890142679214478, 0.17219290137290957, -0.2213701605796814, -0.3867671191692352, -0.4378984272480011, -0.37745600938797, 0.9077650904655457, 0.5987861156463623, -0.1183689832687378, -0.24728240072727203, -0.1781150847673416,