(128, NULL, 'EXPLORING BUHI CORPUS USING NATURAL LANGUAGE PROCESSING (NLP)', 'Buhi is a municipality located in the coastal province of Ca- marines Sur. It has 38 barangays and its residents speak a dialect called Buhinon, which is a blend of features from the Bikol of Polangui, Albay, and the Iriga variant of Rinconada Bicol. Buhinon is considered a lone language and is the only one used in Camarines Sur province. Because of its unique and distinct dialect, researchers have proposed a study to develop a web-based application that can translate Buhi- non words into Filipino words, complete with corresponding speech tags and named entities. This will help non-native speakers, such as students, teachers, and researchers, to understand unfamiliar words. The proposed web-based applica- tion provides two functions for natural language processing (NLP): Filipino to Buhinon and Buhinon to Filipino. The re- searchers collected 1000 Buhinon words from San Pedro, San Pascual, and San Buena in Buhi, Camarines Sur as their dataset. To evaluate the translation quality, the researchers used the BLEU score metric, which compares a candidate\'s translation with one or more reference translations. The researchers obtained an average of 74 from the Buhinon ref- erence and Tagalog reference translation. Studying another culture based on their dialect is like building a relationship with the native speakers and the people around the area. It\'s an eye-opener to non-native speakers that someone\'s dialect will never be a barrier to anyone.', 'Jeed Leo Gaveria Cortan, Khayzel L. Ricafort, Jinky Villagracia', '[0.1173584684729576, 0.599141538143158, -2.689490795135498, -1.8459311723709104, 0.968894898891449, -0.7900131940841675, -1.4114503860473633, -0.0016605742275714874, -0.5291140675544739, -0.9304512143135072, 0.04793943837285042, 0.1087036281824112, 1.1077795028686523, -0.649064302444458, -0.13618499040603638, -1.5531234741210938, -1.0070340633392334, -0.9607791900634766, -0.13987146