(130, NULL, 'IMAGE CLASSIFICATION OF BANANA LEAF DISEASES IN THE PHILIPPINES USING CONVOLUTIONAL NEURAL NETWORK (CNN) ALGORITHM', 'Banana is considered one of the most important crops grown in the Philippines and could provide a potential source of in- come for large and small-scale farmers. The proposed study was created to aid banana farmers in classifying one of the main banana leaf diseases in the Philippines, called Black Sigatoka, Banana Bunchy Top Virus (BBTV), and Panama disease. The researchers developed a model by training and testing the dataset using the VGG16 architecture. Also, the researchers collected 750 banana leaf image datasets for each disease, which included banana leaf images taken from dif- ferent online websites, and used preprocessing methods like cropping and resizing the images to develop a model to classify the diseases of banana leaves. This study used the F1 score as an evaluation method for the accuracy of the model, Researchers found that the smaller number of train- ing datasets could not improve the accuracy of the trained model because of a lack of learning from the data. Also, the algorithm used in the model has revealed a loss metric of 0.6333, an accuracy of 0.7117, and a f1 score of 0.7037. These results highlight the practical utility of the CNN approach for disease classification, suggesting promising applications in managing banana leaf diseases in the agricultural context of the Philippines.', 'Maryfrance Abinal, Kenje Delfino, Justine Desiree Buquid, John-Nhel Tanay', '[1.1014950275421145, 0.21528908610343933, -3.652238368988037, -0.6096659898757935, 0.6641584634780884, -0.04035704582929611, 0.16227978467941284, -0.36518609523773193, -0.13114646077156067, -0.23812906444072723, 0.7474645972251892, 0.5849547386169434, 2.9635374546051025, 0.5516685843467712, -0.6975111961364746, -0.8197281956672668, -1.9684995412826536, -0.6376986503601074, -0.1837606430053711, 0.12636955082416534, -0.5064659118652344, 1.098679780960083, 0.1