(131, NULL, 'IP ROUTING TO FIND OPEN SHORTEST PATH USING DIJKSTRA\'S ALGORITHM', 'Each network\'s router maintains a table of IP addresses and other subtle router information, as well as information about other systems with which it has previously been paired. It compares the target IP address to its list of systems once it receives the packet from the nearby computer or network. In the unlikely event that a coordinate is discovered, the packet is sent to the router or list of routers that will compare it before routing it to the destination node. The research aimed to select the most optimal route through the network from the source subnet or host to the destination sub- net or host is one of the primary goals of all routing protocols. The routing protocols\' metrics determine which route is the most optimal. Hence, monitoring of the company\'s networking system and the usage of a network simulation are related with the task of determining the open shortest path using Dijkstra\'s Algorithm on the routing protocol used in computer networks. In order to use the system, the end user needs to be familiar with networking basic. This study investigates and demonstrates the IP routing suit- ability of Dijkstra\'s algorithm. It performed a network animation in NetAnim. Since the accuracy of the algorithm was fulfilled by implementing to the project as shown in the findings, it could ac- cept any valid network scenario concerning any design of graph representation and could be demonstrate through simulation.', 'Twirly Joy L. Paballa, Rommel Jay A. Fedelino, Giselle I. Infante', '[-0.4212045669555664, 1.4669888019561768, -3.563892126083374, -0.48329055309295654, 0.31728440523147583, -0.926249623298645, 0.39189261198043823, 0.19569721817970276, -0.2266721874475479, -0.5623689889907837, -0.3580120801925659, 0.42105215787887573, 1.7534486055374146, 0.3847517967224121, -0.8000435829162598, -0.5152174234390259, -0.6014829874038696, -0.47253549098968506, -0.15727035701274872, -0.0