(132, NULL, 'Keystroke Injection Detection System using Naive Bayes Algorithm and Pattern Recognition', 'A USB device is normally used to connect devices to computers or store data. However, a sophisticated device emerged that mim- ics keystroke inputs into the computer system. These devices are called BadUSB\'s. These are USB Devices that are programmed to execute keystroke payloads and launch then onto the computer system. To counteract against this threat, particularly keystroke injection attacks, this paper introduces a Keystroke Injection Detec- tion System (KI.D.S). Employing sophisticated pattern recognition and the Naive Bayes algorithm, the system scrutinizes user key- stroke patterns to differentiate between authentic and manipulated input. Leveraging the user-friendly and effective nature of Naive Bayes, the system classifies data after training on a dataset of typ- ical typing behaviors. The system constructs a robust model that identifies anomalies indicative of keystroke injection attempts by analyzing temporal and spatial keystroke characteristics through advanced pattern recognition algorithms. With an efficiency rate of 98%, K.I.D.S exhibits low false-positive rates, real-time detection, and adaptability to evolving attack vectors. Experimental results demonstrate its effectiveness across various scenarios, further en- hancing cyber security protocols. The combination of Naive Bayes and pattern recognition proves to be a promising approach for developing reliable and accurate keystroke injection detection sys- tems.', 'Jan Paul M. Bondad, Diana G. Arnante, Rodolf Ryamn C. Nacario', '[0.4963243305683136, 0.911856770515442, -3.2097651958465576, -0.3985363245010376, 0.7607204914093018, -0.9712306261062622, 0.36017149686813354, 0.9051814079284668, -0.5638549327850342, -0.31677746772766113, -0.6300102472305298, 0.8175786733627319, 1.3510782718658447, -0.17201754450798035, -0.058592893183231354, -0.7523274421691895, -0.14566712081432345, 0.235482096672058