(137, NULL, 'Vehicle Plate Number Recognition Using Digital Image Processing and Optical Character Recognition', 'The rapid development and growth of smart cities and intelligent systems have brought intelligent transportation systems where vehicle number plates for analysis and monitoring have become vital. An identification tool for vehicles would help law enforcers in the contactless enforcement of traffic and road laws and violations, ensuring road safety and security. This study aims to develop a prototype that will detect and recognize vehicle plate characters using an ensemble of image processing methods, Digital Image Processing (DIP), and Optical Character Recognition (OCR). The prototype extracts the character from the plate number and trans- forms it into a text-based output. The dataset was gathered over the internet and through first-party data collection. The prototype\'s performance was evaluated and has achieved an overall accuracy score of 85% suggesting that the ensemble of algorithms is reliable in image processing and character recognition.', 'Paul Nigel Resurrecion, Alexander Eufracio, Swetzel Zuñiga, Rodel Secillano, Angel Katherine Verceluz', '[-0.47681963443756104, 0.3064047694206238, -3.583003520965576, -1.04597806930542, 1.2309578657150269, -0.08212801069021225, 0.6456533670425415, 0.8002630472183228, 0.28263574838638306, 0.11231914162635805, 0.10510849207639694, 0.2700146734714508, 1.7333128452301023, -0.21102258563041687, 0.8045738935470581, -1.2570229768753052, -0.222634419798851, -1.5399305820465088, -0.0601937435567379, 0.3002004623413086, 0.095023974776268, 0.9328633546829224, -1.1351492404937744, -0.039803288877010345, 2.3609602451324463, 0.3173134922981262, 0.437738299369812, -0.15690001845359802, -0.5299838185310364, -0.1359567940235138, 0.7645699381828308, -0.803648829460144, -0.07682648301124573, -1.1563347578048706, 0.4233818054199219, -1.2370150089263916, 1.1921794414520264, 0.4339897036552429, 1.4954352378845217, 1.48287391662