(138, NULL, 'Developing a Signature Forgery Detection Prototype using Convolutional Neural Networks', 'In this study, the main goal was to develop a signature forgery de- tection prototype targeting the significant problem of authenticity in areas, including financial and legal domains. Signature-based authentication is prevalent in various real-world applications but has a major problem with forgery and fraud, which can lead to fi- nancial loss and disputes. The rescarchers utilized a Convolutional Neural Network, specifically the ResNet50 architecture, to enhance the reliability of signature verification. The study involved train- ing the ResNet model on a dataset of signature images, followed by rigorous evaluation using metrics such as accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score. The model achieved an impressive accuracy rate of 87.95%, demonstrating its effectiveness in identifying forged signatures. The study created a prototype to function as an offline application, allowing users to perform signature verification with- out the need for an internet connection. The prototype successfully provided reliable and efficient signature verification, enabling users to enhance security and authenticity in critical transactions.', 'Jhan Lenard Troa Aguilar, Loren J. Llorin, Justine D. Labios', '[0.35200512409210205, 0.9839887619018556, -3.246473789215088, -0.634742259979248, 1.233128309249878, -1.1559871435165403, 0.35332056879997253, 1.591579556465149, -0.06563952565193176, 0.353488951921463, -1.237802267074585, 0.5545970797538757, 1.1137758493423462, -0.35661768913269043, -0.3332342505455017, -0.5030105710029602, -0.06392017006874084, -0.30348438024520874, -0.17715556919574738, 0.29607242345809937, -0.4350371658802033, -0.33389413356781006, -0.3019663691520691, 0.20406319200992584, 1.479935646057129, -0.004824652336537838, -0.1974224150180817, -0.2720223069190979, -0.24879315495491028, -0.9619908928871156, 0.7408717274665833, -1.0877552032470703, -0.27226656675338745, -