(141, NULL, 'Quail Eggs Quality Detector using Convolutional Neural Network', 'This work introduced the design of a Quail Eggs Quality Detector in the form of a CNN model employing the ResNet50-V2 model to improve the speed and precision of sorting quail eggs accord- ing to their quality parameters. As the conventional technique of sorting manually is time-consuming, expensive, and have higher chances of error, the purpose of the present study was to integrate an automation feature in the sorting process. The proposed system connected CNNs with a Raspberry Pi device to categorize quail eggs by inspecting appearance of the shell and surface imperfections. Moreover, manual coded approach utilized. The model was trained through 2,880 images in total of quail eggs with data augmentation and attained approximately 99 percent accuracy. Also, the models’ performance was evaluated by the accuracy, precision, recall and F1-score. It gave an desirable sorting accuracy of approximately 75 percent among 285 test images and in the manually coded model, it saved in TensorFlow Lite format where received only 75.79 percent where numerous inaccuracies in predictions. In this research, a reliable automated system was developed and implemented that improved the quality of the quail eggs and reduced the operational cost for producers. The identified results revealed opportunities for machine learning in agriculture while contributing the prospects towards the development of further advanced sorting methods.', 'Archie L. Inocentes, Derick Emmanuel J. Marpuri, Mariana Jane L. Ramos', '[0.162141814827919, 1.2790024280548096, -3.428500175476074, -1.1766598224639893, 0.9517166614532472, -0.12071648240089417, 0.1614730954170227, -0.21373251080513, -0.6371841430664062, -0.2164602279663086, -0.3948086500167846, -0.13745321333408356, 1.9278185367584229, 0.29797041416168213, -0.7822322845458984, -0.3058846890926361, -0.4566102623939514, -0.9941017627716064, 0.23393820226192472, -0.02925691008567