(144, NULL, 'IMPLEMENTATION OF IMAGE RECOGNITION FOR AUTOMATED CAMPUS PARKING', 'This presents the Implementation of Image Recognition for Automated Campus Parking in campus canteen, aimed at enhancing parking efficiency through advanced image recognition technology focusing on the utilization of the YOLOv9 (You Only Look Once version 9) architecture to enhance parking management through real-time vehicle detection and classification. The researchers employed a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) model to detect and classify vehicles in real-time using camera images. The study aims the effectives and feasibility incorporating image recognition of campus parking, investigating the challenges such as lighting condition, vehicle diversity and security concern. The YOLOv9 model was trained on this dataset, achieving promising results in terms of precision, recall and mean average precision. The model achieved a 93.5% of the object detected. A prototype web application was developed using Streamlit to demonstrate the realtime detection capabilities of the trained model. The prototype successfully identified parking spaces and classified their occupancy status and the performance and showcasing the potential of the model for real world applications in parking.', 'Cecil D. Dagon, Jason L. Serillano, Jade B. Sinfuego', '[-0.20395681262016296, 0.1527203619480133, -2.8545734882354736, -0.2137768715620041, 1.351215124130249, -0.5188323855400085, 1.215336799621582, 1.2199445962905884, -0.6188086271286011, 0.0742873102426529, 0.39457160234451294, -0.5085644721984863, 2.2899861335754395, 0.01159699261188507, -0.06166556850075722, -0.5279927849769592, -0.6711734533309937, -1.0106600522994995, 0.08850036561489105, -0.25503990054130554, 0.8558879494667053, 0.7023274302482605, -1.228637456893921, -0.2957187592983246, 2.0537922382354736, 0.9099860787391664, 0.33810797333717346, 0.1559668779373169, 0.8292432427406311, -0.08194971084594727, 1.4256008863449097, -0.7310695052146912, -0.292