(145, NULL, 'Enhancing Disaster Response Planning in Nabua, Camarines Sur through Map Visualization and Dijkstra’s Algorithm', 'Disaster was a serious problem that happens over a period of time and causes so much harm to people, things, economies, or in the environment that affect community or in the society that it cannot handle by its own. The main goal of this study was to develop a map and determine the shortest path in Nabua using Dijkstra\'s algorithm, which was aid both government and non-government entities in achieving faster response times. The Dijkstra Algorithm was one of the algorithm for finding the shortest paths between nodes in a weighted graph.It\'s the best option to use this algorithm in path finding, one of the algorithm that stands out as a powerful tool for efficient navigation. Three test cases were conducted, each with a starting and ending point. The distances recorded were; True Shortest Path, the actual shortest distance, used as the gold standard. Altemative Path, a longer and less efficient route, illustrating the problem\'s complexity. Proposed Path, the distance calculated by the algorithm, compared to the True Shortest Path to assess accuracy. Dijkstra\'s Algorithm was successfully integrated into the disaster response map using Python with Tkinter. The map\'s road netwoek was represented as a weighted graph, with weights assigned based on all the barangay. Nabua map layout was taken from MDRRMO of Nabua that was served to provide a clear vision for the path and list of barangays in Nabua.', 'Jushua Jay P. Delos Santos, Rose Ann M. Agravante, Princes J. Aquiler, John Hananel P. Deleon', '[-0.22369158267974856, 0.5965273380279541, -3.749130725860596, -1.0156782865524292, 0.6365829706192017, -0.058941781520843506, 0.07460112124681473, 0.6007328629493713, 0.2715458869934082, -0.25652608275413513, 0.19343310594558716, -0.04726051539182663, 2.5387253761291504, 0.05636325478553772, -0.10562308132648468, 0.019026480615139008, -0.44323295354