(148, NULL, 'CONVERSATIONAL CHATBOT FOR PERSONALIZED RECOMMENDATIO N OF BICYCLE PARTS ON SHOPEE', 'This study aims to address the overwhelming choice and lack of personalized assistance faced by customers shopping for bicycle parts on Shopee by developing a conversational chatbot for per- sonalized recommendations. The chatbot was developed using a constructive research design, combining traditional NLP and LLMs to ensure precise intent recognition and contextual understanding for complex queries. Utilizing the Shopee bicycle parts dataset, the model (Llama-3-8b-bnb-4bit ) was iteratively refined through data cleaning, training, and validation with the Unsloth framework. The chatbot was built using a fine-tuned natural language processing model, leveraging gathered data to improve its ability to understand user preferences and suggest relevant products. Evaluation results showed a BLEU score of 0.81, indicating strong alignment between generated responses and reference answers, particularly in technical specifications. The F1-score of 0.62 demonstrated a good balance between precision and recall, showing the chatbot\'s ability to identify relevant bicycle parts while reducing incorrect suggestions. Response times increased, with an average of 29.76 seconds, reflecting the additional processing time required for per- sonalized recommendations. Despite the increase in response time, the chatbot showed significant improvements in relevance (7.61) and personalization (7.6), compared to its pre-trained version. The study concluded that while the chatbot demonstrated strong potential in enhancing user experience and supporting decision-making. further optimization in accuracy, response consistency, and efficiency is essential for broader application in e-commerce.', 'Mark B. Tagum, Rodney S.R. Carlo, James D. Ballerda', '[-0.9949429035186768, 1.2945867776870728, -2.9389030933380127, -0.7528867721557617, 1.066131353378296, -0.0511387400329113, 0.2102611213922501, 0.1096794