(149, NULL, 'A CUSTOMIZED PROTOTYPE OF TRANSACTION APPOINMENT SYSTEM FOR THE REGISTRAR OFFICE', 'The Students Registration and Records Office (SRRO) utilizes manual process of transactions. In connection, this study aims to design a customized prototype appointment system for the registrar\'s office of Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges. Specifically, this study analyzes the existing transaction, determines the problems encountered by the clients, and designs a customized prototype appointment system. This research utilized the mixed- method approach. The respondents of this study were the staff of the SRRO and clients such as the students, alumni, and parents. After data gathering through an interview guide, observation checklist, and survey questionnaire, analysis was done using the percentage technique and weighted mean. On the side of Information System Planning Framework, researchers systematically follow the phases of DMAIC methodology under Lean Six Sigma. Upon analysis of collected data, result shows that the SRRO uses manual process of transaction. Thus, the frequently encountered problems during transaction are long queues and waiting times resulting in congested waiting area. To address the problems, the researchers designed a web-based appointment system prototype. Further, the evaluation of the prototype\'s acceptability revealed that it was acceptable in terms of operation with a weighted mean of 4.53 and highly acceptable in terms of the design with a mean of 4.65 for the clients. The staff was rated highly acceptable, with a weighted mean of 4.65 for the operation and 4.69 for the prototype design. In connection, the CSPC can use the prototype to strategize a good plan for an Information System and automate the transaction in the SRRO.', 'EUGENE D. CASTROVERDE, ROBERT A. ISAAC, RAFAEL A. ABANO, MARK ANTHONY L. AZURES', '[-0.8655023574829102, 1.4956258535385132, -3.2536745071411133, -0.6619060039520264, 0.005576007068157196, -1.1133077144622805, 1.192