(150, NULL, 'ANALYSIS AND REDESIGN OF UVOTE SYSTEM IN CAMARINES SUR POLYTECHNIC COLLEGES DEVELOPMENT AND EVALUATION OF INTEGRATED ENROLMENT AND BILLING INFORMATION SYSTEM', 'E-voting is a method for increasing electoral efficiency and building trust in election administration, and CSPC Innovative IT solutions to enhance organizational processes has been everywhere because of its many uncovered benefits. This is evident in the educational arena, and this study is an initiative to attempt the integration of a technology in one of the most important processes in the academic institutions. The Enrollment and Billing Information System, a computerized system, is used to eliminate specific problems in the manual process. In general, the objective of the study is to develop an enrollment and billing information system which provide a more accessible system along with functional sustainability, maintainability, compatibility, portability usability, reliability, security, and performance efficiency. To addressthe objectives of the study, the researchers used a mixed-method research design and a rational unified process iterative model. Data were obtained through interviews and survey questionnaires. Due to problems encountered with the highest frequency of loss or damage of billing records and loss of data in the enrollment and billing process of St. Jude Thaddeus Learning Center. Thus, the development of enrollment and billing information system acceptability was different from the manual process, interpretation revealed that the developed system is acceptable for the respondents to possible loss or damage of billing records, loss of data, and time consumption. As the result, the enrollment and billing information system will speed up the process and refrain from losing data and records, and can back-up data.', 'POLICARPO III E. BANTE, JOHN ROVIC M. CORBILLA, HUE D. GANALON, MARY CRIZ G. ORBON, ABIGAIL B. RIBAYA, MEL CHRISTIAN M. MASCULINO, MARK ANTHONY B. BOLO, JUVEREN A. 