(151, NULL, 'STRATEGIC PLAN FOR CSPC LEONS UTILIZATION', 'Learning Management System has been one of the solutions that is applied by the government and education sector during pandemic evolution. In relation to this, CSPC has implemented Learning Online Space (LeOnS). In the utilization of the system, problems and barriers are observed. With these, the study is conducted to analyze and evaluate the feedbacks of users in utilizing the system. This study specifically aims to develop an Evaluation Team as well as determine the level of satisfaction of users towards the system and the level of performance according to ISO 25010 quality characteristics. Additionally, to determine the problems encountered as for this enhancement proposal plan is formulated. The study follows the Information System Evaluation Framework. The study has used quantitative approach in descriptive form; respondents of the study are the students and faculty members of CSPC and the results are calculated with the use of Slovin’s Formula. Data acquisition is conducted through Google Form and Paper-based wherein maid questions are applied. Analysis and evaluation results are done using Weighted Mean and Ranking Method. The study analyzes that there is a gap between students and faculty members towards system. In terms of system level of performance according to ISO 25010 standardization, the system is efficient and accurately enough to accomplish task. Based on this evaluation, problems and barriers in utilizing the system such as repetition of logging into the system and lack of notification for new uploaded materials and resources are occasionally encountered. Therefore, formulation of an Operational Manual of the system is needed to be accomplished and executed.', 'CATHERINE S. DECIERRA, ROSE ALMA F. LUCQUIAO, SOPHIA B. MONGE, MERYJOY B. PLOTADO, ALLAN A. PODAWAN', '[-0.4237285554409027, 0.9389090538024902, -2.6426734924316406, -0.749350905418396, 0.6340168118476868, 0.29312267899513245, 0.36452