(152, NULL, 'TOWARDS A PROPOSED UPGRADED DESIGN OF THE MULTI-EVENT TABULATION SYSTEM (METAsys)', 'Multi-Event Tabulation System (METAsys) is a system developed in Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges that can be used for any competitions, such as beauty pageants and talent contests, to obtain an overall and centralized result, an organized record-keeping of the events, as well as to ease the process of result computation. The study was conducted to analyze, evaluate, and redesign the METAsys. Specifically, it aims to determine the problems and issues encountered by using the current METAsys in terms of user interface design and database of the system, the proposed design of system Database Schema and user interface. Additionally, to evaluate the proposed design of the database schema and user interface of METAsys in terms of System Usefulness, System Capability Shortcomings, and System Reliability. The study follows the Information System Evaluation Framework. The study used a mixed- method approach in descriptive form; its respondents are IT Experts and JPCS Officers using a purposive sampling method. In this study, the researchers analyzed the identified problems and issues regarding user interface and database. The study redesigned and improved the system database and optimized the user interface and added more features and functionalities. The weighted mean from the System’s Value metrics in the proposed system’s database schema with an average weighted mean of 3.78 is “Strongly Agree” from IT experts. The proposed system’s user interfaces with an average weighted mean of 3.82, which is “Strongly Agree” from JPCS officers, and 3.78, which is “Strongly Agree” from IT experts.', 'RAYMON V. BARDINAS, NORMAN A. CASTILLA JR., PETER PAUL O. MENDOZA, JENICCAH P. RULL', '[-1.205369472503662, 1.374098539352417, -2.958656311035156, -0.18536359071731567, -0.02377992868423462, -1.0400768518447876, 0.40772902965545654, 0.41478198766708374, 0.10765856504440308, -0.3907580077648