(153, NULL, 'ANALYSIS AND DESIGN FOR ONLINE APPOINTMENT MANAGEMENT IN CAMARINES SUR POLYTECHNIC COLLEGES ADMISSION OFFICE', 'An Online Appointment Management is a software application to well organize the admission process for educational institutions such as schools, colleges, and universities. The Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges Admission Office already has an existing process where applicants will submit application form and schedule entrance examination. This study was conducted to analyze and design Online Appointment Management in Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges Admission Office. In general, the objective is to design user interface of online appointment management and database. To address the objectives of the study, the researchers used a mixed method research design and the design thinking framework. Data were obtained through interviews and survey questionnaires. The study respondents were the students of Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges and administrators in Admission Office. The data was evaluated and interpreted using a weighted mean. Due to problems encountered with the time consuming, duplication of applicant’s name, lack of automation in appointment confirmations, delays and errors because of high volume of applicants and complex application process. To address this, the study designed the user interface and Database. Thus, the overall interpretation revealed that the designed user interface and database satisfied the respondents. As a result, designing of the User Interface and Database will speed up the appointment process, avoid duplication of applicant’s name and provide better experience for applicants and admission staffs.', 'RENELA ROSE A. GAROL, MARY JOY E. TUYAY, PABLO R. TALAGTAG JR', '[-1.468340516090393, 1.0742450952529907, -2.675567150115967, -0.5444217920303345, 0.2785091996192932, -0.13978950679302216, 1.5442702770233154, 0.8023470640182495, 0.3918725550174713, 0.8929177522659302, -0.008088719099760056, -0.3743856549263001, 2.8