(154, NULL, 'ANALYSIS AND DESIGN OF ENROLLMENT SYSTEM OF TABURNAL LEARNING CENTER, BATO', 'Enrollment is the process of signing up for a particular school. Enrollment systems are used to record and verify a student’s information. Retrieving important information about the students’ using the manual system can cause trouble because the important student records might be lost, can lead to inaccurate evaluation of the student, and lastly, slow processing of enrollment. Taburnal Learning Center, Bato already has an existing enrollment process which is the pen and paper method. The main focus of the research is to pinpoint the issues and obstacles within the process of their current enrollment system. This entails comprehending the challenges that students and administrative staff encounter while undergoing the enrollment process. The project\'s objective is to boost the efficiency of the enrollment system by designing a low-fidelity prototype and database of online enrollment system. Through this, the researchers seek to decrease the time required for enrollment and diminish errors in the enrollment data, ultimately leading to a more streamlined and error-free process. The primary aim of the project is to enhance the overall user experience for both students and administrative staff.', 'MARL LOUWELLE ARGARIN, SHIELA MAE PANGILINAN ALANIS, RICA THERESA VILLAMER ADANTE', '[-0.6708333492279053, 0.987763285636902, -2.8946774005889893, -0.3121970295906067, 0.4574882388114929, 0.16439193487167358, 1.2784457206726074, 0.44220882654190063, 0.21721309423446655, 0.8573360443115234, 0.048249922692775726, 0.4083944261074066, 2.347456455230713, 0.988469123840332, 0.3670423030853271, -0.4668065905570984, 0.06506237387657166, -1.331370830535889, -0.8740202188491821, 0.17139989137649536, 0.1693064272403717, -0.7390615344047546, -1.098334550857544, 0.004179172217845917, 1.243135929107666, 0.9334880113601683, -0.7804409861564636, -0.3631633520126343, -0.40705394744873047, -0.319141387939