(155, NULL, 'ANALYSIS AND DEVELOPMENT OF ICT REPAIR MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR CAMARINES SUR POLYTECHNIC COLLEGES', 'ICT systems require maintenance and repair to ensure their longevity and optimal performance. In CSPC, the current repair management system for ICT systems is conducted manually and paper based. This method can be inefficient and prone to errors, which can result in delays in the repair process. Manual systems make it challenging to manage the inventory of ICT equipment and maintain proper records of repairs and maintenance work. In general, the objective is to Design and develop an ICT Repair Management System with Functional suitability, Performance efficiency, Usability, Reliability, and Maintainability. To address the objectives of the study, the researchers used a mixed method research design and the Extreme Programming. The study respondents were the faculties, admin, and ICT Repair and Maintenance Staff/technician. The data was obtained using an interview guide and survey questionnaire. The data was evaluated and interpreted using a weighted mean. The research findings indicate that there are problems with Time Efficiency, Potential Loss of Data, Generating Reports, and File Tracing Issues. Thus, the overall interpretation revealed that the suggested system is highly acceptable to the respondents. As a result, the proposed system is acceptable for implementation in Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges ICT Repair.', 'ROLAND B. POCON III, LHORENZ DALE C. PONTILLAS, JESSA MAY B. LANUZO', '[-0.027726799249649048, 0.17458756268024445, -3.27296781539917, -0.9799859523773192, 0.8355391025543213, -0.23799122869968417, 0.8807275891304016, 0.33553969860076904, 0.41092342138290405, -0.4515833854675293, 0.28753966093063354, -1.1204447746276855, 1.1035021543502808, 0.4111337661743164, -0.537639856338501, -0.18830780684947968, -0.652644157409668, -0.24518555402755737, -1.2144851684570312, 1.0136889219284058, 1.0428866147994995, -1.1880558729171753, -1.2649743556976