L, NULL, 'published'),
(162, NULL, 'BUILDING A PROPOSED PROTOTYPE USING DESIGN-THINKING: TOWARDS ENHANCING THE REGISTRATION PROCESS OF 4PS', 'With the advancement of technology, organizations constantly seek operational enhancements to improve customer satisfaction. This study focuses on optimizing manual transactions for the Department of Social Welfare and Development (DSWD) personnel, specifically in the registration process for 4Ps beneficiaries, using design thinking principles. The Pantawid Pamilyang Pilipino Program (4Ps) aims to break the cycle of poverty by providing cash grants to impoverished households, but challenges persist, particularly in the manual registration process. The study proposes a prototype based on design thinking principles to streamline operations, reduce workload, and enhance efficiency for DSWD personnel. To address the objectives of the study, the researchers will employ a mixed-method approach, incorporating both qualitative and quantitative research methods. The study respondents will be selected based on their availability and knowledge of the program, including DSWD staff/stakeholders and IT experts from the office of DSWD in Nabua, responsible for enrolling eligible households in the program. Data will be gathered through an interview guide to determine the current registration of 4Ps beneficiaries, observation to capture the actual journey of beneficiaries in the program, and evaluation of the proposed design system through a survey questionnaire. The analysis will be conducted using the weighted mean. The research findings indicate a significant acceptance rate of the Proposed Prototype Design among clients, receiving \"Strongly Agree\" ratings across various criteria, including system visibility status, technical feasibility, efficiency, and data security. Additionally, this highlights the unique strengths of digitalized automated registration compared to the manual registration process for 4Ps beneficiaries, addressing the specific needs of the main clients. Consequently, these recommendations suggest that future researchers should continue studying the system\'s implementation in the DSWD organization, striving to improve the system interface used by DSWD personnel in their daily operations.', 'ANNE-GELINE H. ACBANG, JOAN A. SILAVA', '[-0.8831794261932373, 1.1350884437561035, -3.3460264205932617, -0.6630693078041077, 0.5463829636573792, -0.2900373935699463, 0.4166436791419983, 1.112796664237976, 0.34890756011009216, 0.19792568683624268, 0.14179310202598572, -0.70448899269104, 1.2054383754730225, 0.201386034488678, 0.06605121493339539, 0.047432415187358856, -0.11413343250751495, -1.0604420900344849, -0.6393107175827026, 1.0021995306015017, 0.1532454788684845, -0.8408728837966919, -1.067983865737915, -0.39435797929763794, 1.4424538612365725, 0.5349356532096863, -0.2660037875175476, -0.6017272472381592, 0.09243720769882202, -0.8827145099639893, 0.47843486070632935, -0.33103954792022705, -0.09244346618652344, -0.517317533493042, -0.6080176830291748, -0.5092549324035645, 0.9273248910903932, -0.2708902955055237, 0.5474908351898193, -0.3587428033351898, 0.25016218423843384, -1.050401210784912, -0.19808244705200195, -1.1600342988967896, 1.3949904441833496, 0.15071798861026764, 1.6102027893066406, -0.419531762599945, 1.2815042734146118, 0.0801970362663269, 0.6250766515731812, -0.5420780181884766, 0.09687967598438264, 0.1734059453010559, 0.10214650630950928, -0.31727102398872375, -0.8859521150588989, 0.22589565813541412, -1.300485134124756, -0.8303748369216919, 1.4081778526306152, 2.5221304893493652, -0.2897503674030304, 1.8037900924682615, 0.9704063534736632, -0.13648855686187744, 0.4803609251976013, 0.21504652500152588, 0.5234956741333008, -0.9598021507263184, 0.10410558432340622, 0.6132074594497681, -0.7438976764678955, -0.2604370713233948, 0.9404261112213136, 0.601952314376831, -0.7487889528274536, -0.5800532102584839, -0.7951139211654663, 0.8256859183311462, 1.0034077167510986, -0.36756783723831177, 1.0255692005