(166, NULL, 'EVALUATION OF CSPC WEB-BASED TRAVEL AND TOURS SYSTEM OF THE COLLEGE OF TOURISM, HOSPITALITY, AND BUSINESS MANAGEMENT', 'With the advancement of technology, this study evaluates the CSPC Web-Based Travel and Tours System of the College of Tourism, Hospitality, and Business Management (CTHBM) to determine and alignment with the educational objectives of the Bachelor of Science in Tourism Management (BSTM) program. Using the DeLone and McLean IS Success Model, the research examines six dimensions: Information Quality, System Quality, Service Quality, Usage Intention, User Satisfaction, and Net System Benefits. A mixed-methods approach, incorporating surveys and interviews with faculty and students, was employed to collect qualitative and quantitative data. Findings indicate that the system effectively supports basic functionalities, such as reservation management, but reveals limitations in advanced features like real-time updates, system integration, and tailored user interfaces. Students and faculty expressed moderate satisfaction, particularly appreciating the system\'s role in bridging theoretical learning with practical application. However, areas such as information accuracy and user-centric service design require significant improvement. The study concludes that while the system has potential as a teaching tool, it necessitates enhancements to meet evolving academic and industry standards. Recommendations include updating system features for improved usability, integrating real-time functionalities, and aligning content with diverse user needs to ensure it remains an effective educational resource for future tourism professionals.', 'BEVERLY O. BEATO, AILA MARIE B. DAZA, MICAH ANGELA A. ESCOLANO', '[-1.712975263595581, 1.159287929534912, -3.5333476066589355, 0.18756431341171265, 0.4758524298667908, 1.183923840522766, 1.1295667886734009, 0.6535365581512451, 1.1595251560211182, -0.15892642736434937, 0.4696922302246094, -0.253786563873291, 1.3494027853