(168, NULL, 'IMPLEMENTATION OF DESIGN THINKING APPROACH IN ANALYSIS AND DESIGN OF APPOINTMENT TRANSACTION SYSTEM FOR MOTHER THERESA COLEGIO DE IRIGA', 'In today’s technology-driven world, integrating digital solutions has become crucial for improving efficiency, productivity, and user experience across various industries. Educational institutions, in particular, benefit significantly from streamlined processes that reduce manual workloads and enhance service delivery. In response to these needs, this study focuses on designing a user-centric Appointment and Transaction System for Mother Theresa Colegio de Iriga to address inefficiencies in traditional administrative processes such as appointment scheduling, financial transactions, and document requests. Using the Design Thinking approach, the project aims to optimize workflows with features like online payments and consultation scheduling, ensuring a visually appealing and reliable framework through tools such as Figma for UI design and Dia for database architecture. The system\'s effectiveness is evaluated through Heuristic Evaluation and ISO/IEC 25012 metrics, achieving high user satisfaction with a UI score of 3.48 and a database score of 3.67. The system excels in areas like user control and error prevention, while the database performs well in accuracy and credibility. A mixed-method approach, combining both qualitative and quantitative data collection, will be used to further explore these findings and enhance the system\'s overall usability and data quality.', 'KARLENE J. OBRERO, JOSEPH P. SALCEDO, ZYNIALEN D. SAUNAR', '[-0.4647343456745148, 1.30967116355896, -2.6372547149658203, -0.82129967212677, 0.4781078398227692, -0.7345976829528809, 0.8687694072723389, 0.8034943342208862, 0.11147452890872955, 0.8873792886734009, -0.005085214972496033, -0.5486197471618652, 1.9116125106811523, 0.61529541015625, -0.22641989588737488, 0.30881643295288086, -0.3661121726036072, -0.5589272975921631, -0.5272461175918579, 1.2594