(169, NULL, 'eLABA: A MOBILE BASED DESIGN FOR LAUNDRY SHOP', 'The study aimed to address operational inefficiencies in laundry shop services by designing a mobile-based system focused on user-centric features. The system included functionalities for booking, notifications, and logistics activities to streamline operations and improve user experience. The design incorporated user-centric principles to streamline workflows for both customers and shop administrators. The system was designed using user-centered design and Figma tool, meeting ISO 9241-210 usability and ISO/IEC 25012 data quality criteria. This approach ensured the design aligned with industry standards and incorporated principles of usability and human-centered design. The data reveals identified problems and challenges, and proposes a solution using UI and database design. Respondents highly approve of the UI design for accessibility, effectiveness, efficiency, human-centered design, satisfaction, and usability, while the database design is highly praised for accuracy, consistency, and completeness. The system\'s overall rating was strongly agreed upon for both usability and database metrics. The study\'s recommendations include extended data collection, incorporating a chat feature in the design application, considering system development for future projects, seeking UI and database experts to validate design solutions, and seeking 5-8 experts to enhance the credibility of the paper. In summary, by emphasizing effectiveness, usability, and optimized processes, the study effectively designed a user-centric, mobile-based system to address operational difficulties in wash shops. Through contemporary, visually appealing solutions, the design provides a basis for enhancing the customer experience and shop management procedures.', 'CLARIZA PLETADO ALARCON, EARL JAMES FOLLOSCO TRINIDAD, JESEBELLE DE LEON FUNDADOR', '[-0.948532223701477, 1.5050911903381348, -2.757551431655884, -1.315126657485962, 0.20690688490