(170, NULL, 'A Comprehensive Analysis and Design of SK Management System for Barangay Sagumay', 'Technology has become a transformative force across various sectors, and the public sector is no exception. In this connection, this study generally aimed to analyze and design a SK Management system for Barangay Sagumay. The evaluation will focus on system usability, and data quality. To address the objectives of the study, the researcher utilized the mixed-method approach, employing both quantitative and qualitative research methods. The study respondents were youth, SK officials, UI and IT experts of CSPC. The data was gathered through the researcher\'s evaluation through a survey questionnaire, analysis was done using the weighted mean and arithmetic mean. The researchers systematically followed the phases of the Design Thinking phases. The result shows that existing transaction process of SK transaction such as record-keeping, financial tracking, and project documentation are done manually. Furthermore, the evaluation of system usability and data quality was evaluated by the respondents with the overall average of 3.43 for system usability indicating “Highly Acceptable”, and 0.86 for data quality indicating as “Highly Acceptable”. As a result, these recommendations suggest future studies to develop and implement the proposed SK Management System.', 'NIÑO R. DACLESON, AMELYN T. LUZON, MICHELLE R. RIBOR', '[-0.6281493306159973, 1.4824196100234983, -2.775009870529175, -0.8552250266075134, 0.7332851886749268, -0.05351358652114868, 0.799014151096344, 0.134924054145813, 0.36788854002952576, 0.7205317616462708, 0.5975754261016846, -1.526315450668335, 1.7617374658584597, 0.48257043957710266, -0.05485234782099724, -0.5798599720001221, -1.11783766746521, -1.0158759355545044, -1.0772244930267334, 1.0016337633132937, 0.3302410840988159, -0.72306889295578, -0.8940005302429199, 0.24917583167552948, 1.4021190404891968, 0.03642410784959793, -0.34413447976112366, -0.0637120753526687