(171, NULL, 'EVALUATION OF AGONOS DENTAL CLINIC: IMPLEMENTING DELONE AND MCLEAN APPROACH', 'This research assesses the quality of services and information systems of Agonos Dental Clinic based on the DeLone and McLean Information Systems Success Model. The purpose of the research is to assess patient care processes and technology utilization in management to determine their effectiveness and pinpoint the clinic’s strengths and weaknesses. Primary data was collected through survey questionnaires and interviews of patients and staff with specific focus on the six dimensions: system quality; information quality; service quality; use; user satisfaction; and net benefits. The research findings show that the quality of service and satisfaction of users are high but the system and information quality are lacking in some aspects. The analysis indicates that there is a potential benefit for patients, and an improvement in operations, if these dimensions are lifted. This study advances the knowledge base in practice, showing how the DeLone and McLean model can be implemented by a dental clinic, and provides the clinic with strategies on how to improve service and technology penetration.', 'JESICA ELCANO, KRISTINE P. MEDIADO, MARICEL S. ZAGADA', '[-0.7800639867782593, 0.750109851360321, -3.1789703369140625, -1.5851554870605469, 1.0382128953933716, -0.2056805789470673, 0.11890110373497008, 0.20176933705806732, 1.125694990158081, 0.5492576956748962, 0.5745710134506226, -0.2035273015499115, 1.7264634370803833, -0.5208340287208557, 0.3506905734539032, -0.5299960374832153, -0.9427189826965332, -1.1287353038787842, -0.3743304610252381, 0.2156047821044922, -0.4270443916320801, -0.7198092341423035, -0.9331289529800416, -1.57379150390625, 1.6593506336212158, 1.0271368026733398, -0.01823631301522255, 0.5687078237533569, -0.5315333008766174, 0.12543654441833496, 1.3314588069915771, -0.5572894215583801, -0.3113950788974762, 0.1475871205329895, -0.7132288217544556, -0.6916892528533936, -0.