(172, NULL, 'Implementation of Delone and McLean Model in the Impact Assessment of CSPC Library Kiosks', 'The study implements the Delone and McLean Information System Success Model to assessThe study implements the Delone and McLean Information System Success Model to assess the impact of Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges (CSPC) Library Kiosks, focusing on the OPAC and Log-In Kiosk systems. These kiosks are critical in streamlining library processes, enhancing accessibility, and ensuring efficient service delivery. This research aims to evaluate system effectiveness based on six dimensions: system quality, information quality, service quality, intention to use, user satisfaction, and net benefits. Using a mixed-methods approach, the study combined qualitative interviews to define existing processes and quantitative surveys to assess user feedback on system performance. The findings reveal that both kiosks effectively meet user expectations, with the OPAC kiosk scoring 3.48 and the Log-In kiosk scoring 3.42 in system quality. For information quality, the OPAC kiosk achieved a score of 3.40, while the Log-In kiosk scored 3.36. Similarly, in service quality, the OPAC kiosk scored 3.34 and the Log-In kiosk 3.30. In terms of intention to use, the OPAC kiosk received a score of 3.62 and the Log-In kiosk 3.58. User satisfaction scores were slightly lower, with the OPAC kiosk achieving 3.45 and the Log-In kiosk 3.39. Lastly, the net benefits dimension saw the OPAC kiosk scoring 3.57 and the Log-In kiosk 3.53. While these results demonstrate the kiosks’ effectiveness, limitations such as database dependency, occasional hardware failures, and maintenance challenges were identified. The research highlights the need for continuous system updates, addressing these limitations, and incorporating user feedback to enhance functionality. The findings underscore the importance of leveraging advanced information systems to optimize library services, ensuring user satisfaction, and meeting institutional goals. The study concludes by proposing actionable recommendations for system improvements and emphasizes the Delone and McLean model’s relevance in evaluating information systems in library settings. These insights aim to guide future technological adaptations and policymaking within academic libraries.', 'MICHAEL JOSHUA A. ALDAVE, APPRILLE MARGRETE BANTE, KENT A. REFORSADO', '[-1.1962463855743408, 0.9130235910415648, -2.368086814880371, -1.964169979095459, 0.5060616135597229, -0.138311505317688, -0.3179309070110321, 1.612615942955017, 0.13090190291404724, 0.15189340710639954, -0.1165737435221672, -0.5912132263183594, 2.4354166984558105, 0.4508425891399383, 1.1711225509643557, -0.4778062701225281, -0.18442149460315704, -1.2993344068527222, 0.12978850305080414, 0.331952840089798, -0.3436228036880493, -0.8261038064956665, -2.552234411239624, -1.5979173183441162, 1.7752078771591189, 1.1278924942016602, 0.1943813264369965, -0.1979397088289261, -1.1500968933105469, 0.6604009866714478, 0.4703523516654968, -0.9122332334518432, -0.5185058116912842, -0.9865050315856934, -1.2066466808319092, 0.1289462000131607, 0.30332624912261963, -0.47081854939460754, 0.327284574508667, 0.6849453449249268, 0.33449530601501465, -0.20576587319374084, 0.6054543256759644, -0.3224468231201172, 0.10358081012964249, -0.4646859169006348, 0.7600101232528687, -0.01015140861272812, 1.014609694480896, -0.26600274443626404, 0.4366614818572998, 0.03054036572575569, 0.1845187544822693, 0.8841041326522827, 0.10246435552835464, 0.694325864315033, -0.38531243801116943, -0.48240792751312256, -0.4024386703968048, -0.6131224632263184, 1.5725741386413574, 2.021510601043701, -0.5835985541343689, 0.8425202965736389, 0.9816614389419556, -0.7728825807571411, 0.27597692608833313, 1.318747878074646, 0.6277037858963013, -0.8859140276908875, 0.6321120262145996, 0.31943410634994507, 0.1389477550983429, -0.1719740927219391, 0.03550312668085098, 0.906301736831665, -0.6671665906906128, -0.5265547037124