(174, NULL, 'Design of a Web-based Platform for Management and Analysis of Disaster and Emergency Report in Nabua, Camarines Sur', 'Technology in the modern world is rapidly changing and companies can transition of manual-based activities and move to use digital systems that are more efficient. The purpose of the study was to design an online system of disaster and emergency reports management and analysis in the Municipality of Nabua, Camarines Sur. In this regard, the researchers have utilized the User-Centered Design (UCD) tool corresponding to ISO 9241-210 to make sure that the web-based platform directly responded to issues and needs of the Municipal Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Office (MDRRMO). The researchers optimized the interface of the platform and general functionalities of the site through survey, interview, usability, and expert review to enhance accessibility, readability, and data sorting. Results showed that the developed system improved the management of disaster reports greatly with high rates being accepted in functionality, satisfaction and usability, and that users rated that the workflows became smoother, the process of retrieving the information became quicker and the accuracy of documented reports was improved. Specifically, digitalization enabled the employees of MDRRMO to work more on decision-making and response to emergencies instead of doing the same encoding over and over again. The research proposes the extension of the platform by real-time capabilities, automated analytics, and mobile capabilities to enhance the disaster preparedness of Nabua. Future researchers can also replicate or expand the system to other municipalities to investigate how a single digital platform can facilitate the process of disaster and emergency operations across Camarines Sur.', 'MARK RAYVEN A. ADANTE, RHEDELYN A. SALAZAR, JINKY A. VELASCO', '[-0.30583322048187256, 0.1519998013973236, -3.603198528289795, -0.3163485527038574, 1.3276721239089966, -