(181, NULL, 'A User-Centered Design of Registrar’s Transaction Management System for Mother Theresa Colegio de Iriga', 'In today\'s computerized world, technology enhances an organization\'s capacity to manage files or documents that helps to automate processes and improves employee work performance effectively and efficiently. The study aimed to create a system tailored to the Registrar’s specific needs. The general objective of this study aims to design a UI/UX and database design for Mother Theresa Colegio De Iriga Registrar’s Office. It specifically aims to; determine the current processes; identify current problems encountered; and design a user interface and database for the Registrar Transaction Management System for Mother Theresa Colegio De Iriga. The researchers followed the User Centered Design Framework and Data collection involved interviews, observations, and surveys. The findings are; lack of centralized data management resulted in delays, difficulty in retrieving information, increased potential errors; strong consensus that a digital solution could significantly improve overall student experience. The transaction Management System; designed prototype was rated by the respondents; (3.37) “Highly Acceptable”, and database design was evaluated resulting (0.86) - \"Highly Acceptable”. Therefore; Transaction Management System support by a robust database design and user-friendly interface; offers a solution to address these issues; proposed system automates the operations and enhance the transparency of transactions. The interactive prototype was created utilizing Figma, while MySQL provided the backend database; the system adheres to essential usability principles. Future research can create a mobile application version of the system; further develop and fully implement the proposed Transaction Management System for the Registrar’s Office; could enhance system features; and may integrate AI to automate processes.', 'RYAN G. OLLERES, PATRICK M. PAPA, GEL