(182, NULL, 'Odoo Enterprise Resource Planning Implementation for An Entrepreneur Managing Multiple Businesses', 'This study developed and implemented an Odoo Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) system for JMampuag Grooming Studio and Coffee 360°, two distinct businesses owned by a single entrepreneur. The project aimed to centralize and automate core operations, such as sales, purchasing, inventory, and point of sale (POS), to enhance decision-making and efficiency. Using Business Process Modeling Notation (BPMN), existing workflows were analyzed and redesigned. A mixed-methods approach combined qualitative insights from stakeholder interviews with quantitative evaluation based on ISO 25010 software quality standards. The system was rigorously assessed across four key criteria: functional suitability, performance efficiency, compatibility, and interaction capability. Results from business users and ERP experts revealed strong performance, with functional suitability and performance efficiency both rated highly, with a weighted mean of 4.95, indicating robust support for core processes and fast, reliable operation. Compatibility scored 4.9, confirming excellent integration across devices and seamless data exchange between modules. Interaction capability scored 4.75, reflecting a user-friendly interface, though a slight learning curve was noted for non- technical staff. The findings demonstrate that the implemented Odoo ERP system significantly reduced manual errors, accelerated transactions, and provided real-time operational visibility. The study confirms Odoo ERP as a scalable, cost-effective solution for entrepreneurs managing multiple businesses, effectively bridging operational gaps and fostering data-driven management. Recommendations include optimizing real-time synchronization and enhancing user training to maximize system adoption and long-term impact for SMEs in multi-service environments.', 'ADRIAN S. ALIVIADO, JOHN LLOYD M. BOTEÑO, KLYNTZ YTRX T. ELEVADO'