(183, NULL, 'Designing Alert Hub: A User-Centered Web Interface for Barangay Disaster Response', 'The health of a community is at risk by both natural and man-made disasters, which frequently cause disorganization when planning is insufficient. Rising data on disaster-related casualties, which show insufficient resilience in certain areas, highlights the Philippines as one of the countries most prone to these kinds of disasters. The researchers will use a mixed-methods research design, combining qualitative and quantitative techniques, to examine the current level of preparedness for disasters and evaluate the possible effects of creating a web interface for the Barangay Disaster Response for the Barangay Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Committee (BDRRMC). The system evaluation using Nielsen’s 10 Heuristics shows that barangay officials and staff found AlertHub highly functional and user-friendly, appreciating its clear alerts, intuitive interface, and organized layout. Meanwhile, the data quality assessment under ISO/IEC 25012:2008 indicates that the system generally performs', 'JOHN LESTER P. DELA CRUZ, JOSHUA R. BUSTAMANTE, CRISZABETH ANGELA B. AMOTO', '[-0.4980576038360596, 0.25032350420951843, -3.566164493560791, -0.5060812830924988, 1.846341133117676, 0.17133311927318573, 0.39653876423835754, 0.32844170928001404, 0.3434925973415375, -1.5983803272247314, 0.5435738563537598, -1.0181481838226318, 1.6001726388931274, 1.0734448432922363, 0.9617438316345216, -0.9402558207511902, -0.5905728340148926, -0.0007030721753835678, -1.4608920812606812, 0.5626727342605591, -0.342875599861145, -0.951300084590912, -0.5643431544303894, 0.1153176799416542, 0.8389471173286438, 1.009727954864502, 0.46929022669792175, 0.7631186842918396, -0.7745321393013, -0.6771793961524963, 0.49080342054367065, -0.7033801078796387, -0.7393527030944824, -1.059484601020813, -0.14578701555728912, -0.2251617461442947, -0.8250212669372559, -0.32931774854660034, 0.6964857578277588, 0.292994529008