(184, NULL, 'Designing an Online Platform for Streamlining Boarding House Selection Near CSPC Campus', 'In the current academic year, while the demand for boarding houses is high, the process of finding a suitable and accredited boarding house remains a significant problem for students and parents. The project aimed to identify SASO’s challenges, analyze manual boarding house selection methods, develop a web-based design and database, and evaluate these using established standards. The evaluation utilized ISO/IEC 25024:2015 for the database design and Heuristic Evaluation for the User Interface (UI). The methodology employed was the Design Thinking Approach. The research design utilized a mixed-method approach that combined qualitative (interview guide) and quantitative (questionnaire) methods. Data gathering procedures focused on Specific Objectives 1 and 2 (interviews) and Specific Objectives 3 and 4 (questionnaires). Data analysis was conducted using the weighted mean. Based on the gathered data, it was found that the process is still manual and has no central online platform. Additionally, the evaluation of the system design and database, conducted by UI and DB experts, yielded favorable results: the overall average for the DB evaluation is 3.45 (indicating \"Strongly Agree\") and for the UI evaluation is 3.64 (indicating \"Strongly Agree\"). The primary conclusion is that collaboration between the Local Government Unit (LGU) of Nabua and SASO is crucial for implementation. The recommendations suggest that the logical next step for this project is the full development and implementation of the proposed design.', 'CARL JOSHUA P. BELORO, MARK ALLEN B. OLINO, JOREY L. TUBIERAS', '[-0.2920694351196289, 1.6331833600997925, -3.1124043464660645, -1.0056217908859253, -0.6950799226760864, 0.8304957747459412, 0.4817374646663666, 1.6461694240570068, 0.21959371864795685, 0.029747191816568375, -0.4334861040115357, -0.60003662109375, 1.9535408020019531, 0.7661067843437195, -0