(187, NULL, 'A User-Centered Design for Zantua-Nonato Dental Care (ZNDC) Clinic Management System', 'Many dental clinics still use manual appointment scheduling and paper-based patient records, which often cause long waiting times, scheduling conflicts, and difficulty in retrieving patient information. This study presents a user-centered design for a Clinic Management System intended for the multiple branches of Zantua-Nonato Dental Care (ZNDC). The proposed system aims to improve appointment scheduling, patient record management, clinic workflow, usability, accessibility, and data quality. The study followed the Design Thinking methodology, consisting of the Empathize, Define, Ideate, Prototype, and Test phases. Data were gathered through interviews, surveys, and observations involving dentists, clinic staff, and patients. The system design focuses on simple and intuitive UI/UX, accessibility features, and structured data management based on ISO/IEC 25012 data quality standards. Evaluation results from end-users and database experts indicate that the proposed design is easy to use, improves clinic efficiency, and ensures more accurate and consistent data compared to the existing manual process. The study concludes that a user-centered design approach is effective in improving clinic operations and user experience in dental clinics.', 'HAROLD B. FERRER, MECHAELLA T. LITA, RICKO D. ZORILLA', '[-0.5790995359420776, 0.551262378692627, -2.8334689140319824, -0.9897394180297852, -0.2814975380897522, -0.46617549657821655, 0.830952525138855, -0.34467318654060364, 0.6912921071052551, 0.03912879899144173, -0.005896089598536491, -0.6113664507865906, 1.888128638267517, -0.6813802719116211, -0.12620028853416443, -0.1552167385816574, -0.9696066975593568, -0.4456450939178467, -1.1897528171539309, 0.5297729969024658, -0.14232954382896423, -0.11620232462882996, -0.759042501449585, -0.4754730463027954, 0.8720812797546387, 0.3886024057865143, 0.8735684156417847, 1.178756833076477, -0.