(188, NULL, 'Implementation of Smart Barangay Census System in Bacolod, Bato Camarines Sur: A Feasibility Study', 'The census process in Barangay Bacolod, Bato, Camarines Sur heavily relies on manual, paper-based, and house-to-house data collection methods, making it time-consuming, labor-intensive, and prone to data loss. This study aims to assess the feasibility of implementing a SMART Barangay Census System to improve the census process and enhance operational efficiency. Specifically, it examines the current census procedures, identifies existing issues and challenges, and evaluates the feasibility of adopting the proposed system using the TELOS framework, which assesses five key factors: Technical, Economic, Legal, Operational, and Schedule feasibility. A mixed-method approach combining quantitative and qualitative research designs was utilized. Data were collected through surveys, field observations, and structured interviews with barangay officials, census enumerators, and IT experts’ individuals directly involved in the census process. Supporting documents and journals were also reviewed for data validation. Quantitative data gathered through a Likert- scale survey were analyzed using weighted means, while qualitative data were thematically analyzed to provide deeper insights. Results revealed that the current census process suffers from issues such as incomplete resident data, data loss due to calamities, and discrepancies between census forms and record books. The feasibility analysis indicated strong agreement across all aspects of the TELOS framework, with local server hosting identified as the most suitable option for implementation, this implies that barangay is capable in developing the proposed system. The study recommends a strategic plan to guide Barangay Bacolod in adopting the SMART Barangay Census System in alignment with its available resources and assessment results.', 'JUNHECA CASTRO, LADYLINE I. BENEGAS, JOHN JOWARD S. LORIA', '[-0.215015888