(189, NULL, 'Integration of Robotic Process Automation (RPA) 1.0 for Student Prospectus Generation in the College of Computer Studies', 'As technological advancements continue to accelerate, automation has emerged as a key enabler of process efficiency. This study focused on integrating Robotic Process Automation (RPA) 1.0 into the student prospectus generation process of the College of Computer Studies (CCS) at Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges (CSPC). To achieve this, the researchers used Business Process Management (BPM) to improve the current process for completing the prospectus. The existing process of student prospectus generation was first examined to assess its potential for automation then redesigning the process with RPA 1.0 using Power Automate Desktop (PAD) and evaluating the integration for accuracy and time efficiency. Multi-methods, including interviews and observations, inspection journal, and simulation journal offered constructive feedback from the students, faculties and CCS Dean’s Office Staff. These insights improved the development of the redesigned and automated student prospectus generation. Findings revealed that integrating RPA 1.0 significantly enhanced the student prospectus generation, achieving 100% accuracy, reducing the process time by an average of 12 minutes per section, and shortening the manual prospectus from seven days to one day. Particularly, automation allowed human staff to manage complex cases effectively. The study recommends implementing RPA in future enrollment procedure to further improve the student prospectus process. Future researchers can conduct the same study in other colleges whether Robotic Process Automation could automate and streamline the academic operations in Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges.', 'EZRA FAE M. ALFORTE, HAZEL M. NOJARA, CHRISTINE JOY M. RELATORES', '[-0.2587572932243347, 0.8993418216705322, -2.850656032562256, -0.5792118310928345, 0.35232311487197876, 0.2339089512825012, 1.4352288246154783