(193, NULL, 'RESIDENT AND VISITOR MANAGEMENT SYSTEM: A FRONT-END AND DATABASE DESIGN', 'This study presents the design of a Resident and Visitor Management System focused on front-end development and database structuring for small to mid-sized apartment operations. Many Philippine residential establishments still rely on manual record-keeping, resulting in inconsistent data, limited accessibility, and inefficient workflows for tenant profiling, visitor logging, billing, maintenance requests, and notifications. To address these issues, the study applied the User-Centered Design (UCD) framework to analyze existing business processes in three apartment sites, identify user requirements, and produce a semi-functional web-based prototype. The interface was developed using HTML, Alpine.js, and Tailwind CSS, while the database design was modeled using MySQL and normalized to ensure accuracy and consistency. The system includes modules for tenant profiling, visitor management, lease and billing tracking, service requests, and emergency notifications, all tailored to reflect real operational workflows. Usability and database quality were evaluated by 30 tenants, 3 landlords, 6 UI experts, and 6 database experts using heuristic metrics such as Match Between System and the Real World, Consistency and Standards, and ISO/IEC 25012 data-quality principles. Findings indicate that the prototype effectively improves clarity, reduces redundancy, and supports organized digital management. Although not fully implemented, the prototype demonstrates the feasibility of adopting user-centered, database-driven solutions in apartment settings.', 'JOSHUA RYAN R. TATARO, MARLO ANTHONY T. NUEVA, DANICA M. CADAG', '[-0.6161755323410034, 1.085443377494812, -3.4626731872558594, -0.388063371181488, -0.013197568245232104, -0.38050320744514465, 0.863813579082489, 0.7613809704780579, 0.18691220879554749, -0.7231537699699402, -0.1671869456768036, -0.8241351842880249, 1.3860273361206057, -0.457903712987