(196, NULL, 'EFFECTIVENESS OF SERVICES IN CSPC LIBRARY AND SATISFACTION OF FACULTY AND STUDENTS IN UTILIZING THE LIBRARY SERVICES OF CAMARINES SUR POLYTECHNIC COLLEGES, NABUA, CAMARINES SUR SY 2019-2020', 'Libraries serve as organizers and play a key role in the distribution of information resources and services to assist library users with their research and education. The library is a repository for information (i.e., print and non- print format). In any library, the users are at the center. They must, in turn, because libraries exist solely to serve their patrons, be satisfied with the quality of services provided by the library. The study was carried out to examine the effectiveness of services in the CSPC library and the satisfaction of faculty and students in utilizing the library services. Data was collected using a survey questionnaire from 229 respondents from the College of Computerstudies. The results showed that library users were “Strongly Agree” on the level of effectiveness and have a \"Very High\" satisfaction with library service before the pandemic; library users were \"Agree\" on the level of effectiveness and have a “High\" satisfaction with library service during the pandemic. A significant difference was noted between different library services when grouped according to faculty and student before and during pandemic. Likewise, there was a significant relationship between the respondent assessment before and during the pandemic; theoretical and practical implications were discussed. It was concluded in the study that the Academic library service of CSPC before and during the pandemic is efficient and effective, but due to the pandemic its services were limited to multiple access, but still considerable and it is still efficient and effective that way. The clientele both students and teachers were satisfied.', 'Carla V. Galan, Janiña D. Villarico, Ma. Jessa G. Florin', '[-1.3000516891479492, 0.9264429807662964, -3.649974822998047, -1.262548685073