(1, 1, 'duplication-checks/KkLE3OdUEiwyXOtWqlBAA9g89DvL3gzx1DDQ3VLC.pdf', '{\"sdm\": \"Agile Development Methodology\", \"scope\": \"The proposed web system will focus exclusively on capstone-related activities within CSPC–CCS, centralizing all processes to improve workflow efficiency and maintain academic integrity.\", \"title\": \"CapsTrack: A Centralized Web-Based Capstone Project Management System at CSPC– College of Computer Studies\", \"domain\": \"Web System\", \"keywords\": [\"web-based\", \"capstone project\", \"management\", \"centralized\", \"secure accounts\", \"AI plagiarism detection\", \"workflow efficiency\"], \"sdg_goals\": \"SDG 4 – Quality Education\", \"main_topic\": \"Development of a web-based capstone management system for CSPC–CCS\", \"limitations\": \"The system is limited to CSPC–CCS capstone projects only; duplication checking is restricted to archived prior studies and stored capstone outputs; internet access is required for the system to function; grading, evaluation, and final decisions remain the responsibility of instructors; the platform does not replace official academic record systems.\", \"target_users\": \"Students and instructors at CSPC–CCS\", \"technologies\": [\"web-based\", \"AI plagiarism detection\", \"secure accounts\"], \"research_agenda\": [\"Technology Development and Innovation\", \"e-Services\", \"Educational Management\", \"Applications and Systems Development\"], \"problem_statement\": \"The College of Computer Studies (CCS) of CSPC currently lacks a centralized web-based system for managing capstone projects, leading to inefficiencies, miscommunication, delayed outputs, and potential academic integrity issues.\", \"proposed_solution\": \"Develop a web-based capstone management system for CSPC–CCS, providing secure student and instructor accounts, allowing students to apply for advisers, consultants, and grammarians, submit capstone outputs online, review and annotate submissions, manage schedules, track progress, and perform AI-based duplication checks.\"}', 40, 'Passed', '[{\"score\": 40, \"title\": \"CAPSTONE PROJECT AND THESIS CLASS INFORMATIONMAN AGEMENT SYSTEM\", \"reason\": \"Both systems focus on managing capstone projects but differ in specific features and scope.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"Capstone projects have become a crucial part of a student\'s education in the modern world, laying the foundation for further learning. It gives students the capacity to retain the information they learned during college studies and use it when want to pursue a certain academic path in college. Paper-based solutions lack flexibility in handling evaluations, are less effective at gathering data, and are challenging to access when communicating information about a Capstone Project. Students were unable to obtain assessments that they required to make changes as a result, which delayed the encoding of grades. In general, the objective is to develop a system that were automate the process of Capstone Project and Thesis Class Information with Deliverables Monitoring, Participation Rating, Oral Examination Scheduling, Oral Examination Rating, and Honorarium Computation. To address the objectives of the study, the researcher used a mixed-method research design and an Extreme programming model. The study respondents were the Capstone Subject Adviser, Thesis Subject Adviser, Panelist, and Capstone Students of the Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges. The data was obtained using interviews, and surveys, and the data was evaluated using a weighted mean and percentage. The research findings indicate that there are problems with manually rating the paper of students, having trouble creating reports, and sharing the data. Thus, the overall interpretation revealed that the suggested system is moderately acceptable to the respondents. As a result, the developed system Capstone Project and Thesis Class Information Management System (CAPTCIMS) still needs further development for improvement.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Consider adding AI-based plagiarism detection or workflow optimization features to align with the core concept of a management system for capstone projects.\", \"archived_id\": 57, \"differences\": \"CapsTrack focuses on AI-based plagiarism detection and workflow efficiency, while the archived document emphasizes grading and honorarium computation.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"both manage capstone projects for students and faculty\", \"academic_year\": \"2022\"}, {\"score\": 34, \"title\": \"ESCHOLAR: A COMPREHENSIVE WEB-BASED SCHOLARSHIP APPLICATION PORTAL CONNECTING GOVERNMENT AND STUDENTS\", \"reason\": \"Semantically similar based on vector embedding analysis.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The eScholar Web-Based Scholarship Application Portal is an online portal was created to address the challenges in government scholarship procedure. The main objective of the study is to develop a centralized system that allows students to find scholarships at ease, can submit applications through online, and also allowed them to track their application progress, while on the other hand, administrators and government officials managed the posting management, application assessment and communication that allowed students to be informed. The study used a mixed method approach that combined qualitative interview methods with quantitative survey data and system evaluation results to develop and evaluate the system. The system development used agile methodologies that followed a structure based on data flow diagrams, entity relationship diagrams, and modular functional components. The equivalent partition testing with the use of Puppeteer simulation tool, it showed that all essential system modules worked correctly without discovering any system failures. The User acceptance testing produced a mean rating of 4.51 that showed that the system achieved high levels of usability, simplicity, and usefulness. The evaluation instrument showed high reliability because its Cronbach’s alpha score reached 0.98 which indicates excellent internal consistency. The system maintained a stable performance during stress testing that involved with multiple simulated users at once and security testing proved that the system protected against typical high security threats.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 27, \"differences\": \"\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 34, \"title\": \"EDUCONNECT: A SMART WEB-BASED ACADEMIC MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR STA. JUSTINA NATIONAL HIGH SCHOOL\", \"reason\": \"Semantically similar based on vector embedding analysis.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"Academic management in secondary schools have to deal with manual and semi-digital processes. These processes lead to inefficiencies, inaccuracies in data, and a lack of communication among stakeholders. This is the case with Sta. Justina National High School (SJNHS), where traditional methods dominate operations. This paper contributes to the field by proposing EduConnect: A Smart Web-Based Academic Management System. EduConnect is designed to automate and streamline the central processes and pent processes of academics and administration. These include enrollment, attendance, grade tracking, scheduling, announcements, and reporting. EduConnect provides role-based access to students, teachers, administrators, and parents. The system is built on a technical stack that includes CodeIgniter 4, PHP, JavaScript, MySQL, HTML 5, and Bootstrap. The system was built using the Agile Software Development Methodology. This is a process that allows for incremental development and refinement based on user feedback. Existing academic workflows were analyzed to identify gaps and difficulty in record keeping, accessibility of information, and communication. EduConnect was assessed using Black Box Testing to meet the requirements of the ISO 25010 software quality model. Use case testing and requirement-based testing scored 0.99 while usability testing was 0.99 and compatibility testing was 1.00 . According to the Nikto Docker security test, EduConnect has proper data and access control along with good security configurations. EduConnect has no critical or high security risks. The third-party findings were also non-impacting. With performance testing using Apache JMeter, the findings show concurrent users, given all 1,809 requests finished with 0 errors, took reasonable time to respond, and recorded 5.20 transactions per second, on average. Overall, EduConnect passed all tests confirming it is operational, user oriented, safe, efficient, and dependable, thereby greatly improving SJNHS’ academic management.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 32, \"differences\": \"\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 34, \"title\": \"CHRONOLOCK: AN INTEGRATION OF WEB-BASED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR THE SMART DOOR LOCK SYSTEM OF CCS ERP LABORATORY\", \"reason\": \"Semantically similar based on vector embedding analysis.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"This study addresses the challenges faced in the ERP Laboratory of the College of Computer Studies, including an unsecured access control system, inefficient attendance monitoring, inflexible scheduling, and inefficient laboratory security monitoring. To enhance laboratory management, a web-based management system was developed utilizing Lean Agile methodology alongside a mixed-method research approach that combined both quantitative and qualitative data. Total enumeration sampling was employed to select respondents for the study. The evaluation of the system\'s functionality and performance involved black box testing, with unit testing conducted in collaboration with end users, including students, faculty, laboratory personnel, and administrative staff. IT experts performed integration, load, and stress testing to assess the system\'s capabilities. The arithmetic mean was employed to assess the gathered data. Load testing demonstrated strong performance, with an error rate of 0.00% across various workload conditions. Unit, stress, and integration testing each achieved a perfect score of 1.00, confirming the system\'s compliance with requirements, efficiency under high loads, and seamless component integration. The results indicate that the newly developed web-based management system is ready to significantly improve convenience and overall management in the CCS ERP Laboratory.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 92, \"differences\": \"\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"\", \"academic_year\": \"2024\"}, {\"score\": 34, \"title\": \"CHRONOLOCK: A MOBILE APPLICATION FOR INTERNET-ENABLE D ACCESS CONTROL OF THE CCS ERP LABORATORY SMART DOOR LOCK SYSTEM SPENSYS: WEB-BASED SOLUTIONS FOR ENROLLMENT AND ACADEMIC RECORDS WITH AI CHATBOT FOR NABUA NATIONAL HIGH SCHOOL\", \"reason\": \"Semantically similar based on vector embedding analysis.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The increasing demand for efficient and accurate school information systems highlights the need for digital solutions that streamline enrollment, scheduling, and academic records management. SPEnSys addresses this need by providing Nabua National High School with an integrated web-based platform capable of automating student registration, managing academic records, generating real-time reports, and offering 24/7 support through an AI chatbot named SPEnBot. The system centralizes academic and administrative processes, reduces manual encoding errors, enhances accessibility, and supports data-driven decision-making through analytics. This project aimed to evaluate and develop a fully functional digital solution that improves the institution’s workflow. Guided by the Extreme Programming (XP) methodology, the system underwent iterative development, continuous stakeholder involvement, and thorough testing. Data were gathered from administrators, teachers, students, and IT experts through surveys and multiple testing procedures. Black box testing, including unit testing, user acceptance testing, performance testing, and usability testing, was used to validate the system’s functionality. Results showed that SPEnSys achieved a “Highly Functional” rating across all testing phases, confirming its reliability, efficiency, and readiness for deployment. Overall, SPEnSys successfully addressed the challenges of Nabua National High School’s semi-manual processes by providing a centralized, secure, and user-friendly digital platform. The integration of the AI chatbot, cloud-based deployment, and role- based access control further positions the system as a modern, scalable solution capable of supporting future academic and administrative requirements.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 17, \"differences\": \"\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 34, \"title\": \"CBSTrac: A Web-Based Alumni Tracking System for Central Bicol State University of Agriculture\", \"reason\": \"Semantically similar based on vector embedding analysis.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"Fragmented alumni records, low participation, and the lack of automated reporting are among the current problems that the Alumni Office of Central Bicol State University of Agriculture (CBSUA) face. This paper introduces CBSTrac, a web-based alumni tracking system for the Central Bicol State University of Agriculture in response to the identified problems. The system includes key features such as alumni onboarding with masterlist cross-checking, profile management, tracer survey, QR code event attendance, job posting using APIs for scraping and fetching, donation tracking, internal messaging, and analytics-based reporting. The researchers found that CBSTrac has the potential to create a centralized place for all alumni employment, involvement and participation information in a near real-time environment with ease of access, organization and analysis. From the results of our black box testing, CBSTrac was rated highly. The Functionality score was (3.77), Usability (3.83), Compatibility Score (3.77), Security Score (3.87), and Performance Score (3.77) giving the overall score of (3.80) which was interpreted as Excellent. The results demonstrated that the CBSTrac is . The findings from this study supported that CBSTrac met its purpose by providing a secure and efficient means of using data, improving the accuracy of data, automating many administrative processes, and enhancing alumni participation and tracking. Additionally, this study lays the foundation for future enhancements that may also explore the implementation of advanced predictive modeling and machine learning to forecast employment trends and further align the university curriculum with evolving industry needs.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 51, \"differences\": \"\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 34, \"title\": \"CSPC Student Event Calendar System Version 3.0\", \"reason\": \"Semantically similar based on vector embedding analysis.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"In today\'s society, technology plays a crucial role in communication, information storage, and learning, facilitating access to essential information and aiding in educational endeavors. This capstone project aimed to develop and implement a CSPC Student Event Calendar Version 3.0 for the students of the Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges. The objectives were to identify the functionality limitations of the Android-based CSPC Calendar System Version 2.0, develop an improved version, and evaluate Version 3.0 using black box techniques like use case testing and requirement-based testing. The study employed a mixed- method research design, with 387 students, 33 CSPC Organization Officers, and 6 SASO staff as target respondents. Findings revealed functional limitations of CSPC Calendar v2.0, notably its lack of integration with other devices and unreliable distribution of announcements, hindering seamless interaction in different technological environments and communication efficiency at events. Version 3.0 addressed these issues by utilizing Extreme Programming and technologies like Dart, Flutter, and Firebase, enhancing account review, database security, feedback features, and announcements capability. Black Box Testing demonstrated high system capability, with scores of 0.93 in Use Case Testing and 0.99 in Requirement-based Testing, indicating improved user experience, security, and participation. These findings underscore the importance of addressing system vulnerabilities and implementing upgrades to meet the diverse needs of the CSPC community effectively. In conclusion, the upgrade to v3.0 successfully addressed performance limitations seen in v2.0, notably enhancing account verification, database security, and announcement features.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 79, \"differences\": \"\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"\", \"academic_year\": \"2023\"}, {\"score\": 30, \"title\": \"OptiCCS: AN INTEGRATED SYSTEM FOR MONITORING AND MANAGING COMPUTER AND LABORATORY EQUIPMENT FOR THE COLLEGE OF COMPUTER STUDIES\", \"reason\": \"The core concept of the archived document focuses on managing laboratory equipment, not capstone projects.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The College of Computer Studies (CCS) at Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges struggles with inefficient paper-based laboratory management that lacks real-time monitoring for student activity and equipment. To address this, the researchers developed OptiCCS, an integrated web- based system for laboratory and equipment management. The system, built using Agile Scrum methodology, integrates a web application with a real-time monitoring application. The web application, developed on the CodeIgniter PHP framework with a MySQL database, manages inventory, class creation, role-based access, and report generation. The real-time monitoring service uses a Python client agent on each computer unit, connecting to a server built with React HTTP for API requests and the Ratchet WebSocket library for bi-directional communication, enabling live status reporting, screenshot feeds, violation detection, and remote command execution. The system uses Google OAuth for authentication. System validation involved black box testing for functionality, usability, and performance. Administrators, faculty, technicians, and students participated using a questionnaire, and the results were assessed based on the ISO 25010 software quality standard. Findings demonstrated a strong readiness for daily operation: Unit Testing yielded a mean score of 1.00, confirming components function as intended. User Acceptance Testing produced a mean score of 0.99, indicating the system meets end-user requirements. Stress Testing also achieved a mean score of 0.99, proving the system remains stable and responsive under load conditions. The study concludes that OptiCCS is a reliable and accepted solution capable of replacing the college’s manual methods with a centralized, efficient system that provides reliable real-time data for administrative decisions.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"The student should focus on the specific features of their capstone management system, such as AI plagiarism detection and secure student accounts, rather than attempting to incorporate laboratory management functionalities.\", \"archived_id\": 13, \"differences\": \"one manages computer and laboratory equipment, the other manages capstone projects\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"both are web-based systems for managing resources within a college setting\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 30, \"title\": \"CPAG: CULTURAL AND PERFORMING ARTS GROUP MANAGEMENT SYSTEM WITH INCENTIVE MONITORING FOR CAMARINES SUR POLYTECHNIC COLLEGES (CSPC)\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain and target users.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"Educational institutions face significant challenges in managing cultural and performing arts programs where manual processes lead to operational inefficiencies, data loss, and accountability issues. At Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges (CSPC), the Cultural Affairs Office struggled with paper-based member applications, unreliable attendance tracking, inconsistent performance evaluations, inadequate inventory management, and labor-intensive incentive computations, resulting in administrative delays and difficulty monitoring student participation. This study aimed to develop a web-based Cultural and Performing Arts Group Management System with Incentive Monitoring (CPAG) that automates core operations through eight integrated modules: User Management, Member Application, Attendance Monitoring, Inventory Management, Incentive Management, Notification and Messaging, Reports and Analytics, and Event Management. The system was developed using Agile Extreme Programming (XP) methodology with CodeIgniter 4 framework and MySQL database, integrating DigitalPersona U.are.U 4500 fingerprint scanners for biometric attendance. Black box testing was conducted with 582 respondents comprising student performers, applicants, trainers, officers, administrators, and IT experts. Results demonstrated exceptional performance: Unit Testing achieved 0.99 (Highly Functional), User Acceptance Testing scored 0.99 (Highly Acceptable), Usability Testing obtained 1.00 (Highly Usable), and Security Testing using OWASP ZAP v2.16.1 yielded 0.98 (Highly Secure). All modules met functional requirements with scores ranging from 0.98 to 1.00. The CPAG system successfully transformed cultural group management at CSPC by eliminating paperwork, ensuring accurate attendance tracking through fingerprint biometrics, automating transparent incentive distribution, and providing real-time data access. Future enhancements include mobile application development and SMS notification integration.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Focus on the specific features relevant to the target users of the capstone project management system, such as AI-based plagiarism detection and secure account management.\", \"archived_id\": 11, \"differences\": \"one is for students and advisers, the other is for cultural and performing arts group management.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"both focus on managing capstone projects.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 20, \"title\": \"WEB-BASED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR CSPC’S PRODUCTION AND AUXILIARY SERVICES WITH INVETORY AND SALES TRACKING\", \"reason\": \"The core concept of the archived document focuses on inventory and sales tracking for an institution\'s production and auxiliary services, while the pre-proposal is about a capstone project management system for a college of computer studies.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"In an institution like the Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges, where operational efficiency and controlled use of resources is required, manual processes within the Production and Auxiliary Services (PAxS) office created a critical bottleneck. This resulted in records supposedly prone to errors and a significant lack of real-time visibility in inventory and sales. The Web-Based Management System for CSPC Production and Auxiliary Services with Inventory and Sales Tracking thus emerges as a transformational solution to revolutionize basic PAxS operations. This new web-based system specifically provides the accuracy required by setting up automated and centralized tracking of sales, inventory, and vehicle pass applications, thus improving overall accountability and administrative control. Automating these key workflows substantially reduces the administrative load on personnel and significantly increases the quality and expedience of service delivery. Developed using the Agile Scrum Methodology, the iterative, user-friendly process ensured the final system architecture—includin g User Account Management, User Ordering, Digital Vehicle Pass Application, Integrated Sales and Inventory Tracking, Payment Processing, and Comprehensive Report Generation modules—met all stakeholder requirements. To determine the system\'s quality and institutional readiness, comprehensive black-box testing was conducted in three important dimensions. The strict quantitative findings reveal the system to be viable: Functional Testing scored an outstanding 0.97 (High Functionality), proving all modules acted as per specifications. Performance Testing scored 0.88 (High Performance), indicating system stability and efficiency under full transaction load. Security Testing yielded 0.89 (Low Risk), which confirms strong controls were established to keep sensitive institutional information safe. The study\'s aims were achieved with the development of this web-based system, which provides PAxS with a stable, productive, and secure solution that significantly improves accountability, increases operational speed, and enables data-driven decision-making, making the platform applicable for large-scale institutional adoption.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"The student should focus on refining the scope of the capstone project management system to include more specific features such as AI-based plagiarism detection and workflow optimization.\", \"archived_id\": 2, \"differences\": \"The archived document addresses inventory and sales tracking, while the pre-proposal focuses on capstone project management.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both involve web-based systems for managing processes related to academic or operational tasks.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}]', '[]', '2026-09-08 02:01:36', '2026-09-08 02:01:36');
INSERT INTO `duplication_checks` (`id`, `student_s_y_id`, `document_path`, `concepts`, `top_score`, `verdict`, `matches`, `instructors_suggested`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(2, 2, 'duplication-checks/4empFBtStQSeznQKkkn2QwELZPmo9r0fReLi7nMk.pdf', '{\"sdm\": \"Agile Development Methodology\", \"scope\": \"The proposed web system will focus exclusively on capstone-related activities within CSPC–CCS, centralizing all processes to improve workflow efficiency and maintain academic integrity.\", \"title\": \"CapsSys: Web-based Capstone Management System for CSPC CCS\", \"domain\": \"Web System\", \"keywords\": [\"web-based\", \"capstone management\", \"CSPC CCS\", \"quality education\", \"AI plagiarism detection\", \"agile development\"], \"sdg_goals\": \"SDG 4 – Quality Education\", \"main_topic\": \"Developing a web-based system for managing capstone projects at CSPC CCS\", \"limitations\": \"The system is limited to CSPC–CCS capstone projects only; duplication checking is restricted to archived prior studies and stored capstone outputs; internet access is required for the system to function; grading, evaluation, and final decisions remain the responsibility of instructors; the platform does not replace official academic record systems.\", \"target_users\": \"Students and instructors at CSPC CCS\", \"technologies\": [\"web-based\", \"AI plagiarism detection\", \"secure accounts\", \"online submission\"], \"research_agenda\": [\"Technology Development and Innovation\", \"e-Services\", \"Educational Management\", \"Applications and Systems Development\"], \"problem_statement\": \"The College of Computer Studies (CCS) of CSPC currently lacks a centralized web-based system for managing capstone projects, leading to inefficiencies, miscommunication, delayed outputs, and potential academic integrity issues.\", \"proposed_solution\": \"Develop a web-based capstone management system for CSPC–CCS, providing secure accounts for both students and instructors, allowing them to apply for advisers, consultants, and grammarians, submit capstone outputs online, review and annotate submissions, manage schedules, track progress, and perform duplication checks with AI.\"}', 40, 'Passed', '[{\"score\": 40, \"title\": \"CAPSTONE PROJECT AND THESIS CLASS INFORMATIONMAN AGEMENT SYSTEM\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on managing capstone projects but differ in specific features and scope.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"Capstone projects have become a crucial part of a student\'s education in the modern world, laying the foundation for further learning. It gives students the capacity to retain the information they learned during college studies and use it when want to pursue a certain academic path in college. Paper-based solutions lack flexibility in handling evaluations, are less effective at gathering data, and are challenging to access when communicating information about a Capstone Project. Students were unable to obtain assessments that they required to make changes as a result, which delayed the encoding of grades. In general, the objective is to develop a system that were automate the process of Capstone Project and Thesis Class Information with Deliverables Monitoring, Participation Rating, Oral Examination Scheduling, Oral Examination Rating, and Honorarium Computation. To address the objectives of the study, the researcher used a mixed-method research design and an Extreme programming model. The study respondents were the Capstone Subject Adviser, Thesis Subject Adviser, Panelist, and Capstone Students of the Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges. The data was obtained using interviews, and surveys, and the data was evaluated using a weighted mean and percentage. The research findings indicate that there are problems with manually rating the paper of students, having trouble creating reports, and sharing the data. Thus, the overall interpretation revealed that the suggested system is moderately acceptable to the respondents. As a result, the developed system Capstone Project and Thesis Class Information Management System (CAPTCIMS) still needs further development for improvement.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Consider adding AI features or improving the grading and participation rating system to differentiate your proposal further.\", \"archived_id\": 57, \"differences\": \"CapsSys focuses on AI plagiarism detection and agile development, while the archived document emphasizes grading and honorarium computation.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"both manage capstone projects for students and faculty\", \"academic_year\": \"2022\"}, {\"score\": 34, \"title\": \"CHRONOLOCK: AN INTEGRATION OF WEB-BASED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR THE SMART DOOR LOCK SYSTEM OF CCS ERP LABORATORY\", \"reason\": \"Semantically similar based on vector embedding analysis.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"This study addresses the challenges faced in the ERP Laboratory of the College of Computer Studies, including an unsecured access control system, inefficient attendance monitoring, inflexible scheduling, and inefficient laboratory security monitoring. To enhance laboratory management, a web-based management system was developed utilizing Lean Agile methodology alongside a mixed-method research approach that combined both quantitative and qualitative data. Total enumeration sampling was employed to select respondents for the study. The evaluation of the system\'s functionality and performance involved black box testing, with unit testing conducted in collaboration with end users, including students, faculty, laboratory personnel, and administrative staff. IT experts performed integration, load, and stress testing to assess the system\'s capabilities. The arithmetic mean was employed to assess the gathered data. Load testing demonstrated strong performance, with an error rate of 0.00% across various workload conditions. Unit, stress, and integration testing each achieved a perfect score of 1.00, confirming the system\'s compliance with requirements, efficiency under high loads, and seamless component integration. The results indicate that the newly developed web-based management system is ready to significantly improve convenience and overall management in the CCS ERP Laboratory.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 92, \"differences\": \"\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"\", \"academic_year\": \"2024\"}, {\"score\": 34, \"title\": \"ESCHOLAR: A COMPREHENSIVE WEB-BASED SCHOLARSHIP APPLICATION PORTAL CONNECTING GOVERNMENT AND STUDENTS\", \"reason\": \"Semantically similar based on vector embedding analysis.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The eScholar Web-Based Scholarship Application Portal is an online portal was created to address the challenges in government scholarship procedure. The main objective of the study is to develop a centralized system that allows students to find scholarships at ease, can submit applications through online, and also allowed them to track their application progress, while on the other hand, administrators and government officials managed the posting management, application assessment and communication that allowed students to be informed. The study used a mixed method approach that combined qualitative interview methods with quantitative survey data and system evaluation results to develop and evaluate the system. The system development used agile methodologies that followed a structure based on data flow diagrams, entity relationship diagrams, and modular functional components. The equivalent partition testing with the use of Puppeteer simulation tool, it showed that all essential system modules worked correctly without discovering any system failures. The User acceptance testing produced a mean rating of 4.51 that showed that the system achieved high levels of usability, simplicity, and usefulness. The evaluation instrument showed high reliability because its Cronbach’s alpha score reached 0.98 which indicates excellent internal consistency. The system maintained a stable performance during stress testing that involved with multiple simulated users at once and security testing proved that the system protected against typical high security threats.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 27, \"differences\": \"\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 34, \"title\": \"EDUCONNECT: A SMART WEB-BASED ACADEMIC MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR STA. JUSTINA NATIONAL HIGH SCHOOL\", \"reason\": \"Semantically similar based on vector embedding analysis.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"Academic management in secondary schools have to deal with manual and semi-digital processes. These processes lead to inefficiencies, inaccuracies in data, and a lack of communication among stakeholders. This is the case with Sta. Justina National High School (SJNHS), where traditional methods dominate operations. This paper contributes to the field by proposing EduConnect: A Smart Web-Based Academic Management System. EduConnect is designed to automate and streamline the central processes and pent processes of academics and administration. These include enrollment, attendance, grade tracking, scheduling, announcements, and reporting. EduConnect provides role-based access to students, teachers, administrators, and parents. The system is built on a technical stack that includes CodeIgniter 4, PHP, JavaScript, MySQL, HTML 5, and Bootstrap. The system was built using the Agile Software Development Methodology. This is a process that allows for incremental development and refinement based on user feedback. Existing academic workflows were analyzed to identify gaps and difficulty in record keeping, accessibility of information, and communication. EduConnect was assessed using Black Box Testing to meet the requirements of the ISO 25010 software quality model. Use case testing and requirement-based testing scored 0.99 while usability testing was 0.99 and compatibility testing was 1.00 . According to the Nikto Docker security test, EduConnect has proper data and access control along with good security configurations. EduConnect has no critical or high security risks. The third-party findings were also non-impacting. With performance testing using Apache JMeter, the findings show concurrent users, given all 1,809 requests finished with 0 errors, took reasonable time to respond, and recorded 5.20 transactions per second, on average. Overall, EduConnect passed all tests confirming it is operational, user oriented, safe, efficient, and dependable, thereby greatly improving SJNHS’ academic management.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 32, \"differences\": \"\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 34, \"title\": \"CBSTrac: A Web-Based Alumni Tracking System for Central Bicol State University of Agriculture\", \"reason\": \"Semantically similar based on vector embedding analysis.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"Fragmented alumni records, low participation, and the lack of automated reporting are among the current problems that the Alumni Office of Central Bicol State University of Agriculture (CBSUA) face. This paper introduces CBSTrac, a web-based alumni tracking system for the Central Bicol State University of Agriculture in response to the identified problems. The system includes key features such as alumni onboarding with masterlist cross-checking, profile management, tracer survey, QR code event attendance, job posting using APIs for scraping and fetching, donation tracking, internal messaging, and analytics-based reporting. The researchers found that CBSTrac has the potential to create a centralized place for all alumni employment, involvement and participation information in a near real-time environment with ease of access, organization and analysis. From the results of our black box testing, CBSTrac was rated highly. The Functionality score was (3.77), Usability (3.83), Compatibility Score (3.77), Security Score (3.87), and Performance Score (3.77) giving the overall score of (3.80) which was interpreted as Excellent. The results demonstrated that the CBSTrac is . The findings from this study supported that CBSTrac met its purpose by providing a secure and efficient means of using data, improving the accuracy of data, automating many administrative processes, and enhancing alumni participation and tracking. Additionally, this study lays the foundation for future enhancements that may also explore the implementation of advanced predictive modeling and machine learning to forecast employment trends and further align the university curriculum with evolving industry needs.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 51, \"differences\": \"\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 34, \"title\": \"CCS Faculty Lounge Smart Door Lock with Web Based Access Log and Class Sched- ule Viewing System\", \"reason\": \"Semantically similar based on vector embedding analysis.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The Smart Door Lock System integrates RFID and fingerprint authentication with a web-based access log and class schedule viewing functionality to enhance security and scheduling efficiency for educational institutions. This system addresses the limitations of traditional access control and scheduling methods, which are prone to unauthorized entry, human error, and inefficient scheduling processes. By ensuring only authorized students, instructors, and admins can access secured areas and view class schedules, the system offers improved reliability and transparency. The access log component allows real-time entry/exit tracking, enhancing monitoring capabilities. The system was developed using the Agile methodology, allowing for iterative development, continuous feedback, and adaptive planning to meet evolving user needs. Data collection involved qualitative and quantitative methods, including interviews and surveys. The system underwent black-box testing to verify functionality, load, stress, and security performance. Surveys were distributed to 290 students, 23 instructors, and 2 IT experts, and 2 admins to assess system usability and effectiveness. The survey responses were analyzed using the Arithmetic Mean to ensure comprehensive feedback. Results showed a 95% function- ality rating, indicating high reliability and performance. The system’s effectiveness was validated through purposive and convenience sampling, ensuring that the solution met all user needs. Testing approaches such as functional, load, stress, and security testing confirmed the system’s dependability and security compliance. **Additionally, the system’s user- friendly interface contributed to its high usability rating, as participants reported ease of navigation. Future improvements may include integrating mobile notifications and AI-based analytics for enhanced security insights.**\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 104, \"differences\": \"\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"\", \"academic_year\": \"2024\"}, {\"score\": 34, \"title\": \"CHRONOLOCK: A MOBILE APPLICATION FOR INTERNET-ENABLE D ACCESS CONTROL OF THE CCS ERP LABORATORY SMART DOOR LOCK SYSTEM SPENSYS: WEB-BASED SOLUTIONS FOR ENROLLMENT AND ACADEMIC RECORDS WITH AI CHATBOT FOR NABUA NATIONAL HIGH SCHOOL\", \"reason\": \"Semantically similar based on vector embedding analysis.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The increasing demand for efficient and accurate school information systems highlights the need for digital solutions that streamline enrollment, scheduling, and academic records management. SPEnSys addresses this need by providing Nabua National High School with an integrated web-based platform capable of automating student registration, managing academic records, generating real-time reports, and offering 24/7 support through an AI chatbot named SPEnBot. The system centralizes academic and administrative processes, reduces manual encoding errors, enhances accessibility, and supports data-driven decision-making through analytics. This project aimed to evaluate and develop a fully functional digital solution that improves the institution’s workflow. Guided by the Extreme Programming (XP) methodology, the system underwent iterative development, continuous stakeholder involvement, and thorough testing. Data were gathered from administrators, teachers, students, and IT experts through surveys and multiple testing procedures. Black box testing, including unit testing, user acceptance testing, performance testing, and usability testing, was used to validate the system’s functionality. Results showed that SPEnSys achieved a “Highly Functional” rating across all testing phases, confirming its reliability, efficiency, and readiness for deployment. Overall, SPEnSys successfully addressed the challenges of Nabua National High School’s semi-manual processes by providing a centralized, secure, and user-friendly digital platform. The integration of the AI chatbot, cloud-based deployment, and role- based access control further positions the system as a modern, scalable solution capable of supporting future academic and administrative requirements.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 17, \"differences\": \"\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 30, \"title\": \"WEB-BASED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR CSPC’S PRODUCTION AND AUXILIARY SERVICES WITH INVETORY AND SALES TRACKING\", \"reason\": \"The core concept of managing capstone projects at CCS does not match the web-based management system for production and auxiliary services with inventory and sales tracking.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"In an institution like the Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges, where operational efficiency and controlled use of resources is required, manual processes within the Production and Auxiliary Services (PAxS) office created a critical bottleneck. This resulted in records supposedly prone to errors and a significant lack of real-time visibility in inventory and sales. The Web-Based Management System for CSPC Production and Auxiliary Services with Inventory and Sales Tracking thus emerges as a transformational solution to revolutionize basic PAxS operations. This new web-based system specifically provides the accuracy required by setting up automated and centralized tracking of sales, inventory, and vehicle pass applications, thus improving overall accountability and administrative control. Automating these key workflows substantially reduces the administrative load on personnel and significantly increases the quality and expedience of service delivery. Developed using the Agile Scrum Methodology, the iterative, user-friendly process ensured the final system architecture—includin g User Account Management, User Ordering, Digital Vehicle Pass Application, Integrated Sales and Inventory Tracking, Payment Processing, and Comprehensive Report Generation modules—met all stakeholder requirements. To determine the system\'s quality and institutional readiness, comprehensive black-box testing was conducted in three important dimensions. The strict quantitative findings reveal the system to be viable: Functional Testing scored an outstanding 0.97 (High Functionality), proving all modules acted as per specifications. Performance Testing scored 0.88 (High Performance), indicating system stability and efficiency under full transaction load. Security Testing yielded 0.89 (Low Risk), which confirms strong controls were established to keep sensitive institutional information safe. The study\'s aims were achieved with the development of this web-based system, which provides PAxS with a stable, productive, and secure solution that significantly improves accountability, increases operational speed, and enables data-driven decision-making, making the platform applicable for large-scale institutional adoption.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Consider focusing on a specific area within the capstone management system, such as improving AI plagiarism detection or enhancing user account management.\", \"archived_id\": 2, \"differences\": \"one focuses on academic projects (capstone management) while the other manages operational resources (inventory and sales tracking)\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"both are web-based systems for managing institutional processes\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 30, \"title\": \"CPAG: CULTURAL AND PERFORMING ARTS GROUP MANAGEMENT SYSTEM WITH INCENTIVE MONITORING FOR CAMARINES SUR POLYTECHNIC COLLEGES (CSPC)\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain and target users.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"Educational institutions face significant challenges in managing cultural and performing arts programs where manual processes lead to operational inefficiencies, data loss, and accountability issues. At Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges (CSPC), the Cultural Affairs Office struggled with paper-based member applications, unreliable attendance tracking, inconsistent performance evaluations, inadequate inventory management, and labor-intensive incentive computations, resulting in administrative delays and difficulty monitoring student participation. This study aimed to develop a web-based Cultural and Performing Arts Group Management System with Incentive Monitoring (CPAG) that automates core operations through eight integrated modules: User Management, Member Application, Attendance Monitoring, Inventory Management, Incentive Management, Notification and Messaging, Reports and Analytics, and Event Management. The system was developed using Agile Extreme Programming (XP) methodology with CodeIgniter 4 framework and MySQL database, integrating DigitalPersona U.are.U 4500 fingerprint scanners for biometric attendance. Black box testing was conducted with 582 respondents comprising student performers, applicants, trainers, officers, administrators, and IT experts. Results demonstrated exceptional performance: Unit Testing achieved 0.99 (Highly Functional), User Acceptance Testing scored 0.99 (Highly Acceptable), Usability Testing obtained 1.00 (Highly Usable), and Security Testing using OWASP ZAP v2.16.1 yielded 0.98 (Highly Secure). All modules met functional requirements with scores ranging from 0.98 to 1.00. The CPAG system successfully transformed cultural group management at CSPC by eliminating paperwork, ensuring accurate attendance tracking through fingerprint biometrics, automating transparent incentive distribution, and providing real-time data access. Future enhancements include mobile application development and SMS notification integration.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Focus on the specific challenges of managing cultural and performing arts programs rather than just capstone projects.\", \"archived_id\": 11, \"differences\": \"One is for a specific college (CCS), the other is for a cultural and performing arts group.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both focus on managing capstone projects.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 30, \"title\": \"OptiCCS: AN INTEGRATED SYSTEM FOR MONITORING AND MANAGING COMPUTER AND LABORATORY EQUIPMENT FOR THE COLLEGE OF COMPUTER STUDIES\", \"reason\": \"The core concept of the archived document focuses on managing laboratory equipment, not capstone projects.\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The College of Computer Studies (CCS) at Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges struggles with inefficient paper-based laboratory management that lacks real-time monitoring for student activity and equipment. To address this, the researchers developed OptiCCS, an integrated web- based system for laboratory and equipment management. The system, built using Agile Scrum methodology, integrates a web application with a real-time monitoring application. The web application, developed on the CodeIgniter PHP framework with a MySQL database, manages inventory, class creation, role-based access, and report generation. The real-time monitoring service uses a Python client agent on each computer unit, connecting to a server built with React HTTP for API requests and the Ratchet WebSocket library for bi-directional communication, enabling live status reporting, screenshot feeds, violation detection, and remote command execution. The system uses Google OAuth for authentication. System validation involved black box testing for functionality, usability, and performance. Administrators, faculty, technicians, and students participated using a questionnaire, and the results were assessed based on the ISO 25010 software quality standard. Findings demonstrated a strong readiness for daily operation: Unit Testing yielded a mean score of 1.00, confirming components function as intended. User Acceptance Testing produced a mean score of 0.99, indicating the system meets end-user requirements. Stress Testing also achieved a mean score of 0.99, proving the system remains stable and responsive under load conditions. The study concludes that OptiCCS is a reliable and accepted solution capable of replacing the college’s manual methods with a centralized, efficient system that provides reliable real-time data for administrative decisions.\", \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"The student should focus on the specific features of their capstone management system, such as AI plagiarism detection and agile development, rather than diverting into laboratory management.\", \"archived_id\": 13, \"differences\": \"one manages laboratory equipment, the other manages capstone projects\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"both are web-based systems for managing educational resources\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}]', '[]', '2026-09-08 02:19:37', '2026-09-08 02:19:37');
INSERT INTO `duplication_checks` (`id`, `student_s_y_id`, `document_path`, `concepts`, `top_score`, `verdict`, `matches`, `instructors_suggested`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(16, 2, 'duplication-checks/tE3ETLRoeSS1qd8w502O7PhOWc2AHBIxk4LCmtH1.pdf', '{\"sdm\": \"Agile Development Methodology\", \"scope\": \"Project & Contract Management; Geospatial Mapping & Area Tracking; Timeline & Progress Monitoring; Automated Alerts; Comprehensive Reporting; Document Archiving; AI Intelligence Engine\", \"title\": \"PROJ-TRACK: An Integrated Monitoring and Automated Notification System for CSPC-PPFMS\", \"domain\": \"Web System\", \"keywords\": [\"PROJ-TRACK\", \"Integrated Monitoring\", \"Automated Notification\", \"CSPC\", \"PPFMS\", \"Geospatial Mapping\", \"Area Tracking\", \"AI Intelligence Engine\", \"Agile Development Methodology\"], \"sdg_goals\": \"SDG 9 – Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure; SDG 11 – Sustainable Cities and Communities; SDG 16 – Peace, Justice, and Strong Institutions\", \"main_topic\": \"Development of a web-based system for monitoring and automating notifications in project management for the CSPC Office of the Director - PPFMS\", \"limitations\": \"Connectivity; Data Entry; Integration; AI Accuracy; Geospatial Precision\", \"target_users\": \"Administrators of the CSPC Office of the Director - PPFMS\", \"technologies\": [\"Google Maps API\", \"AI Intelligence Engine\"], \"research_agenda\": [\"Process Automation\", \"Information Science\", \"Smart Computing\", \"Business Administration and Management\"], \"problem_statement\": \"The CSPC Office of the Director - PPFMS currently relies on manual, paper-based records to monitor infrastructure, leading to risks of lost documents and delayed reporting, and a lack of spatial visualization.\", \"proposed_solution\": \"The project proposes a web-based system that centralizes project records and provides automated notifications, integrating the Google Maps API for geospatial mapping and area tracking.\"}', 70, 'High Similarity', '[{\"score\": 70, \"title\": \"RESEARCH PROJECT INFORMATION MANAGEMENT AND TRACKING SYSTEM\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on managing research project information and tracking progress for an AI Research Center.\", \"authors\": \"China T. Bea, Louie B. Molina, Jessemri A. Tabayag\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"Through Research Project Information Management, the researchers come up with the idea to lessen the work in the AI Research Center for Community Development, or AIRCoDe, by managing and tracking the research project and its progress. Hence, this study aimed to develop a web-based system entitled “Research Project Information Management and Tracking System”, (RPIMTS) that help faculties and researchers in managing each research projects. The RPIMTS is paperless-based management system in which the researchers who are willing to propose new research can find it easier to apply their research. Applying for exploratory research, this study considered the data provided by the director, staff, researchers, and reviewers in the AIRCoDe. The researchers used stratified sampling techniques to gather data. The Blackbox testing for AIRCoDe’s system results reveal low vulnerability risk, excellent performance, and full functionality, with no detected errors. of the system. The researcher used the Extreme Programming (XP) phases for the development of the system, and by doing so, they created a great RPIMTS. By exploring the functionalities of the AIRCoDe, the researchers created a process flow that serves as a guide for every user that will use the system. After the development of the system, it undergoes testing, such as Use Case Testing, Performance Testing, and Security Testing, to show its level of functionality for use case testing, its level of vulnerability for security testing, and its level of response for performance testing. By those tests, it gives the results of passing those tests. The findings of this study may serve as a fundamental basis for the researchers to use the system in managing and tracking the research project and its progress.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 75, \"differences\": \"Scope of features differs slightly; one emphasizes web-based system, the other blackbox testing and extreme programming phases\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"Managing research projects, tracking progress\", \"academic_year\": \"2023\"}, {\"score\": 70, \"title\": \"OptiCCS: AN INTEGRATED SYSTEM FOR MONITORING AND MANAGING COMPUTER AND LABORATORY EQUIPMENT FOR THE COLLEGE OF COMPUTER STUDIES\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on integrated monitoring and automated notification systems for managing equipment or records.\", \"authors\": \"Jan Andrew R Barte, Novie Heralyn B. Placides, Reymelene E. Valera\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The College of Computer Studies (CCS) at Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges struggles with inefficient paper-based laboratory management that lacks real-time monitoring for student activity and equipment. To address this, the researchers developed OptiCCS, an integrated web- based system for laboratory and equipment management. The system, built using Agile Scrum methodology, integrates a web application with a real-time monitoring application. The web application, developed on the CodeIgniter PHP framework with a MySQL database, manages inventory, class creation, role-based access, and report generation. The real-time monitoring service uses a Python client agent on each computer unit, connecting to a server built with React HTTP for API requests and the Ratchet WebSocket library for bi-directional communication, enabling live status reporting, screenshot feeds, violation detection, and remote command execution. The system uses Google OAuth for authentication. System validation involved black box testing for functionality, usability, and performance. Administrators, faculty, technicians, and students participated using a questionnaire, and the results were assessed based on the ISO 25010 software quality standard. Findings demonstrated a strong readiness for daily operation: Unit Testing yielded a mean score of 1.00, confirming components function as intended. User Acceptance Testing produced a mean score of 0.99, indicating the system meets end-user requirements. Stress Testing also achieved a mean score of 0.99, proving the system remains stable and responsive under load conditions. The study concludes that OptiCCS is a reliable and accepted solution capable of replacing the college’s manual methods with a centralized, efficient system that provides reliable real-time data for administrative decisions.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 13, \"differences\": \"Specific subjects (computer lab vs. project management) and users differ\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"Integrated monitoring, automated notifications\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 23, \"title\": \"GIS- INTEGRATED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR EVANGELICAL CEMETERY IN SANTIAGO, IRIGA CITY\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages project monitoring, the other cemetery records.\", \"authors\": \"John Rick L. Babila, Maria Lourdes S. Arcilla, John Mark David S. Pajenago\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The Evangelical Cemetery in Santiago, Iriga City had experienced disadvantages that come along with the traditional way of keeping records, inefficient plot tracking, and limited access to burial information which led to data inaccuracies and service delays. In an attempt to solve the problem, a GIS-Integrated Management System was launched that would be helpful in the modernization of cemetery operations while also taking into consideration the local cultural and religious practices. The aim of the research was to devise, create a web-based system that includes functions for managing burial records, allocating and tracking plots, managing deceased profiles, providing notification services, and visualization of plots based on GIS technology. A black-box testing approach was taken to evaluate the system, wherein different testing methods like functional, integration, security, compatibility, and usability were applied. The total average score of 0.99 was achieved for both functional and integration testing, where integration got the highest rating of 1.00 meaning there was 100% module interaction. Secured, compatible, and usability testing then reported their average scores of 4.50, 4.46, and 4.48, respectively, which were all seen as Highly Functional. It can thus be concluded that the system is able to significantly enhance efficiency, accuracy, data security, and accessibility. Overall, the research work establishes the claim that GIS and web technologies can be easily and effectively combined to create a record management system and service delivery solution that works in a local context.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define your specific problem and target users to avoid overlap with the archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 48, \"differences\": \"One focuses on project workflow; the other on burial information and access control.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage records for modernization\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 20, \"title\": \"ELEVATEGS: A PROGRESSIVE WEB APPLICATION LEARNING MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR GRADUATE SCHOOL OF USANT\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages project monitoring and notifications, the other learning management system.\", \"authors\": \"Kristhan B. Aguilar, Lenard Anthony A. Gaa, Lyle Mathew S. Ramales\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"This study developed ElevateGS a Progressive Web Application (PWA) Learning Management System, to address critical operational inefficiencies at the University of Saint Anthony (USANT) Graduate School, specifically the heavy reliance on manual grading, decentralized announcement channels, and scattered course management that complicates resource retrieval. Utilizing the Adapted Agile Scrum Framework, the system features a decoupled architecture with a PHP Laravel backend and Vue.js frontend, incorporating Service Workers and IndexedDB to enable offline synchronization and centralize academic materials. A mixed-method evaluation involving 60 respondents including faculty, students, and IT experts revealed that the system is \\\"Highly Functional\\\" (composite mean of 0.99), with a 100% success rate for offline capabilities. Usability was rated as \\\"High\\\" (weighted mean of 3.82) and user satisfaction as \\\"Good\\\" (System Usability Scale score of 78.76), confirming that ElevateGS successfully bridges the gap between fragmented, manual processes and digital demands by providing a centralized, and offline- capable platform for the graduate school.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define the unique problem being solved and target users for each system.\", \"archived_id\": 19, \"differences\": \"Different specific features (project vs. learning management) and target users (students/advisers vs. faculty, IT experts)\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage centralization of records/notifications\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 20, \"title\": \"WEB-BASED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR CSPC’S PRODUCTION AND AUXILIARY SERVICES WITH INVETORY AND SALES TRACKING\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages project monitoring for infrastructure, the other manages inventory and sales for an office.\", \"authors\": \"Jancee Kenn E. Abonita, Kathleen Tess I. Hugo, Julian Paul M. Padua\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"In an institution like the Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges, where operational efficiency and controlled use of resources is required, manual processes within the Production and Auxiliary Services (PAxS) office created a critical bottleneck. This resulted in records supposedly prone to errors and a significant lack of real-time visibility in inventory and sales. The Web-Based Management System for CSPC Production and Auxiliary Services with Inventory and Sales Tracking thus emerges as a transformational solution to revolutionize basic PAxS operations. This new web-based system specifically provides the accuracy required by setting up automated and centralized tracking of sales, inventory, and vehicle pass applications, thus improving overall accountability and administrative control. Automating these key workflows substantially reduces the administrative load on personnel and significantly increases the quality and expedience of service delivery. Developed using the Agile Scrum Methodology, the iterative, user-friendly process ensured the final system architecture—includin g User Account Management, User Ordering, Digital Vehicle Pass Application, Integrated Sales and Inventory Tracking, Payment Processing, and Comprehensive Report Generation modules—met all stakeholder requirements. To determine the system\'s quality and institutional readiness, comprehensive black-box testing was conducted in three important dimensions. The strict quantitative findings reveal the system to be viable: Functional Testing scored an outstanding 0.97 (High Functionality), proving all modules acted as per specifications. Performance Testing scored 0.88 (High Performance), indicating system stability and efficiency under full transaction load. Security Testing yielded 0.89 (Low Risk), which confirms strong controls were established to keep sensitive institutional information safe. The study\'s aims were achieved with the development of this web-based system, which provides PAxS with a stable, productive, and secure solution that significantly improves accountability, increases operational speed, and enables data-driven decision-making, making the platform applicable for large-scale institutional adoption.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define the specific scope and target users for each system to avoid overlap.\", \"archived_id\": 2, \"differences\": \"One focuses on infrastructure monitoring; the other on inventory and sales.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage resource tracking.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 20, \"title\": \"WEB-BASED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM WITH SMS NOTIFICATION FOR BULA MUNICIPAL WATERWORKS\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages project monitoring for infrastructure, the other municipal waterworks operations.\", \"authors\": \"Jahara P. Cervas, Jerl D. Illanza, Cyril Mae L. Pandes\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"In Water utility services, effective operations are crucial to provide the consumers with good services. However, traditional methods of record management and information delivery may affect the timeliness and accuracy of daily operations. To address these, this study focused on developing a Web-Based Management System with SMS Notification to enhance the processes in Bula Municipal Waterworks System (BMWS), which currently serves over 3,000 consumers from 22 barangays. The web-based platform includes several key features, such as consumer management, bill generation, meter reading, consumer support, SMS notification, and reports generation, designed to ensure that billing cycles, service updates, and information control and retrieval are secure, timely and accurate. To guarantee a continuous improvement throughout the system development, the Agile Scrum framework was utilized, allowing flexibility in handling requirements. To evaluate the system, black box testing was conducted to assess both the functional and non-functional aspects of the system, particularly focusing on the functionality, complete workflow, performance, and security. The functionality tests using test cases and end-to-end tests using Selenium IDE showed perfect 1.0 scores, performance achieved 0. 85 (Good Performance) in a load test with Apache JMeter, and security scans using OWASP ZAP found no high risks out of the total 12 findings. The test results reflect the system\'s capability in handling management operations and speeding up processes, which will significantly decrease the workloads of the staff, while gaining consumer trust through transparency. Currently implemented at BMWS, the system helps the local water service transform in terms of modernization, paving the way for future improvements in scalability and community engagement.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define the specific scope and target users for each system to avoid overlap.\", \"archived_id\": 5, \"differences\": \"One focuses on project monitoring; the other on municipal waterworks management.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage operational processes with web-based systems.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 16, \"title\": \"CPAG: CULTURAL AND PERFORMING ARTS GROUP MANAGEMENT SYSTEM WITH INCENTIVE MONITORING FOR CAMARINES SUR POLYTECHNIC COLLEGES (CSPC)\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages project monitoring and notifications, the other cultural arts group management.\", \"authors\": \"Jason F. Balingasa, Jeorge N. Fabillar, Leslie C. Llaban, Renier John L. Vargas\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"Educational institutions face significant challenges in managing cultural and performing arts programs where manual processes lead to operational inefficiencies, data loss, and accountability issues. At Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges (CSPC), the Cultural Affairs Office struggled with paper-based member applications, unreliable attendance tracking, inconsistent performance evaluations, inadequate inventory management, and labor-intensive incentive computations, resulting in administrative delays and difficulty monitoring student participation. This study aimed to develop a web-based Cultural and Performing Arts Group Management System with Incentive Monitoring (CPAG) that automates core operations through eight integrated modules: User Management, Member Application, Attendance Monitoring, Inventory Management, Incentive Management, Notification and Messaging, Reports and Analytics, and Event Management. The system was developed using Agile Extreme Programming (XP) methodology with CodeIgniter 4 framework and MySQL database, integrating DigitalPersona U.are.U 4500 fingerprint scanners for biometric attendance. Black box testing was conducted with 582 respondents comprising student performers, applicants, trainers, officers, administrators, and IT experts. Results demonstrated exceptional performance: Unit Testing achieved 0.99 (Highly Functional), User Acceptance Testing scored 0.99 (Highly Acceptable), Usability Testing obtained 1.00 (Highly Usable), and Security Testing using OWASP ZAP v2.16.1 yielded 0.98 (Highly Secure). All modules met functional requirements with scores ranging from 0.98 to 1.00. The CPAG system successfully transformed cultural group management at CSPC by eliminating paperwork, ensuring accurate attendance tracking through fingerprint biometrics, automating transparent incentive distribution, and providing real-time data access. Future enhancements include mobile application development and SMS notification integration.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define the specific scope and target users for each system to avoid overlap.\", \"archived_id\": 11, \"differences\": \"One focuses on project monitoring for infrastructure, the other on cultural arts programs.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage group activities and member tracking.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 15, \"title\": \"IBARYO: GOVERNANCE AUTOMATED AND KPI MONITORING SYSTEM FOR PALOYON ORIENTAL, NABUA, CAMARINES SUR\", \"reason\": \"Different core domains: one manages project monitoring and notifications, the other governance and KPI monitoring.\", \"authors\": \"Roland Joseph P. Cordez, Rayven Fran M. Toralde, Judah Paulo L. Viñas\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"This study developed iBaryo, a web-based governance system designed to help Barangay Paloyon Oriental manage tasks and services more efficiently. Before the system, the barangay relied on manual paperwork that caused delays, missing records, and difficulty in tracking responsibilities and officials’ performance. With iBaryo, barangay operations are centralized in one platform, including role-based task assignments, online document requests, complaint submissions, event scheduling, census records, real-time notifications, and analytics for monitoring performance. It also uses Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) to check how well officials complete their tasks and respond to residents. The system was created using the Agile method and tested for functionality, usability, efficiency, and security, and results showed that it works well, is easy to use, fast, and secure. Overall, iBaryo makes barangay management more organized, transparent, and convenient for both officials and residents, while reducing paperwork and improving accountability. Future upgrades may include national database integration, predictive features, and a mobile app for better accessibility.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define the specific scope and users for your system to avoid overlap with this archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 24, \"differences\": \"One focuses on project management (PROJ-TRACK) and the other on governance (iBaryo).\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage automated systems for task tracking and reporting.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 15, \"title\": \"BJMP (Bureau of Jail Management and Penology) Record Management System with Electronic Head Counting\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one is a web-based system for project monitoring and notifications, the other is an electronic record management system for inmates.\", \"authors\": \"Angelito M. Arsenal Jr., Mary Grace R. Dilla, Lawrence G. Ramos\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"In today\'s landscape, technology is pivotal, reshaping how we interact, work, and navigate our world. A streamlined Record Management System is vital for organized, accessible, and meticulous record-keeping, promoting accountability and informed decision-making. This study focuses on automating record management for Persons Deprived of Liberty (PDLs), ensuring accurate tracking. Using a Mixed-method approach, Iriga City District Jails Officers were interviewed for data collection, which underwent arithmetic mean analysis. Black box testing showed use case and requirement-based testing achieving a Completely Functional level with a 100 overall average. The application significantly addresses challenges in manual recording and counting of PDLs, justifying the BJMP Record Management System with Electronic Head Counting implementation. This system revolutionizes inmate record-keeping, ensuring accuracy and efficiency. It streamlines data entry, facilitates seamless retrieval and analysis, aiding decision-making and resource allocation. This technological advancement enhances correctional facility operations, showcasing BJMP\'s commitment to modernizing record management, fostering transparency, accountability, and optimal resource utilization.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define the specific users and purpose of your system to avoid overlap with this archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 89, \"differences\": \"One focuses on project workflow and AI intelligence; the other on inmate tracking and resource allocation.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage records digitally.\", \"academic_year\": \"2024\"}, {\"score\": 12, \"title\": \"BATO FARMLAND GEOLOCATION AND MAPPING SYSTEM\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages project monitoring and notifications, the other maps farmland\", \"authors\": \"Junel R. Joven, Julius M. Zaballa, Fernando P. Pasadilla\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The \\\"Bato Farmland Geolocation and Mapping System\\\" is a functional and user-friendly system when it comes to management and land mapping. This addresses the issues associated with manual recording and tracking of registered and insured farmers specifically in the Municipality of Bato. The system, which was specifically built for the Municipal Agriculture Office of Bato, aims to enhance efficiency, and reduce errors in farmers\' registration and tracking of farmland. It is primarily aimed at the office admin and staff that provides real-time monitoring and tracking of every farmland of registered farmers. The system provides accurate data on the location of the land area that serves as a guide to staff during the field visit for data collection. To ensure the level of functionality of the system, the system undergoes several test methods using black-box testing, where the use case and requirement-based testing were applied. The geolocation and mapping solution, developed in response to recognized concerns with manual tracking, of the registered farm and eliminates the need for manual data entry, offering a more efficient digital interface for users. The results of use case testing show a high degree of functionality, with an average mean of 0.98 (Highly Functional). Requirements-based testing confirms its efficacy, with a mean score of 0.98 (Highly Functional). The system\'s performance and alignment with objectives are supported by Local Government of Bato, input from administrators, and staff. “Bato Farmland Geolocation and Mapping System \\\" is set to transform municipal agricultural office administration by offering efficiency, accuracy and user-friendly system.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define your system\'s core purpose and target users to avoid confusion with unrelated projects.\", \"archived_id\": 72, \"differences\": \"Different subjects (project management vs. land mapping) and users\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"No genuine overlap beyond generic wording\", \"academic_year\": \"2023\"}]', '[{\"id\": 92, \"name\": \"Mark Balilla, MIT\", \"role\": \"adviser\", \"reason\": \"Expertise in Data Analytics and Web Development aligns with the development of a web-based system for monitoring and automating notifications.\", \"expertise\": \"Data Analytics, Research Methodology, Web Development\", \"role_label\": \"Adviser\"}, {\"id\": 101, \"name\": \"Kenn Aurillas\", \"role\": \"adviser\", \"reason\": \"Expertise in Research Methodology and Web Development is relevant to the development of a web-based system for project management.\", \"expertise\": \"Research Methodology, Quantitative Research, Mobile Apps, Web Development\", \"role_label\": \"Adviser\"}, {\"id\": 106, \"name\": \"Ian Cyrus S. Tumambing\", \"role\": \"adviser\", \"reason\": \"Expertise in Data Gathering & Instruments, Statistical Analysis, and Research Methodology is suitable for the development of a web-based system for monitoring infrastructure.\", \"expertise\": \"Data Gathering & Instruments, Statistical Analysis, Qualitative Research, Quantitative Research, Research Methodology, Survey Design, Literature Review, Research Ethics\", \"role_label\": \"Adviser\"}, {\"id\": 103, \"name\": \"Ian Tumambing\", \"role\": \"consultant\", \"reason\": \"Expertise in System Analysis & Design, Software Testing/ QA, Database Systems, API Development, Desktop Applications, Mobile Apps, Web Development, UI/UX Design aligns with the need for a web-based system development.\", \"expertise\": \"System Analysis & Design, Software Testing / QA, Database Systems, API Development, Desktop Applications, Mobile Apps, Web Development, UI/UX Design\", \"role_label\": \"Consultant\"}, {\"id\": 92, \"name\": \"Mark Balilla, MIT\", \"role\": \"consultant\", \"reason\": \"Expertise in Data Analytics and Web Development can be leveraged for the AI Intelligence Engine and automated notification functionalities.\", \"expertise\": \"Data Analytics, Research Methodology, Web Development\", \"role_label\": \"Consultant\"}, {\"id\": 101, \"name\": \"Kenn Aurillas\", \"role\": \"consultant\", \"reason\": \"Expertise in Research Methodology and Web Development can support the development of the web-based system for monitoring and automating notifications.\", \"expertise\": \"Research Methodology, Quantitative Research, Mobile Apps, Web Development\", \"role_label\": \"Consultant\"}]', '2026-09-15 00:26:02', '2026-09-15 00:26:02');
INSERT INTO `duplication_checks` (`id`, `student_s_y_id`, `document_path`, `concepts`, `top_score`, `verdict`, `matches`, `instructors_suggested`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(17, 1, 'duplication-checks/UY9hQ29aQlt5YISlbAU5v60VY68Gr7zKlVEieUoH.pdf', '{\"sdm\": \"Agile Development Methodology\", \"scope\": \"The system will include modules for patient records management (maternal & child health), medicine inventory management, expiring medicine notification system, low-Stock alerts and inventory reports, medicine issuance and usage tracking, user account management (admin, midwife, staff), data search, filtering, and report generation.\", \"title\": \"MediTrack-MCH: A Digital Inventory and Patient Records Management System for a Lying-In Clinic\", \"domain\": \"Management System\", \"keywords\": [\"MediTrack-MCH\", \"digital inventory\", \"patient records\", \"lying-in clinic\", \"medicine management\", \"web-based system\", \"Agile Development Methodology\"], \"sdg_goals\": \"SDG 3 – Good Health and Well-Being; SDG 9 – Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure; SDG 16 – Peace, Justice, and Strong Institutions\", \"main_topic\": \"Development of a web-based system for managing patient records and medicine inventory in a Lying-In Clinic\", \"limitations\": \"The system requires internet or local network connectivity; existing paper records must be manually encoded during initial implementation; the system is designed specifically for the Lying-In Clinic and does not cover hospital-wide integration.\", \"target_users\": \"Lying-In Clinic staff, including admin, midwives, and staff\", \"technologies\": [\"web-based system\", \"medicine management\", \"user account management\", \"data search\", \"report generation\"], \"research_agenda\": [\"Health Technologies\", \"Information Science\", \"Process Automation\", \"Smart Computing\"], \"problem_statement\": \"The current manual, paper-based records for managing patient information and medicine inventory increase the risk of lost, damaged, or incomplete records, inaccurate stock monitoring, and delayed identification of expired or low-stock medicines.\", \"proposed_solution\": \"The project proposes the development of a web-based Integrated Patient Records and Medicine Inventory System for the Lying-In Clinic, including modules for patient records management, medicine inventory monitoring, expiring medicine notifications, low-Stock alerts, and user account management.\"}', 75, 'High Similarity', '[{\"score\": 75, \"title\": \"MEDICARE: A WEB-BASED MEDICAL INVENTORY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM WITH DATA ANALYTICS\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on digitalizing medical inventory and patient records management for healthcare facilities.\", \"authors\": \"Arjay B. Bascon, Ma. Angela Janelle D.P., Jeremy L. Siguenza\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The healthcare industry relies on effective inventory management to balance patient needs with resource availability. This project aimed to developed Web-Based Medical Inventory Management System for the Medical Mission Group Hospital and Health Services Cooperative of Camarines Sur by automating, optimizing manual processes, and utilizing data analytics. Black box testing and Scrum Methodology were used, and surveys and interviews were conducted with IT experts, supply officers, medical staff, pharmacists, and cashiers. The MediCare system, which includes the Medical Inventory Management System and Patient Data Management System, was developed in collaboration with Team Aries, ensuring efficient hospital operations.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 78, \"differences\": \"Scope: MediTrack-MCH covers patient records and medicine inventory; MEDICARE focuses on data analytics. Users: MediTrack-MCH targets a lying-in clinic; MEDICARE targets a hospital. Specific features: MediTrack-MCH includes modules for patient records management, medicine inventory monitoring, expiring medicine notifications, low-Stock alerts, and user account management; MEDICARE emphasizes data analytics such as surveys and interviews conducted with IT experts, supply officers, medical staff, pharmacists, and cashiers.\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"Digitalization of medical inventory and patient records\", \"academic_year\": \"2023\"}, {\"score\": 75, \"title\": \"MEDICAL APPOINTMENT AND RECORD MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR NABUA RURAL HEALTH UNIT II\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on managing patient records and medicine inventory for a health unit, targeting the same users (physician and medical staff).\", \"authors\": \"ERJHON A. BALDOZA, CRIZEL B. DOMAGSANG, MA. HANNA N. HERNANDEZ, JOSHUA T. NILO\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The use of computer technology in several online transactions in medical facilities has made various operations and transactions fast and easy. The traditional way of setting appointments and managing records may result in heavy workloads and record loss. With these, this study was conducted to develop a system that will easily schedule appointments for patients with SMS notifications and manage records in RHU II. Generally, this study targets to develop a medical appointment and record management system to shift from the manual process of scheduling to online scheduling and managing patient records in RHU II. This study used a mixed-method research design to contextualize the data thematically and statistically. The respondents of this study were the physician and medical staff of the RHU II. Further, the system only covers the check-up and animal bite. In gathering the data, an interview, observation, and burp suite tool were used. The data gathered were analyzed and interpreted using thematic analysis and weighted mean. Based on analysis of the gathered data, in determining problems encountered in the scheduling process, record management, and data retrieval, researchers identified problems such as time-consuming in managing records, scheduling, and difficulty in retrieving data. Further, upon evaluation of the security performance of the system, it reveals that the system has a low severity with a weighted mean of 1.21 which can protect itself from XSS, SQL injection, and Session Hijacking. Therefore, the Medical Appointment and Record Management System is reasonable enough to be used in the RHU II.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clarify the specific features and scope of your system to avoid overlap with the archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 62, \"differences\": \"Scope differs slightly: one covers appointments and record management, the other only check-ups and animal bites.\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"Managing patient records and medicine inventory for RHU II.\", \"academic_year\": \"2022\"}, {\"score\": 75, \"title\": \"DEVELOPMENT OF MULTI-BRANCH DENTAL PRACTICE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM WITH POINT-OF-SALE AND BUSINESS ANALYTICS FOR DR. WENNIE A. SAMPER DENTAL CLINIC\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on digitalizing dental practice management with core modules including electronic records, appointment scheduling, and business analytics for a clinic setting.\", \"authors\": \"Janine R. Comploma, Alexander Edrian O. Sabroso, Ma. Crizel H. Tucay\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"This study presents the development of a comprehensive, web-based multi-branch dental practice management system designed to modernize the operations of Dr. Wennie A. Samper Dental Clinic by replacing inefficient, error-prone manual processes with an integrated digital solution. Developed using the Agile Scrum methodology, the system centralizes nine core modules including Electronic Medical Records, automated appointment scheduling, Point-of-Sale (POS) billing, and a business analytics dashboard to streamline cross-branch coordination and data-driven decision-making. Rigorous evaluation via black box, usability, performance, and security testing yielded perfect scores, confirming that the platform is highly functional and secure for immediate deployment. By automating administrative workflows and providing real-time operational insights, the system effectively eliminates documentation loss and billing conflicts while establishing a foundation for future enhancements such as teleconsultation and predictive analytics.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 16, \"differences\": \"Scope: One for patient records, the other for multi-branch operations; specific features differ slightly\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"Digitalization of dental practice management\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 75, \"title\": \"DRA. EULALIA ELGAR CLINIC MANAGEMENT SYSTEM\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on a digital management system for clinic operations.\", \"authors\": \"JONNABEL M. AWA, KHRYZ KYE B. BADIOLA, MA. LOURDES D. IBARRETA, ROCHEL F. TABERMEJO\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The emergence of technological advancements provided innovation in organizations to efficiently accomplished tasks. The idea is to eliminate the manual method of doing transactions manually, and saving time in the process of appointment. This study generally aims to develop a web-based Dra. Eulalia Elgar Clinic Management System for Espiritu-Elgar Medical Clinic, with these this study was conducted to develop appointment clinic management system that would systematically organize the appointment scheduling of patients/client, to manage user account, manage patient record, generate the report and generate the data analytics. This study used a mixed-methods research design that combines parts of quantitative and qualitative research to contextualize the data, therefore only the data gathered from the target respondents would be the only references for the development of the proposed system. After the collection of data through an interview with a guide questions, analysis was done using the frequency percentage and weighted mean. The iterative method was utilized throughout the study. On the system development, the result shows that the most frequently encountered problems in the clinic are the patient queue and the manual process of recording patients’ information. Furthermore, the evaluation of the performance of the system, the result shows 1 in level of functionality, and the respondents agree that the functionality of the develop system was excellent. The researchers concluded that clinic management system is necessary in managing clinical processes, the system development is effectively being done by following modules and phases of an Iterative Model, with the use of Black Box Testing. Based from a forementioned conclusions, researchers arrived with the following recommendations that future researchers conduct studies in other relevant research environments, consider document retrieval and document security consider and add billing statement in other related studies for further enhancement of the study.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 60, \"differences\": \"Specific clinic vs. general patient records; different scope of features\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"Digital clinic management system\", \"academic_year\": \"2022\"}, {\"score\": 75, \"title\": \"Queen Hannah Birthing Home Information Management System with SMS Notification\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on digitalizing patient record management for a birthing home setting.\", \"authors\": \"Janette M. Advincula, Rick Anthony R. Agullo, Fitzkirk John Paris P. Angeles, Jovin A. Ylagan\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"Birthing homes play a significant role in healthcare, serving as essential centers for maternal care. Many such facilities, including Queen Hannah Birthing Home, still rely on traditional paper-based processes, contrasting with the advancing landscape of healthcare technology. With these, this study was conducted aimed on digitizing the paper-based patient record system of Queen Hannah Birthing Home. Generally, this study identified the problems encountered in the manual processes of the birthing home, developed and implemented an efficient and effective web-based information management system that manage patient records electronically, update patient for check-up appointments through SMS Notification; and evaluate the system’s performance using Black Box Testing. The respondents of this study were the employees of Queen Hannah Birthing Home specifically the owner, staff, midwife/nurse, and patient. In gathering the data, interview guide and test case via questionnaire were used. The data gathered were analyzed and interpreted using Arithmetic Mean. Upon the analysis of the gathered data, the results have shown that the problems encountered in manual process of managing patient records, notifying of announcements, and generating reports include time-consuming process of paper-based recording, difficulties in relaying updates and announcements to patients, mistakes and inaccuracy in patient numbering, and manual recording of reports. Further, upon the evaluation of the black box testing in terms of boundary value analysis and requirements-based testing, the result has shown an overall rating of 0.97 and is highly functional. Therefore, the implementation of Queen Hannah Birthing Home Information Management System with SMS Notification was recommended to enhance the birthing home’s record-keeping and transactions.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clarify the specific features and scope of your system to avoid overlap with existing solutions.\", \"archived_id\": 101, \"differences\": \"Scope differs slightly - one manages patient records and medicine inventory, the other focuses on SMS notifications.\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"Digitalizing patient records for birthing home.\", \"academic_year\": \"2024\"}, {\"score\": 70, \"title\": \"WEB-BASED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR CSPC’S PRODUCTION AND AUXILIARY SERVICES WITH INVETORY AND SALES TRACKING\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on digitalizing manual processes in an institution\'s operations.\", \"authors\": \"Jancee Kenn E. Abonita, Kathleen Tess I. Hugo, Julian Paul M. Padua\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"In an institution like the Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges, where operational efficiency and controlled use of resources is required, manual processes within the Production and Auxiliary Services (PAxS) office created a critical bottleneck. This resulted in records supposedly prone to errors and a significant lack of real-time visibility in inventory and sales. The Web-Based Management System for CSPC Production and Auxiliary Services with Inventory and Sales Tracking thus emerges as a transformational solution to revolutionize basic PAxS operations. This new web-based system specifically provides the accuracy required by setting up automated and centralized tracking of sales, inventory, and vehicle pass applications, thus improving overall accountability and administrative control. Automating these key workflows substantially reduces the administrative load on personnel and significantly increases the quality and expedience of service delivery. Developed using the Agile Scrum Methodology, the iterative, user-friendly process ensured the final system architecture—includin g User Account Management, User Ordering, Digital Vehicle Pass Application, Integrated Sales and Inventory Tracking, Payment Processing, and Comprehensive Report Generation modules—met all stakeholder requirements. To determine the system\'s quality and institutional readiness, comprehensive black-box testing was conducted in three important dimensions. The strict quantitative findings reveal the system to be viable: Functional Testing scored an outstanding 0.97 (High Functionality), proving all modules acted as per specifications. Performance Testing scored 0.88 (High Performance), indicating system stability and efficiency under full transaction load. Security Testing yielded 0.89 (Low Risk), which confirms strong controls were established to keep sensitive institutional information safe. The study\'s aims were achieved with the development of this web-based system, which provides PAxS with a stable, productive, and secure solution that significantly improves accountability, increases operational speed, and enables data-driven decision-making, making the platform applicable for large-scale institutional adoption.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clarify the unique challenges and benefits of your specific context to differentiate from the archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 2, \"differences\": \"Specific institution (lying-in clinic vs. production and auxiliary services) and different modules (medicine inventory vs. sales tracking)\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"Digitalizing manual processes for inventory and patient records management\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 68, \"title\": \"WEB BASED HEALTH MANAGEMENT SYSTEM WITH DATA ANALYTICS AND RFID FOR CAMARINES SUR POLYTECHNIC COLLEGES CLINIC\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on digitalizing patient records and inventory management for clinics.\", \"authors\": \"Ma.Diah G. Cambronero, Ike Renson S. Landong, Ian Jay Kyle D. Tipanero\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The Web-Based Health Management System with Data Analytics and RFID for Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges Clinic is an essential digital solution for institutional setting that restricts services provision based on manual processes. This platform changes the way the CSPC clinic functions by transferring manual processes with significant labor needs like record processing, appointment booking, and health report creation are being transferred to a safe, digital system. The system aims to enhance daily clinic efficiency for students, employees and staff by eliminating manual inefficiencies, service delays, and inaccurate data. The system uses an Agile Scrum model of flexibility, which has an eight-module structure. The RFID module, Medical/Dental Record Management, Appointment with SMS Notification, and Data Analytics and Reporting modules are the essential elements. These elements make operations digital, increase the accessibility of the records, and offer clinic administrators with the necessary data-driven health insights. System testing was done through rigorous procedures that ensured the system was operational and secure. Unit Testing had a high rating of 0.97, and Usability Testing gave the highest score of 1.0. OWASP scored 0.98 on Security Testing and Performance Testing demonstrated that the system could support many simultaneous users with a small amount of delay. Deployed in a cloud environment, the system provides CSPC digitized services, improved data accuracy, and easier healthcare access. This health management system is a digital hub of institutional healthcare that has shown the use of technology in enhancing the quality of services, health outcomes, and overall institutional effectiveness.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Define unique features that set your system apart from the archived document to strengthen your proposal.\", \"archived_id\": 14, \"differences\": \"Scope and specific features differ slightly (e.g. RFID vs. SMS notification)\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"Digitalizing patient records and inventory management\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 25, \"title\": \"PERFECT SMILE PORTAL: A MULTI-BRANCH WEB-BASED DENTAL CLINIC MANAGEMENT SYSTEM\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on dental clinic management but target different clinics and users.\", \"authors\": \"Brandon R. Caritos, Marc Aron B. Gamban, John Bert O. Manaog\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"Inefficiencies in the manual procedures of Perfect Smile Dental Clinic inspired the development of The Perfect Smile Portal: A Web-Based Dental Clinic Management System. Manual methods in maintaining patient records, scheduling appointments, recording treatments, and managing bills delay clinic operations and risk data accuracy. Guided by the Agile Software Development Model, the researchers designed and implemented a web-based system composing of the Patient Records, Appointment Scheduling, Treatment History, Billing, Staff and User Management, and Reporting & Analytics modules. The system is designed to enhance efficiency for clinics by way of automation, security in data management, and real-time access. Evaluation results proved it to be effective and ready for deployment. Unit Testing recorded a functionality score of 0.98, showing the reliability of module performance; User Acceptance Testing recorded a score of 0.99, reflecting the high satisfaction of its staff and patient volunteers; and Security Testing recorded 1.0, showing strong authentication and protection of data. It successfully migrated the manual process to a digitized one for the clinic by enhancing the accuracy of the records, automating the scheduling and billing processes, streamlining the workflow of the staff, and securing sensitive information. For further enhancement, a mobile application, integration with dental imaging tools, and multi-branch reporting can be added. To sum up, the Perfect Smile Portal marks one of the most important steps toward modern, technology-driven management of the dental clinic.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define your specific clinic or institution to avoid overlap.\", \"archived_id\": 53, \"differences\": \"One is for a lying-in clinic; the other for a dental clinic.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage patient records and clinic operations.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 15, \"title\": \"INFORMATION SYSTEM STRATEGIC PLAN FOR BELEN LYING-IN CLINIC MANAGEMENT SYSTEM NABUA, CAMARINES SUR\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on digitalizing clinic management but for different purposes (patient records vs. inventory monitoring).\", \"authors\": \"HERMOGENES A. HALLARE, JEAN PAULINE S. MABINI, JOHN ARNEL R. REPARIP\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"In the ever-changing business environment of today, organizations employ a three-year information system strategic planning process to synchronize their technological and business objectives, offering adaptability while also looking ahead to technology investments, current priorities, and maintaining competitiveness. In this connection, this generally aimed to create the Information System Strategic Plan for Belen Lying-In Clinic Management System Nabua, Camarines Sur. It specifically aimed to assess the current ICT status of Belen Lying-In Clinic; develop an Information System Strategic Plan for Belen Lying-In Clinic; and evaluate the Information System Strategic Plan based on the available ICT resource requirements of the Belen Lying-In Clinic In response to increasing data volume, Belen Lying-In Clinic faces challenges in managing equipment and inventory records. The objective is to enhance operational efficiency, data accuracy, and decision-making. However, financial constraints, technology availability, staff resistance, evolving regulations, and technological advances may limit implementation and long-term success. While the focus is on the Nabua, Camarines Sur branch, the research emphasizes system design over development, documenting details, and implementing a three-year information system plan. Data collection will involve from individuals currently employed at the Belen Lying-In Clinic in Nabua, Camarines Sur. Information will exclusively be gathered from this specific group within the clinic, and the study duration is limited to the next three years.This research utilized the descriptive research design. The respondents were the currently employed at the Belen Lying-In Clinic in Nabua, Camarines Sur. After the collection of the data through interview questionnaire, analysis was done using narrative analysis.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Define a more unique problem or objective to differentiate from the archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 158, \"differences\": \"Patient records vs. inventory monitoring; specific objectives differ\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Digitalization of clinic management\", \"academic_year\": \"2023\"}, {\"score\": 15, \"title\": \"BARANGAY HEALTH CENTER INFORMATION RECORDS MANAGEMENT SYSTEM\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on digitalizing records for healthcare settings but differ in specific context (lying-in clinic vs. barangay health center).\", \"authors\": \"JUDY ANN L. FORECE, JOANA G. OBERO, ROANNE G. SUMAYOD, ANGELIKA M. QUIDES, MA. JESSABEL B. SILAVA\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"In a highly technological society, human productivity is made more efficient through the development of electronic devices and gadgets. However, the case is different in Barangay Health Centers which still uses manual storing of files and computing, evidently using traditional approach as technology in rural areas is not yet developed. With these, the researchers come up with an idea that need to build a system that will help store the health records of patients make it more organized. Generally, the purpose of this system is to make staffs lessen the manual storage of data and make it easier to manage their transaction towards keeping, updating, deleting, editing, and searching patient’s information. To address the general and specific objectives of the study, the researchers used a mixed method research design and the Extreme Programming (XP) as the software development methodology. It is useful for collecting, analyzing, and interpreting data. The respondents of this study were the patients, Barangay Health Center staff and health workers. The data was obtained using an interview guide, Black Box Testing and the data was evaluated and interpreted using a weighted mean. The research findings indicate that there are problems in the data requirements needed for the system. As a result, the overall interpretation demonstrated that the proposed is beneficial the proposed system is beneficial to the respondents. As a result, this is a perfect opportunity to put the Barangay Health Center Information Records Management System into implementation.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 55, \"differences\": \"Scope and specific features differ significantly\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Digitalizing patient records\", \"academic_year\": \"2022\"}]', '[{\"id\": 92, \"name\": \"Mark Balilla, MIT\", \"role\": \"adviser\", \"reason\": \"Expertise in Data Analytics and Web Development aligns with the development of a web-based system for managing patient records and medicine inventory.\", \"expertise\": \"Data Analytics, Research Methodology, Web Development\", \"role_label\": \"Adviser\"}, {\"id\": 101, \"name\": \"Kenn Aurillas\", \"role\": \"adviser\", \"reason\": \"Expertise in Research Methodology and Web Development is relevant to the development of a web-based system.\", \"expertise\": \"Research Methodology, Quantitative Research, Mobile Apps, Web Development\", \"role_label\": \"Adviser\"}, {\"id\": 106, \"name\": \"Ian Cyrus S. Tumambing\", \"role\": \"adviser\", \"reason\": \"Expertise in Data Gathering & Instruments, Statistical Analysis, and Research Methodology is suitable for the study\'s methodology and data analysis needs.\", \"expertise\": \"Data Gathering & Instruments, Statistical Analysis, Qualitative Research, Quantitative Research, Research Methodology, Survey Design, Literature Review, Research Ethics\", \"role_label\": \"Adviser\"}, {\"id\": 103, \"name\": \"Ian Tumambing\", \"role\": \"consultant\", \"reason\": \"Expertise in System Analysis & Design, Database Systems, API Development, and Web Development aligns with the need for a web-based system for managing patient records and medicine inventory.\", \"expertise\": \"System Analysis & Design, Software Testing / QA, Database Systems, API Development, Desktop Applications, Mobile Apps, Web Development, UI/UX Design\", \"role_label\": \"Consultant\"}, {\"id\": 92, \"name\": \"Mark Balilla, MIT\", \"role\": \"consultant\", \"reason\": \"Expertise in Data Analytics and Web Development can be useful for ensuring the system\'s robustness and user-friendliness.\", \"expertise\": \"Data Analytics, Research Methodology, Web Development\", \"role_label\": \"Consultant\"}, {\"id\": 101, \"name\": \"Kenn Aurillas\", \"role\": \"consultant\", \"reason\": \"While not directly related to the technical aspects, expertise in Research Methodology and Mobile Apps could be beneficial for user interface design and data collection.\", \"expertise\": \"Research Methodology, Quantitative Research, Mobile Apps, Web Development\", \"role_label\": \"Consultant\"}]', '2026-09-16 03:55:41', '2026-09-16 03:55:41');
INSERT INTO `duplication_checks` (`id`, `student_s_y_id`, `document_path`, `concepts`, `top_score`, `verdict`, `matches`, `instructors_suggested`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(20, 11, 'duplication-checks/M3Fh9LkHI1n1JTK3vvl1gT49lqqBVp1Nhi6S6p4H.pdf', '{\"sdm\": \"Agile Development Methodology\", \"scope\": \"Project & Contract Management; Geospatial Mapping & Area Tracking; Timeline & Progress Monitoring; Automated Alerts; Comprehensive Reporting; Document Archiving; AI Intelligence Engine\", \"title\": \"PROJ-TRACK: An Integrated Monitoring and Automated Notification System for CSPC-PPFMS\", \"domain\": \"Web System\", \"keywords\": [\"PROJ-TRACK\", \"Integrated Monitoring\", \"Automated Notification\", \"CSPC-PPFMS\", \"Geospatial Mapping\", \"Area Tracking\", \"AI Intelligence Engine\", \"Agile Development Methodology\"], \"sdg_goals\": \"SDG 9 – Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure; SDG 11 – Sustainable Cities and Communities; SDG 16 – Peace, Justice, and Strong Institutions\", \"main_topic\": \"Development of a web-based system for monitoring and managing infrastructure projects at CSPC-PPFMS.\", \"limitations\": \"Connectivity; Data Entry; Integration; AI Accuracy; Geospatial Precision\", \"target_users\": \"Administrators of CSPC-PPFMS\", \"technologies\": [\"Google Maps API\", \"AI Intelligence Engine\"], \"research_agenda\": [\"Process Automation\", \"Information Science\", \"Smart Computing\", \"Business Administration and Management\"], \"problem_statement\": \"The CSPC Office of the Director - PPFMS currently relies on manual, paper-based records to monitor infrastructure, leading to risks of lost documents and delayed reporting, and a lack of spatial visualization.\", \"proposed_solution\": \"The project proposes a web-based system that centralizes project records and provides automated notifications, integrating the Google Maps API for geospatial mapping and area tracking.\"}', 70, 'High Similarity', '[{\"score\": 70, \"title\": \"RESEARCH PROJECT INFORMATION MANAGEMENT AND TRACKING SYSTEM\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on managing research project information and progress for an AI Research Center.\", \"authors\": \"China T. Bea, Louie B. Molina, Jessemri A. Tabayag\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"Through Research Project Information Management, the researchers come up with the idea to lessen the work in the AI Research Center for Community Development, or AIRCoDe, by managing and tracking the research project and its progress. Hence, this study aimed to develop a web-based system entitled “Research Project Information Management and Tracking System”, (RPIMTS) that help faculties and researchers in managing each research projects. The RPIMTS is paperless-based management system in which the researchers who are willing to propose new research can find it easier to apply their research. Applying for exploratory research, this study considered the data provided by the director, staff, researchers, and reviewers in the AIRCoDe. The researchers used stratified sampling techniques to gather data. The Blackbox testing for AIRCoDe’s system results reveal low vulnerability risk, excellent performance, and full functionality, with no detected errors. of the system. The researcher used the Extreme Programming (XP) phases for the development of the system, and by doing so, they created a great RPIMTS. By exploring the functionalities of the AIRCoDe, the researchers created a process flow that serves as a guide for every user that will use the system. After the development of the system, it undergoes testing, such as Use Case Testing, Performance Testing, and Security Testing, to show its level of functionality for use case testing, its level of vulnerability for security testing, and its level of response for performance testing. By those tests, it gives the results of passing those tests. The findings of this study may serve as a fundamental basis for the researchers to use the system in managing and tracking the research project and its progress.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clarify the specific scope of your project to avoid overlap with the archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 75, \"differences\": \"Scope differs slightly: one manages physical infrastructure, the other academic research.\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"Integrated monitoring and automated notification for infrastructure projects; web-based system for managing research projects\", \"academic_year\": \"2023\"}, {\"score\": 70, \"title\": \"OptiCCS: AN INTEGRATED SYSTEM FOR MONITORING AND MANAGING COMPUTER AND LABORATORY EQUIPMENT FOR THE COLLEGE OF COMPUTER STUDIES\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on integrated monitoring and management systems for computer equipment, targeting the same institution and users.\", \"authors\": \"Jan Andrew R Barte, Novie Heralyn B. Placides, Reymelene E. Valera\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The College of Computer Studies (CCS) at Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges struggles with inefficient paper-based laboratory management that lacks real-time monitoring for student activity and equipment. To address this, the researchers developed OptiCCS, an integrated web- based system for laboratory and equipment management. The system, built using Agile Scrum methodology, integrates a web application with a real-time monitoring application. The web application, developed on the CodeIgniter PHP framework with a MySQL database, manages inventory, class creation, role-based access, and report generation. The real-time monitoring service uses a Python client agent on each computer unit, connecting to a server built with React HTTP for API requests and the Ratchet WebSocket library for bi-directional communication, enabling live status reporting, screenshot feeds, violation detection, and remote command execution. The system uses Google OAuth for authentication. System validation involved black box testing for functionality, usability, and performance. Administrators, faculty, technicians, and students participated using a questionnaire, and the results were assessed based on the ISO 25010 software quality standard. Findings demonstrated a strong readiness for daily operation: Unit Testing yielded a mean score of 1.00, confirming components function as intended. User Acceptance Testing produced a mean score of 0.99, indicating the system meets end-user requirements. Stress Testing also achieved a mean score of 0.99, proving the system remains stable and responsive under load conditions. The study concludes that OptiCCS is a reliable and accepted solution capable of replacing the college’s manual methods with a centralized, efficient system that provides reliable real-time data for administrative decisions.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 13, \"differences\": \"Specific features differ slightly: OptiCCS uses real-time monitoring with a web application; PROJ-TRACK focuses on automated notifications and AI intelligence engine\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"Integrated monitoring and management system for computer equipment\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 34, \"title\": \"SPHERE: CSPC SPACE FACILITY AND EQUIPMENT RENTAL AND EVENT MANAGEMENT SYSTEM\", \"reason\": \"Not assessed - this one was outside the set the checker examined.\", \"authors\": \"Liza Mae B. Cleofe, Katrina G. Luzadas, Jomel G. Tienes\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"This study developed SPHERE: CSPC Space Facility and Equipment Rental and Event Management System, a centralized web-based platform designed to address the inefficiencies of the manual, paper-based booking process used by the Supply and Property Management Office (SPMO) of Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges. The study specifically aimed to identify existing facility and equipment reservation procedures, develop a digital system that automates booking, documentation, and event management, and evaluate the system using Black-Box testing to assess functionality, security, performance, and compatibility. The system was developed through requirements analysis, system design, iterative development, and testing, incorporating features such as real-time availability monitoring, centralized booking management, automated document generation, billing computation, inventory tracking, booking status monitoring, and a QR code–based attendance mechanism. Evaluation results showed that SPHERE met the required quality standards, demonstrating reliable performance, secure data handling, high usability, and cross-device compatibility, while significantly reducing administrative workload and scheduling conflicts and improving transparency and operational efficiency. It is therefore recommended that SPHERE be fully adopted by CSPC and further enhanced through the integration of advanced reporting, expanded attendance analytics, and dynamic facility management to support scalability and continuous institutional digital transformation.\", \"assessed\": false, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 44, \"differences\": \"\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 23, \"title\": \"GIS- INTEGRATED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR EVANGELICAL CEMETERY IN SANTIAGO, IRIGA CITY\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages infrastructure projects, the other cemetery records.\", \"authors\": \"John Rick L. Babila, Maria Lourdes S. Arcilla, John Mark David S. Pajenago\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The Evangelical Cemetery in Santiago, Iriga City had experienced disadvantages that come along with the traditional way of keeping records, inefficient plot tracking, and limited access to burial information which led to data inaccuracies and service delays. In an attempt to solve the problem, a GIS-Integrated Management System was launched that would be helpful in the modernization of cemetery operations while also taking into consideration the local cultural and religious practices. The aim of the research was to devise, create a web-based system that includes functions for managing burial records, allocating and tracking plots, managing deceased profiles, providing notification services, and visualization of plots based on GIS technology. A black-box testing approach was taken to evaluate the system, wherein different testing methods like functional, integration, security, compatibility, and usability were applied. The total average score of 0.99 was achieved for both functional and integration testing, where integration got the highest rating of 1.00 meaning there was 100% module interaction. Secured, compatible, and usability testing then reported their average scores of 4.50, 4.46, and 4.48, respectively, which were all seen as Highly Functional. It can thus be concluded that the system is able to significantly enhance efficiency, accuracy, data security, and accessibility. Overall, the research work establishes the claim that GIS and web technologies can be easily and effectively combined to create a record management system and service delivery solution that works in a local context.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define the specific scope and target users for your system to avoid overlap with this archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 48, \"differences\": \"One focuses on physical infrastructure, the other on burial plots.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage records for monitoring and notifications.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 20, \"title\": \"ELEVATEGS: A PROGRESSIVE WEB APPLICATION LEARNING MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR GRADUATE SCHOOL OF USANT\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages infrastructure projects, the other learning management systems.\", \"authors\": \"Kristhan B. Aguilar, Lenard Anthony A. Gaa, Lyle Mathew S. Ramales\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"This study developed ElevateGS a Progressive Web Application (PWA) Learning Management System, to address critical operational inefficiencies at the University of Saint Anthony (USANT) Graduate School, specifically the heavy reliance on manual grading, decentralized announcement channels, and scattered course management that complicates resource retrieval. Utilizing the Adapted Agile Scrum Framework, the system features a decoupled architecture with a PHP Laravel backend and Vue.js frontend, incorporating Service Workers and IndexedDB to enable offline synchronization and centralize academic materials. A mixed-method evaluation involving 60 respondents including faculty, students, and IT experts revealed that the system is \\\"Highly Functional\\\" (composite mean of 0.99), with a 100% success rate for offline capabilities. Usability was rated as \\\"High\\\" (weighted mean of 3.82) and user satisfaction as \\\"Good\\\" (System Usability Scale score of 78.76), confirming that ElevateGS successfully bridges the gap between fragmented, manual processes and digital demands by providing a centralized, and offline- capable platform for the graduate school.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define your specific problem and target users for a more distinct proposal.\", \"archived_id\": 19, \"differences\": \"Different subjects (infrastructure vs. learning management) and users\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage centralization of records/delays\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 20, \"title\": \"BJMP (Bureau of Jail Management and Penology) Record Management System with Electronic Head Counting\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages infrastructure projects, the other records inmates\' presence.\", \"authors\": \"Angelito M. Arsenal Jr., Mary Grace R. Dilla, Lawrence G. Ramos\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"In today\'s landscape, technology is pivotal, reshaping how we interact, work, and navigate our world. A streamlined Record Management System is vital for organized, accessible, and meticulous record-keeping, promoting accountability and informed decision-making. This study focuses on automating record management for Persons Deprived of Liberty (PDLs), ensuring accurate tracking. Using a Mixed-method approach, Iriga City District Jails Officers were interviewed for data collection, which underwent arithmetic mean analysis. Black box testing showed use case and requirement-based testing achieving a Completely Functional level with a 100 overall average. The application significantly addresses challenges in manual recording and counting of PDLs, justifying the BJMP Record Management System with Electronic Head Counting implementation. This system revolutionizes inmate record-keeping, ensuring accuracy and efficiency. It streamlines data entry, facilitates seamless retrieval and analysis, aiding decision-making and resource allocation. This technological advancement enhances correctional facility operations, showcasing BJMP\'s commitment to modernizing record management, fostering transparency, accountability, and optimal resource utilization.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define your target users and specific problem being solved to avoid overlap with this archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 89, \"differences\": \"One focuses on PPDs and infrastructure monitoring; the other on inmate presence tracking.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both involve automated record-keeping systems.\", \"academic_year\": \"2024\"}, {\"score\": 20, \"title\": \"WEB-BASED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR CSPC’S PRODUCTION AND AUXILIARY SERVICES WITH INVETORY AND SALES TRACKING\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages infrastructure projects, the other production and auxiliary services.\", \"authors\": \"Jancee Kenn E. Abonita, Kathleen Tess I. Hugo, Julian Paul M. Padua\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"In an institution like the Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges, where operational efficiency and controlled use of resources is required, manual processes within the Production and Auxiliary Services (PAxS) office created a critical bottleneck. This resulted in records supposedly prone to errors and a significant lack of real-time visibility in inventory and sales. The Web-Based Management System for CSPC Production and Auxiliary Services with Inventory and Sales Tracking thus emerges as a transformational solution to revolutionize basic PAxS operations. This new web-based system specifically provides the accuracy required by setting up automated and centralized tracking of sales, inventory, and vehicle pass applications, thus improving overall accountability and administrative control. Automating these key workflows substantially reduces the administrative load on personnel and significantly increases the quality and expedience of service delivery. Developed using the Agile Scrum Methodology, the iterative, user-friendly process ensured the final system architecture—includin g User Account Management, User Ordering, Digital Vehicle Pass Application, Integrated Sales and Inventory Tracking, Payment Processing, and Comprehensive Report Generation modules—met all stakeholder requirements. To determine the system\'s quality and institutional readiness, comprehensive black-box testing was conducted in three important dimensions. The strict quantitative findings reveal the system to be viable: Functional Testing scored an outstanding 0.97 (High Functionality), proving all modules acted as per specifications. Performance Testing scored 0.88 (High Performance), indicating system stability and efficiency under full transaction load. Security Testing yielded 0.89 (Low Risk), which confirms strong controls were established to keep sensitive institutional information safe. The study\'s aims were achieved with the development of this web-based system, which provides PAxS with a stable, productive, and secure solution that significantly improves accountability, increases operational speed, and enables data-driven decision-making, making the platform applicable for large-scale institutional adoption.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define your specific institution and scope to avoid overlap with this archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 2, \"differences\": \"One focuses on infrastructure projects (PPFMS), the other on production and auxiliary services.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage project/asset monitoring and automated notifications.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 20, \"title\": \"WEB-BASED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM WITH SMS NOTIFICATION FOR BULA MUNICIPAL WATERWORKS\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages infrastructure projects, the other waterworks operations.\", \"authors\": \"Jahara P. Cervas, Jerl D. Illanza, Cyril Mae L. Pandes\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"In Water utility services, effective operations are crucial to provide the consumers with good services. However, traditional methods of record management and information delivery may affect the timeliness and accuracy of daily operations. To address these, this study focused on developing a Web-Based Management System with SMS Notification to enhance the processes in Bula Municipal Waterworks System (BMWS), which currently serves over 3,000 consumers from 22 barangays. The web-based platform includes several key features, such as consumer management, bill generation, meter reading, consumer support, SMS notification, and reports generation, designed to ensure that billing cycles, service updates, and information control and retrieval are secure, timely and accurate. To guarantee a continuous improvement throughout the system development, the Agile Scrum framework was utilized, allowing flexibility in handling requirements. To evaluate the system, black box testing was conducted to assess both the functional and non-functional aspects of the system, particularly focusing on the functionality, complete workflow, performance, and security. The functionality tests using test cases and end-to-end tests using Selenium IDE showed perfect 1.0 scores, performance achieved 0. 85 (Good Performance) in a load test with Apache JMeter, and security scans using OWASP ZAP found no high risks out of the total 12 findings. The test results reflect the system\'s capability in handling management operations and speeding up processes, which will significantly decrease the workloads of the staff, while gaining consumer trust through transparency. Currently implemented at BMWS, the system helps the local water service transform in terms of modernization, paving the way for future improvements in scalability and community engagement.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define the specific scope and target users for your system to avoid overlap with other domains.\", \"archived_id\": 5, \"differences\": \"One focuses on infrastructure projects (PROJ-TRACK), the other on water utility services.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage record monitoring and automated notifications.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 15, \"title\": \"IBARYO: GOVERNANCE AUTOMATED AND KPI MONITORING SYSTEM FOR PALOYON ORIENTAL, NABUA, CAMARINES SUR\", \"reason\": \"Different core domains: one manages infrastructure projects, the other barangay governance.\", \"authors\": \"Roland Joseph P. Cordez, Rayven Fran M. Toralde, Judah Paulo L. Viñas\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"This study developed iBaryo, a web-based governance system designed to help Barangay Paloyon Oriental manage tasks and services more efficiently. Before the system, the barangay relied on manual paperwork that caused delays, missing records, and difficulty in tracking responsibilities and officials’ performance. With iBaryo, barangay operations are centralized in one platform, including role-based task assignments, online document requests, complaint submissions, event scheduling, census records, real-time notifications, and analytics for monitoring performance. It also uses Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) to check how well officials complete their tasks and respond to residents. The system was created using the Agile method and tested for functionality, usability, efficiency, and security, and results showed that it works well, is easy to use, fast, and secure. Overall, iBaryo makes barangay management more organized, transparent, and convenient for both officials and residents, while reducing paperwork and improving accountability. Future upgrades may include national database integration, predictive features, and a mobile app for better accessibility.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define your specific problem and target users to avoid overlap with iBaryo.\", \"archived_id\": 24, \"differences\": \"One focuses on project monitoring; the other on governance and KPI monitoring.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage automated systems for monitoring and notification.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 12, \"title\": \"BATO FARMLAND GEOLOCATION AND MAPPING SYSTEM\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages infrastructure projects, the other farmland mapping.\", \"authors\": \"Junel R. Joven, Julius M. Zaballa, Fernando P. Pasadilla\", \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The \\\"Bato Farmland Geolocation and Mapping System\\\" is a functional and user-friendly system when it comes to management and land mapping. This addresses the issues associated with manual recording and tracking of registered and insured farmers specifically in the Municipality of Bato. The system, which was specifically built for the Municipal Agriculture Office of Bato, aims to enhance efficiency, and reduce errors in farmers\' registration and tracking of farmland. It is primarily aimed at the office admin and staff that provides real-time monitoring and tracking of every farmland of registered farmers. The system provides accurate data on the location of the land area that serves as a guide to staff during the field visit for data collection. To ensure the level of functionality of the system, the system undergoes several test methods using black-box testing, where the use case and requirement-based testing were applied. The geolocation and mapping solution, developed in response to recognized concerns with manual tracking, of the registered farm and eliminates the need for manual data entry, offering a more efficient digital interface for users. The results of use case testing show a high degree of functionality, with an average mean of 0.98 (Highly Functional). Requirements-based testing confirms its efficacy, with a mean score of 0.98 (Highly Functional). The system\'s performance and alignment with objectives are supported by Local Government of Bato, input from administrators, and staff. “Bato Farmland Geolocation and Mapping System \\\" is set to transform municipal agricultural office administration by offering efficiency, accuracy and user-friendly system.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define your specific problem and target users to avoid confusion with unrelated systems.\", \"archived_id\": 72, \"differences\": \"Different subjects (infrastructure vs. farmland) and users (students vs. farmers)\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"No genuine overlap beyond generic wording\", \"academic_year\": \"2023\"}]', '[{\"id\": 91, \"name\": \"Grom Hellscream\", \"role\": \"adviser\", \"reason\": \"Expertise in Statistical Analysis and Research Methodology aligns with the need for a robust methodology for the web-based system development.\", \"expertise\": \"Statistical Analysis, Quantitative Research, Research Methodology, Survey Design\", \"role_label\": \"Adviser\"}, {\"id\": 92, \"name\": \"Mark Balilla, MIT\", \"role\": \"adviser\", \"reason\": \"Expertise in Data Analytics and Web Development is crucial for the implementation of the AI Intelligence Engine and automated notification features.\", \"expertise\": \"Research Methodology, Data Analytics, Web Development\", \"role_label\": \"Adviser\"}, {\"id\": 106, \"name\": \"Ian Cyrus S. Tumambing\", \"role\": \"adviser\", \"reason\": \"Expertise in Data Gathering and Statistical Analysis is essential for the development of a geospatial mapping and area tracking system.\", \"expertise\": \"Data Gathering & Instruments, Statistical Analysis, Qualitative Research, Quantitative Research, Research Methodology, Survey Design, Literature Review, Research Ethics\", \"role_label\": \"Adviser\"}, {\"id\": 103, \"name\": \"Ian Tumambing\", \"role\": \"consultant\", \"reason\": \"Expertise in System Analysis & Design, Software Testing/ QA, Database Systems, API Development, Desktop Applications, Mobile Apps, Web Development, UI/UX Design aligns with the need for a comprehensive web-based system.\", \"expertise\": \"System Analysis & Design, Software Testing / QA, Database Systems, API Development, Desktop Applications, Mobile Apps, Web Development, UI/UX Design\", \"role_label\": \"Consultant\"}, {\"id\": 92, \"name\": \"Mark Balilla, MIT\", \"role\": \"consultant\", \"reason\": \"Expertise in Research Methodology and Data Analytics can be beneficial for data-driven decision-making and monitoring processes.\", \"expertise\": \"Research Methodology, Data Analytics, Web Development\", \"role_label\": \"Consultant\"}, {\"id\": 109, \"name\": \"Maria Santos\", \"role\": \"consultant\", \"reason\": \"Expertise in Web Development and Research Methodology can support the development of the web-based system for monitoring and managing infrastructure projects.\", \"expertise\": \"Web Development, Research Methodology, Data Analytics\", \"role_label\": \"Consultant\"}]', '2026-09-17 01:43:23', '2026-09-17 01:43:23');
INSERT INTO `duplication_checks` (`id`, `student_s_y_id`, `document_path`, `concepts`, `top_score`, `verdict`, `matches`, `instructors_suggested`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(8, 1, 'duplication-checks/dDM7VJAJBZkCbiVKxMoh0NqQc4lJvlf4UBdPHCIj.pdf', '{\"sdm\": \"Agile Development Methodology\", \"scope\": \"Mobile Problem Reporting (Photo, Description, Location); AR Path Finder for Location Guidance; Report Categorization and Priority Level Assignment; Real-Time Status Tracking (Pending, Ongoing, Resolved); Automated Notifications and Alerts; Analytics Dashboard and Reports; User Account Management (Students, Staff, Maintenance).\", \"title\": \"CSPC SiteSense: Smart Facility Maintenance with AR-Assisted Location Guidance\", \"domain\": \"Mobile App\", \"keywords\": [\"CSPC\", \"Smart Facility Maintenance\", \"AR-Assisted Location Guidance\", \"Problem Reporting\", \"Mobile Application\", \"Augmented Reality\", \"Smart Computing\", \"Process Automation\", \"Information Science\"], \"sdg_goals\": \"SDG 9 – Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure; SDG 11 – Sustainable Cities and Communities; SDG 16 – Peace, Justice, and Strong Institutions\", \"main_topic\": \"Development of a mobile-based Problem Reporting Application integrated with an AR Path Finder for smart facility maintenance.\", \"limitations\": \"AR navigation accuracy depends on device sensors and camera quality; Requires smartphone compatibility with AR features; Internet connection is required for real-time reporting and updates.\", \"target_users\": \"Students, staff, and maintenance personnel\", \"technologies\": [\"Mobile Application\", \"Augmented Reality\", \"Smart Computing\", \"Process Automation\", \"Information Science\"], \"research_agenda\": [\"Augmented Reality and Virtual Reality\", \"Smart Computing\", \"Process Automation\", \"Information Science\"], \"problem_statement\": \"CSPC relies on manual and informal reporting methods for campus-related problems, leading to delayed, incomplete, or misplaced reports, and difficulties in locating exact problem areas.\", \"proposed_solution\": \"Develop a mobile-based Problem Reporting Application with AR Path Finder for real-time visual navigation, automated notifications, and status tracking.\"}', 25, 'Passed', '[{\"score\": 34, \"title\": \"INTEGRATED CAMPUS REPAIR, ICT, AND VEHICLE REQUEST SYSTEM FOR CAMARINES SUR POLYTECHNIC COLLEGES\", \"reason\": \"Not assessed - this one was outside the set the checker examined.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The Integrated Campus Repair, ICT, and Vehicle Request System developed for Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges aims to resolve problems encountered in processing requests manually. These problems include manual processing, errors in requests, and problems in document tracking. Other problems that the system aims to resolve include delays in processing requests, tracking requests, and managing submitting approvals. The system developed is a unified platform that allows users to digitally submit and track requests to all Campus premises. The system is a project developed under Scrum Agile Methodology where researchers designed the system while receiving feedback to adjust the construction to the needs of the user. Final system features include request tracking, automated email notifications, Role-based access control, and a system that collects requests. The system executed features were reviewed with a Unit Testing to inspect subsections of a system. The system\'s Usability and User Acceptance Tests as well as the system Security Tests confirmed that core and additional modules of the system worked. The system allows admins to streamline the way Campus Repair, ICT and Vehicle requests are processed and reduces the time taken to processed, recorded for correction, and responded to requests. From a campus service point of view, the system is a fast, effective, fully digitalized system for campus employees.\", \"assessed\": false, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 10, \"differences\": \"\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 25, \"title\": \"PARKMATE: RFID-BASED PARKING MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR CSPC\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one is a mobile app for problem reporting, the other is an RFID-based parking management system.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The manual parking monitoring system at Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges (CSPC) presents several operational challenges, including traffic congestion at entry points, inaccurate logbook records, and delayed access to parking data for security audits. These issues reduce the efficiency of security personnel and compromise campus safety. This study aimed to design and develop ParkMate, an RFID-based parking management system that automates vehicle entry and exit logging, improves traffic flow, enhances data accuracy, and supports real-time monitoring for campus parking facilities. The system was developed using RFID technology integrated with a centralized database and an administrative dashboard for the General Services Unit (GSU). System development followed a structured design and implementation process, while functionality and performance were evaluated through system testing and real-time campus demonstrations. Testing results showed a significant reduction in entry and exit processing time compared to the manual system, with logging accuracy reaching 100% during test scenarios. Data retrieval time was reduced from several minutes to near real-time access, and parking slot monitoring achieved full operational reliability during demonstrations. ParkMate successfully addresses the limitations of the existing manual parking system by providing a secure, efficient, and scalable RFID-based solution. The system enhances operational speed, data reliability, and campus security while reducing the workload of security personnel, making it a practical solution for institutional parking management\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define the specific users and operational processes each system will cover to avoid overlap.\", \"archived_id\": 25, \"differences\": \"One focuses on smart facility maintenance with AR guidance; the other on RFID-based parking management.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage operational processes (reporting/monitoring).\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 25, \"title\": \"WEB BASED HEALTH MANAGEMENT SYSTEM WITH DATA ANALYTICS AND RFID FOR CAMARINES SUR POLYTECHNIC COLLEGES CLINIC\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one is a mobile app for smart facility maintenance, the other is a web-based health management system.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The Web-Based Health Management System with Data Analytics and RFID for Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges Clinic is an essential digital solution for institutional setting that restricts services provision based on manual processes. This platform changes the way the CSPC clinic functions by transferring manual processes with significant labor needs like record processing, appointment booking, and health report creation are being transferred to a safe, digital system. The system aims to enhance daily clinic efficiency for students, employees and staff by eliminating manual inefficiencies, service delays, and inaccurate data. The system uses an Agile Scrum model of flexibility, which has an eight-module structure. The RFID module, Medical/Dental Record Management, Appointment with SMS Notification, and Data Analytics and Reporting modules are the essential elements. These elements make operations digital, increase the accessibility of the records, and offer clinic administrators with the necessary data-driven health insights. System testing was done through rigorous procedures that ensured the system was operational and secure. Unit Testing had a high rating of 0.97, and Usability Testing gave the highest score of 1.0. OWASP scored 0.98 on Security Testing and Performance Testing demonstrated that the system could support many simultaneous users with a small amount of delay. Deployed in a cloud environment, the system provides CSPC digitized services, improved data accuracy, and easier healthcare access. This health management system is a digital hub of institutional healthcare that has shown the use of technology in enhancing the quality of services, health outcomes, and overall institutional effectiveness.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define the unique features and target users of each system to avoid overlap.\", \"archived_id\": 14, \"differences\": \"One focuses on problem reporting and AR navigation; the other on health record management and appointment booking.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage digital processes for institutional settings.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 25, \"title\": \"WAMS: WEB-BASED APARTMENT MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR EFFICIENT TENANT AND FACILITY ADMINISTRATION\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: apartment management vs. smart facility maintenance.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"Manual apartment management in Nabua, Camarines Sur faces inefficiencies including paper-based records, delayed payment tracking, and slow maintenance handling across seven registered apartments, causing administrative errors and tenant dissatisfaction. This study developed the Web-Based Apartment Management System (WAMS) using Laravel framework and MySQL database to automate property management operations. Core modules include Apartment Unit Management, Applicant Management, Payment Billing System, and Maintenance Request handling with OTP verification, role-based access control, and PHPMailer automated notifications. The system was evaluated through black-box testing with 70 respondents (5 IT experts, 7 property owners, 58 tenants) using binary scoring (0-Failed, 1-Passed) across functional, load, and security dimensions. Results showed Functional Testing achieving 1.00 (Completely Functional), Load Testing scoring 0.96 (High Performance) under concurrent loads, and Security Testing reaching 1.00 (Fully Secure) against SQL injection, XSS attacks, and unauthorized access, yielding overall 0.99 effectiveness. WAMS successfully transformed manual operations into an automated web-based platform that eliminated paper-based delays, enhanced transparency, reduced administrative workload, and improved tenant satisfaction, proving reliable for Philippine apartment complexes with recommendations for mobile integration, analytics dashboards, automated scheduling, multi-language support, and two-factor authentication.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define the unique problem and target users for your smart facility maintenance system.\", \"archived_id\": 37, \"differences\": \"Target users differ (students/staff vs. tenants), specific features differ (payment tracking vs. AR location guidance).\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage administrative tasks for tenants/facilities.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 20, \"title\": \"CAMARINES SUR POLYTECHNIC COLLEGES WEB AND MOBILE-BASED LOST AND FOUND MANAGEMENT SYSTEM WITH IMAGE RECOGNITION\", \"reason\": \"Different core domains: one is smart facility maintenance with AR guidance, the other is lost and found management with image recognition.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"Lost and found operations in academic institutions are often handled manually, causing delays, difficulty in tracking items. This study developed a Web and Mobile-Based Lost and Found for Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges to address these challenges. The system automates item reporting, storage, retrieval, and communication by integrating image recognition using the Gemini 2.0 Flash Lite API, centralized logging, and automated email notifications to improve efficiency and accessibility. It was developed using CodeIgniter 4, React Native, JavaScript, PHP, and MySQL, following the Agile methodology. The respondents included CSPC students, CSPC-SSC, and IT experts selected for their direct involvement and knowledge of lost and found operations. Data were gathered through test cases to evaluate system functionality, usability, performance efficiency, and security. The procedure involved system orientation, actual usage, and evaluation through Black Box Testing. Results revealed that the existing procedure experiences difficulties in documentation, secure storage, retrieval, and communication. Evaluation showed excellent system performance, with Requirement-Based and Usability Testing both scoring 0.99, and Performance Efficiency and Security Testing scoring 1.00. In conclusion, the system effectively addresses manual process limitations by providing a centralized, organized, and secure platform that improves reporting, retrieval, storage, and communication. It demonstrates strong functionality, usability, performance, and security, indicating readiness for campus-wide implementation. It is recommended to maintain system performance and security through regular testing using tools such as JMeter and OWASP ZAP, ensuring improved accessibility and user experience.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define your target users and specific problem being solved to avoid overlap with the archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 36, \"differences\": \"One focuses on real-time navigation and automated notifications; the other emphasizes secure storage and retrieval through image recognition.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage physical items (facilities vs. lost/ found), but for different purposes.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 15, \"title\": \"ANALYSIS AND DEVELOPMENT OF ICT REPAIR MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR CAMARINES SUR POLYTECHNIC COLLEGES\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: ICT repair management vs. smart facility maintenance with AR-assisted location guidance.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"ICT systems require maintenance and repair to ensure their longevity and optimal performance. In CSPC, the current repair management system for ICT systems is conducted manually and paper based. This method can be inefficient and prone to errors, which can result in delays in the repair process. Manual systems make it challenging to manage the inventory of ICT equipment and maintain proper records of repairs and maintenance work. In general, the objective is to Design and develop an ICT Repair Management System with Functional suitability, Performance efficiency, Usability, Reliability, and Maintainability. To address the objectives of the study, the researchers used a mixed method research design and the Extreme Programming. The study respondents were the faculties, admin, and ICT Repair and Maintenance Staff/technician. The data was obtained using an interview guide and survey questionnaire. The data was evaluated and interpreted using a weighted mean. The research findings indicate that there are problems with Time Efficiency, Potential Loss of Data, Generating Reports, and File Tracing Issues. Thus, the overall interpretation revealed that the suggested system is highly acceptable to the respondents. As a result, the proposed system is acceptable for implementation in Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges ICT Repair.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Define a more unique problem or target user group to differentiate from the archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 155, \"differences\": \"One focuses on ICT systems, the other on smart facilities; different specific features and users.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage maintenance processes.\", \"academic_year\": \"2023\"}, {\"score\": 15, \"title\": \"TRACKCSPC: A SMART CAMPUS VEHICLE TRACKING AND RESERVATION PLATFORM\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one is a mobile app for problem reporting, the other is a vehicle tracking platform.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"This study presents TrackCSPC: A smart campus vehicle tracking and reservations platform developed for the Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges–General Services Unit (GSU) to address inefficiencies in manual vehicle reservation processes, including delays, inconsistent documentation, and limited monitoring. The system integrates a mobile application for submitting vehicle requests and tracking reservations in real time with a web-based administrative dashboard for approval, driver assignment, and GPS-based vehicle monitoring. A mixed-method research design was employed using surveys, interviews, and observations, while system evaluation involved functional testing, load testing, and User Acceptance Testing (UAT). Evaluation results yielded an overall mean score of 1.00, interpreted as Completely Functional, indicating high reliability, usability, and operational efficiency. The findings demonstrate that TrackCSPC improves workflow management, communication, and centralized vehicle monitoring, with only minor refinements identified for specific user groups. The study concludes that TrackCSPC effectively enhances campus transportation management through automated reservation workflows and real-time tracking and recommends continuous system maintenance, user training, and future enhancements such as AI-based scheduling and online payment integration. The study employed a mixed-method research design and evaluated the system through surveys, interviews, and direct observations. System performance was assessed using functional testing, load testing, and User Acceptance Testing (UAT). The evaluation results yielded an overall mean score of 1.00, interpreted as Completely Functional, demonstrating the system’s high reliability, usability, and operational efficiency.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define the specific problems each system addresses to avoid overlap.\", \"archived_id\": 31, \"differences\": \"One focuses on smart facility maintenance with AR guidance; the other on vehicle reservations and monitoring.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both address inefficiencies in manual processes.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 15, \"title\": \"E-GUIDANCE: AN ONLINE APPOINTMENT AND INFORMATION SYSTEM FOR THE CENTER FOR GUIDANCE SERVICES\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on modernizing appointment systems but target different institutions and users.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The E-Guidance System aims to modernize the operations at the Center for Guidance Services of Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges (CSPC) by transitioning from manual processes to a digital platform. The problem was that the old system used paper forms, which caused lost records, scheduling errors, and a heavy workload for staff. To fix this, the team built \\\"E-Guidance,\\\" a website meant to make booking appointments easy and information more accessible. Used the Agile method to develop the software and tested it with 62 people, including students and staff. The methodology involved Black-Box Testing and surveys to check if the system was easy to use and safe. The numerical results were excellent, showing a perfect 100% success rate in functionality and a 5.0 mean score for user satisfaction. These scores prove the system is \\\"Highly Functional\\\" and \\\"Highly Usable.\\\" In conclusion, the new system successfully replaced the slow manual steps with a fast, digital process. It keeps student data safe and organized, following strict security rules. The researchers recommend using the system right away to help students better. Future updates should include text message alerts and better data tools to help school leaders make good decisions. This change makes the guidance services modern, reliable, and much faster for everyone at CSPC.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Specify the unique challenges and benefits of your system in relation to smart facility maintenance.\", \"archived_id\": 52, \"differences\": \"One for a guidance center, the other for smart facility maintenance\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Modernize appointment systems\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 15, \"title\": \"ANITALA: A COMMUNITY-DRIVE N PLANT MAPPING AND GEO-TAGGING WEB APPLICATION FOR HARVEST SELLING AND SHARING\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages facility maintenance with AR guidance, the other maps plant locations for harvesting and sharing.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"AniTala is based on the word Ani (harvest) and Tala (record), and as such is a site where harvests by the community are documented and indexed. This exploration ushered in AniTala: A Community-based Plant Mapping and Geo-Tagging Web Application in Harvest Selling and Sharing, which is a system that would help users map the locations of plants, visualize nearest harvests, and conduct community-based or business sharing or commercial transactions. The system reacts to the limitations of the easily available methodologies, which ease the process of identifying plant harvests in local settings. Using Agile methodology, the research team formulated and developed the platform, including features such as plant geo-tagging, map visualization, user management, and a harvest list. Data gathering was conducted in the Rinconada area, comprising 300 respondents, including 125 farmers, 125 students, 50 agricultural workers, and others. Also, black-box testing strategies were applied to assess system functionality and usability. The results 6.48 and rated it “Highly Accepted” that the AniTala platform is useful to support the mapping of plants and distribution of harvests, allowing customers and users to find out and buy the existing produce in their communities. The platform improves the exposure, creates a partnership with the community, and makes local harvests easy to reach. Future improvements can include the creation of a mobile application, the improvement of plant recognition potential, and an increase in mapping analytics.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define your unique problem and target users to avoid overlap.\", \"archived_id\": 26, \"differences\": \"One focuses on smart facility maintenance (e.g. problem reporting, AR navigation), the other on mapping plants for harvest selling/sharing.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage location-based data for community use.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 14, \"title\": \"WEB-BASED RESORT AND APARTMENT MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR BALANG MARISTELA CORPORATION\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: resort and apartment management vs. smart facility maintenance.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"This research focuses on the development of a Web-Based Resort and Apartment Management System for Balang Maristela Corporation. This aims to improve the efficiency, accuracy, and convenience of managing business operations, customer communications, and reporting compared to manual processes. The project encompasses various functionalities, including user management, booking and reservation systems, payment and billing processing, employee management, notifications, and report generation. However, it has limitations, particularly its reliance on internet connectivity and its applicability being confined to the corporation\'s operations. The study employed agile methodology and mixed-method design for data collection, involving administrators, staff, IT experts, and tenants as respondents. Data was gathered through interviews and questionnaires, analyzed using the arithmetic mean, and interpreted with the Likert Scale. The evaluation included testing the system’s functionality, reliability, compatibility, interaction capability, performance efficiency, and maintainability, in accordance with criteria set in ISO 25010. Findings indicate that the manual processes were plagued by inaccuracy and delays, while the proposed system demonstrated potential to improve real-time information management, garnering a total score of 0.98. Thus, it is concluded that despite its advantages in accessibility and efficiency, the system faces structural instability and significant technical debt, suggesting risks to long-term performance and sustainability.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define your unique problem and target users to differentiate from the archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 30, \"differences\": \"One focuses on booking and reservations; the other on problem reporting and AR-assisted location guidance.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage operations efficiently.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}]', '[]', '2026-09-09 05:37:15', '2026-09-09 05:37:15');
INSERT INTO `duplication_checks` (`id`, `student_s_y_id`, `document_path`, `concepts`, `top_score`, `verdict`, `matches`, `instructors_suggested`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(9, 11, 'duplication-checks/C9Ar2RYimSMm7LBqH2dDecQ0DdkUxpok1enCb6F0.pdf', '{\"sdm\": \"Agile Development Methodology\", \"scope\": \"The system will include modules for patient records management (maternal & child health), medicine inventory management, expiring medicine notification system, low-Stock alerts and inventory reports, medicine issuance and usage tracking, user account management (admin, midwife, staff), data search, filtering, and report generation.\", \"title\": \"MediTrack-MCH: A Digital Inventory and Patient Records Management System for a Lying-In Clinic\", \"domain\": \"Management System\", \"keywords\": [\"MediTrack-MCH\", \"digital inventory\", \"patient records\", \"lying-in clinic\", \"medicine management\", \"web-based system\", \"Agile Development Methodology\"], \"sdg_goals\": \"SDG 3 – Good Health and Well-Being; SDG 9 – Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure; SDG 16 – Peace, Justice, and Strong Institutions\", \"main_topic\": \"Development of a web-based system for managing patient records and medicine inventory in a Lying-In Clinic\", \"limitations\": \"The system requires internet or local network connectivity; existing paper records must be manually encoded during initial implementation; the system is designed specifically for the Lying-In Clinic and does not cover hospital-wide integration.\", \"target_users\": \"Lying-In Clinic staff, including admin, midwives, and staff\", \"technologies\": [\"web-based system\", \"medicine management\", \"user account management\", \"data search\", \"report generation\"], \"research_agenda\": [\"Health Technologies\", \"Information Science\", \"Process Automation\", \"Smart Computing\"], \"problem_statement\": \"The current manual, paper-based records for managing patient information and medicine inventory increase the risk of lost, damaged, or incomplete records, inaccurate stock monitoring, and delayed identification of expired or low-stock medicines.\", \"proposed_solution\": \"The project proposes the development of a web-based Integrated Patient Records and Medicine Inventory System for the Lying-In Clinic, including modules for patient records management, medicine inventory monitoring, expiring medicine notifications, low-Stock alerts, and user account management.\"}', 75, 'High Similarity', '[{\"score\": 75, \"title\": \"MEDICARE: A WEB-BASED MEDICAL INVENTORY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM WITH DATA ANALYTICS\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on digitalizing medical inventory and patient records management for healthcare facilities.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The healthcare industry relies on effective inventory management to balance patient needs with resource availability. This project aimed to developed Web-Based Medical Inventory Management System for the Medical Mission Group Hospital and Health Services Cooperative of Camarines Sur by automating, optimizing manual processes, and utilizing data analytics. Black box testing and Scrum Methodology were used, and surveys and interviews were conducted with IT experts, supply officers, medical staff, pharmacists, and cashiers. The MediCare system, which includes the Medical Inventory Management System and Patient Data Management System, was developed in collaboration with Team Aries, ensuring efficient hospital operations.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Define a more specific scope that clearly distinguishes between digitalizing medical inventory and patient records versus incorporating data analytics in healthcare operations.\", \"archived_id\": 78, \"differences\": \"Scope: MediTrack-MCH covers patient records and medicine inventory; MEDICARE focuses on data analytics. Users: MediTrack-MCH targets a lying-in clinic; MEDICARE targets a hospital. Specific features: MediTrack-MCH includes modules for patient records management, medicine inventory monitoring, expiring medicine notifications, low-Stock alerts, and user account management; MEDICARE emphasizes data analytics such as surveys and interviews conducted with IT experts, supply officers, medical staff, pharmacists, and cashiers.\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"Digitalization of medical inventory and patient records\", \"academic_year\": \"2023\"}, {\"score\": 75, \"title\": \"DRA. EULALIA ELGAR CLINIC MANAGEMENT SYSTEM\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on a digital management system for clinic operations, targeting the same users (patients and staff).\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The emergence of technological advancements provided innovation in organizations to efficiently accomplished tasks. The idea is to eliminate the manual method of doing transactions manually, and saving time in the process of appointment. This study generally aims to develop a web-based Dra. Eulalia Elgar Clinic Management System for Espiritu-Elgar Medical Clinic, with these this study was conducted to develop appointment clinic management system that would systematically organize the appointment scheduling of patients/client, to manage user account, manage patient record, generate the report and generate the data analytics. This study used a mixed-methods research design that combines parts of quantitative and qualitative research to contextualize the data, therefore only the data gathered from the target respondents would be the only references for the development of the proposed system. After the collection of data through an interview with a guide questions, analysis was done using the frequency percentage and weighted mean. The iterative method was utilized throughout the study. On the system development, the result shows that the most frequently encountered problems in the clinic are the patient queue and the manual process of recording patients’ information. Furthermore, the evaluation of the performance of the system, the result shows 1 in level of functionality, and the respondents agree that the functionality of the develop system was excellent. The researchers concluded that clinic management system is necessary in managing clinical processes, the system development is effectively being done by following modules and phases of an Iterative Model, with the use of Black Box Testing. Based from a forementioned conclusions, researchers arrived with the following recommendations that future researchers conduct studies in other relevant research environments, consider document retrieval and document security consider and add billing statement in other related studies for further enhancement of the study.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Define a more specific scope to differentiate your proposal further.\", \"archived_id\": 60, \"differences\": \"Specific features differ slightly - one focuses on appointment scheduling, the other on user account management, patient records, and data analytics.\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"Digital management system for clinic operations\", \"academic_year\": \"2022\"}, {\"score\": 75, \"title\": \"Queen Hannah Birthing Home Information Management System with SMS Notification\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on digitalizing patient record management for a birthing home setting.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"Birthing homes play a significant role in healthcare, serving as essential centers for maternal care. Many such facilities, including Queen Hannah Birthing Home, still rely on traditional paper-based processes, contrasting with the advancing landscape of healthcare technology. With these, this study was conducted aimed on digitizing the paper-based patient record system of Queen Hannah Birthing Home. Generally, this study identified the problems encountered in the manual processes of the birthing home, developed and implemented an efficient and effective web-based information management system that manage patient records electronically, update patient for check-up appointments through SMS Notification; and evaluate the system’s performance using Black Box Testing. The respondents of this study were the employees of Queen Hannah Birthing Home specifically the owner, staff, midwife/nurse, and patient. In gathering the data, interview guide and test case via questionnaire were used. The data gathered were analyzed and interpreted using Arithmetic Mean. Upon the analysis of the gathered data, the results have shown that the problems encountered in manual process of managing patient records, notifying of announcements, and generating reports include time-consuming process of paper-based recording, difficulties in relaying updates and announcements to patients, mistakes and inaccuracy in patient numbering, and manual recording of reports. Further, upon the evaluation of the black box testing in terms of boundary value analysis and requirements-based testing, the result has shown an overall rating of 0.97 and is highly functional. Therefore, the implementation of Queen Hannah Birthing Home Information Management System with SMS Notification was recommended to enhance the birthing home’s record-keeping and transactions.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Define more clearly the unique features and target users to differentiate from the archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 101, \"differences\": \"Scope and specific features differ slightly (e.g. SMS notifications vs. web-based system)\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"Digitalization of patient records\", \"academic_year\": \"2024\"}, {\"score\": 75, \"title\": \"WEB-BASED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR CSPC’S PRODUCTION AND AUXILIARY SERVICES WITH INVETORY AND SALES TRACKING\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on digitalizing manual processes for inventory and patient records management in a healthcare setting.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"In an institution like the Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges, where operational efficiency and controlled use of resources is required, manual processes within the Production and Auxiliary Services (PAxS) office created a critical bottleneck. This resulted in records supposedly prone to errors and a significant lack of real-time visibility in inventory and sales. The Web-Based Management System for CSPC Production and Auxiliary Services with Inventory and Sales Tracking thus emerges as a transformational solution to revolutionize basic PAxS operations. This new web-based system specifically provides the accuracy required by setting up automated and centralized tracking of sales, inventory, and vehicle pass applications, thus improving overall accountability and administrative control. Automating these key workflows substantially reduces the administrative load on personnel and significantly increases the quality and expedience of service delivery. Developed using the Agile Scrum Methodology, the iterative, user-friendly process ensured the final system architecture—includin g User Account Management, User Ordering, Digital Vehicle Pass Application, Integrated Sales and Inventory Tracking, Payment Processing, and Comprehensive Report Generation modules—met all stakeholder requirements. To determine the system\'s quality and institutional readiness, comprehensive black-box testing was conducted in three important dimensions. The strict quantitative findings reveal the system to be viable: Functional Testing scored an outstanding 0.97 (High Functionality), proving all modules acted as per specifications. Performance Testing scored 0.88 (High Performance), indicating system stability and efficiency under full transaction load. Security Testing yielded 0.89 (Low Risk), which confirms strong controls were established to keep sensitive institutional information safe. The study\'s aims were achieved with the development of this web-based system, which provides PAxS with a stable, productive, and secure solution that significantly improves accountability, increases operational speed, and enables data-driven decision-making, making the platform applicable for large-scale institutional adoption.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Define unique features or additional users to distinguish your proposal from the archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 2, \"differences\": \"Scope: one manages medicine inventory, the other patient records; users: both target staff but differ in specific roles (PAxS vs. clinic)\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"Digitalization of manual processes for inventory and patient records\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 68, \"title\": \"WEB BASED HEALTH MANAGEMENT SYSTEM WITH DATA ANALYTICS AND RFID FOR CAMARINES SUR POLYTECHNIC COLLEGES CLINIC\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on digitalizing patient records and inventory management for clinics.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The Web-Based Health Management System with Data Analytics and RFID for Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges Clinic is an essential digital solution for institutional setting that restricts services provision based on manual processes. This platform changes the way the CSPC clinic functions by transferring manual processes with significant labor needs like record processing, appointment booking, and health report creation are being transferred to a safe, digital system. The system aims to enhance daily clinic efficiency for students, employees and staff by eliminating manual inefficiencies, service delays, and inaccurate data. The system uses an Agile Scrum model of flexibility, which has an eight-module structure. The RFID module, Medical/Dental Record Management, Appointment with SMS Notification, and Data Analytics and Reporting modules are the essential elements. These elements make operations digital, increase the accessibility of the records, and offer clinic administrators with the necessary data-driven health insights. System testing was done through rigorous procedures that ensured the system was operational and secure. Unit Testing had a high rating of 0.97, and Usability Testing gave the highest score of 1.0. OWASP scored 0.98 on Security Testing and Performance Testing demonstrated that the system could support many simultaneous users with a small amount of delay. Deployed in a cloud environment, the system provides CSPC digitized services, improved data accuracy, and easier healthcare access. This health management system is a digital hub of institutional healthcare that has shown the use of technology in enhancing the quality of services, health outcomes, and overall institutional effectiveness.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Define unique selling points or additional features to differentiate from the archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 14, \"differences\": \"Scope and specific features differ slightly (e.g. RFID vs. SMS notification)\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"Digitalization of patient records and inventory management\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 25, \"title\": \"PERFECT SMILE PORTAL: A MULTI-BRANCH WEB-BASED DENTAL CLINIC MANAGEMENT SYSTEM\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on digital management systems but for different contexts (dentistry vs. lying-in clinic).\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"Inefficiencies in the manual procedures of Perfect Smile Dental Clinic inspired the development of The Perfect Smile Portal: A Web-Based Dental Clinic Management System. Manual methods in maintaining patient records, scheduling appointments, recording treatments, and managing bills delay clinic operations and risk data accuracy. Guided by the Agile Software Development Model, the researchers designed and implemented a web-based system composing of the Patient Records, Appointment Scheduling, Treatment History, Billing, Staff and User Management, and Reporting & Analytics modules. The system is designed to enhance efficiency for clinics by way of automation, security in data management, and real-time access. Evaluation results proved it to be effective and ready for deployment. Unit Testing recorded a functionality score of 0.98, showing the reliability of module performance; User Acceptance Testing recorded a score of 0.99, reflecting the high satisfaction of its staff and patient volunteers; and Security Testing recorded 1.0, showing strong authentication and protection of data. It successfully migrated the manual process to a digitized one for the clinic by enhancing the accuracy of the records, automating the scheduling and billing processes, streamlining the workflow of the staff, and securing sensitive information. For further enhancement, a mobile application, integration with dental imaging tools, and multi-branch reporting can be added. To sum up, the Perfect Smile Portal marks one of the most important steps toward modern, technology-driven management of the dental clinic.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 53, \"differences\": \"Different contexts: dental clinic vs. lying-in clinic; specific features differ significantly\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Digital management system\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 20, \"title\": \"DEVELOPMENT OF MULTI-BRANCH DENTAL PRACTICE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM WITH POINT-OF-SALE AND BUSINESS ANALYTICS FOR DR. WENNIE A. SAMPER DENTAL CLINIC\", \"reason\": \"Different domain: dental practice vs. lying-in clinic\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"This study presents the development of a comprehensive, web-based multi-branch dental practice management system designed to modernize the operations of Dr. Wennie A. Samper Dental Clinic by replacing inefficient, error-prone manual processes with an integrated digital solution. Developed using the Agile Scrum methodology, the system centralizes nine core modules including Electronic Medical Records, automated appointment scheduling, Point-of-Sale (POS) billing, and a business analytics dashboard to streamline cross-branch coordination and data-driven decision-making. Rigorous evaluation via black box, usability, performance, and security testing yielded perfect scores, confirming that the platform is highly functional and secure for immediate deployment. By automating administrative workflows and providing real-time operational insights, the system effectively eliminates documentation loss and billing conflicts while establishing a foundation for future enhancements such as teleconsultation and predictive analytics.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define the unique challenges and benefits of your system for the specific clinic context.\", \"archived_id\": 16, \"differences\": \"Different target users (dentists vs. midwives) and specific features (appointment scheduling, POS billing vs. medicine management)\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage patient records and inventory\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 15, \"title\": \"MEDICAL APPOINTMENT AND RECORD MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR NABUA RURAL HEALTH UNIT II\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on medical appointment and record management but target different institutions (lying-in clinic vs. rural health unit).\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The use of computer technology in several online transactions in medical facilities has made various operations and transactions fast and easy. The traditional way of setting appointments and managing records may result in heavy workloads and record loss. With these, this study was conducted to develop a system that will easily schedule appointments for patients with SMS notifications and manage records in RHU II. Generally, this study targets to develop a medical appointment and record management system to shift from the manual process of scheduling to online scheduling and managing patient records in RHU II. This study used a mixed-method research design to contextualize the data thematically and statistically. The respondents of this study were the physician and medical staff of the RHU II. Further, the system only covers the check-up and animal bite. In gathering the data, an interview, observation, and burp suite tool were used. The data gathered were analyzed and interpreted using thematic analysis and weighted mean. Based on analysis of the gathered data, in determining problems encountered in the scheduling process, record management, and data retrieval, researchers identified problems such as time-consuming in managing records, scheduling, and difficulty in retrieving data. Further, upon evaluation of the security performance of the system, it reveals that the system has a low severity with a weighted mean of 1.21 which can protect itself from XSS, SQL injection, and Session Hijacking. Therefore, the Medical Appointment and Record Management System is reasonable enough to be used in the RHU II.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Specify the unique challenges and benefits of your system for the specific institution to differentiate it from the archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 62, \"differences\": \"One is specifically for a lying-in clinic; the other is for a rural health unit.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage appointments and records for healthcare facilities.\", \"academic_year\": \"2022\"}, {\"score\": 15, \"title\": \"INFORMATION SYSTEM STRATEGIC PLAN FOR BELEN LYING-IN CLINIC MANAGEMENT SYSTEM NABUA, CAMARINES SUR\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: patient records vs. inventory management\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"In the ever-changing business environment of today, organizations employ a three-year information system strategic planning process to synchronize their technological and business objectives, offering adaptability while also looking ahead to technology investments, current priorities, and maintaining competitiveness. In this connection, this generally aimed to create the Information System Strategic Plan for Belen Lying-In Clinic Management System Nabua, Camarines Sur. It specifically aimed to assess the current ICT status of Belen Lying-In Clinic; develop an Information System Strategic Plan for Belen Lying-In Clinic; and evaluate the Information System Strategic Plan based on the available ICT resource requirements of the Belen Lying-In Clinic In response to increasing data volume, Belen Lying-In Clinic faces challenges in managing equipment and inventory records. The objective is to enhance operational efficiency, data accuracy, and decision-making. However, financial constraints, technology availability, staff resistance, evolving regulations, and technological advances may limit implementation and long-term success. While the focus is on the Nabua, Camarines Sur branch, the research emphasizes system design over development, documenting details, and implementing a three-year information system plan. Data collection will involve from individuals currently employed at the Belen Lying-In Clinic in Nabua, Camarines Sur. Information will exclusively be gathered from this specific group within the clinic, and the study duration is limited to the next three years.This research utilized the descriptive research design. The respondents were the currently employed at the Belen Lying-In Clinic in Nabua, Camarines Sur. After the collection of the data through interview questionnaire, analysis was done using narrative analysis.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define your target users and specific features to avoid overlap with the archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 158, \"differences\": \"One focuses on patient records, the other on inventory; different users (clinic staff vs. patients) and specific features\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage medical records\", \"academic_year\": \"2023\"}, {\"score\": 15, \"title\": \"BARANGAY HEALTH CENTER INFORMATION RECORDS MANAGEMENT SYSTEM\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on digitalizing records for healthcare settings but differ in specific context (lying-in clinic vs. barangay health center).\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"In a highly technological society, human productivity is made more efficient through the development of electronic devices and gadgets. However, the case is different in Barangay Health Centers which still uses manual storing of files and computing, evidently using traditional approach as technology in rural areas is not yet developed. With these, the researchers come up with an idea that need to build a system that will help store the health records of patients make it more organized. Generally, the purpose of this system is to make staffs lessen the manual storage of data and make it easier to manage their transaction towards keeping, updating, deleting, editing, and searching patient’s information. To address the general and specific objectives of the study, the researchers used a mixed method research design and the Extreme Programming (XP) as the software development methodology. It is useful for collecting, analyzing, and interpreting data. The respondents of this study were the patients, Barangay Health Center staff and health workers. The data was obtained using an interview guide, Black Box Testing and the data was evaluated and interpreted using a weighted mean. The research findings indicate that there are problems in the data requirements needed for the system. As a result, the overall interpretation demonstrated that the proposed is beneficial the proposed system is beneficial to the respondents. As a result, this is a perfect opportunity to put the Barangay Health Center Information Records Management System into implementation.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 55, \"differences\": \"Scope and specific features differ significantly\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Digitalizing patient records\", \"academic_year\": \"2022\"}]', '[{\"id\": 91, \"name\": \"Grom Hellscream\", \"role\": \"adviser\", \"reason\": \"Holds the adviser role, with expertise in General.\", \"expertise\": \"General\", \"role_label\": \"Adviser\"}]', '2026-09-13 01:51:59', '2026-09-13 01:51:59');
INSERT INTO `duplication_checks` (`id`, `student_s_y_id`, `document_path`, `concepts`, `top_score`, `verdict`, `matches`, `instructors_suggested`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(10, 11, 'duplication-checks/Laq3PhUswy7ZC3zgEMUQJfQ7SAoYHa3hC2wDX2gQ.pdf', '{\"sdm\": \"Agile Development Methodology\", \"scope\": \"Project & Contract Management; Geospatial Mapping & Area Tracking; Timeline & Progress Monitoring; Automated Alerts; Comprehensive Reporting; Document Archiving; AI Intelligence Engine\", \"title\": \"PROJ-TRACK: An Integrated Monitoring and Automated Notification System for CSPC-PPFMS\", \"domain\": \"Web System\", \"keywords\": [\"PROJ-TRACK\", \"Integrated Monitoring\", \"Automated Notification\", \"CSPC-PPFMS\", \"Geospatial Mapping\", \"Area Tracking\", \"AI Intelligence Engine\", \"Agile Development Methodology\"], \"sdg_goals\": \"SDG 9 – Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure; SDG 11 – Sustainable Cities and Communities; SDG 16 – Peace, Justice, and Strong Institutions\", \"main_topic\": \"Development of a web-based system for monitoring and managing infrastructure projects at CSPC-PPFMS.\", \"limitations\": \"Connectivity; Data Entry; Integration; AI Accuracy; Geospatial Precision\", \"target_users\": \"Administrators of CSPC-PPFMS\", \"technologies\": [\"Google Maps API\", \"AI Intelligence Engine\"], \"research_agenda\": [\"Process Automation\", \"Information Science\", \"Smart Computing\", \"Business Administration and Management\"], \"problem_statement\": \"The CSPC Office of the Director - PPFMS currently relies on manual, paper-based records to monitor infrastructure, leading to risks of lost documents and delayed reporting, and a lack of spatial visualization.\", \"proposed_solution\": \"The project proposes a web-based system that centralizes project records and provides automated notifications, integrating the Google Maps API for geospatial mapping and area tracking.\"}', 70, 'High Similarity', '[{\"score\": 70, \"title\": \"RESEARCH PROJECT INFORMATION MANAGEMENT AND TRACKING SYSTEM\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on managing research project information and progress for an AI Research Center.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"Through Research Project Information Management, the researchers come up with the idea to lessen the work in the AI Research Center for Community Development, or AIRCoDe, by managing and tracking the research project and its progress. Hence, this study aimed to develop a web-based system entitled “Research Project Information Management and Tracking System”, (RPIMTS) that help faculties and researchers in managing each research projects. The RPIMTS is paperless-based management system in which the researchers who are willing to propose new research can find it easier to apply their research. Applying for exploratory research, this study considered the data provided by the director, staff, researchers, and reviewers in the AIRCoDe. The researchers used stratified sampling techniques to gather data. The Blackbox testing for AIRCoDe’s system results reveal low vulnerability risk, excellent performance, and full functionality, with no detected errors. of the system. The researcher used the Extreme Programming (XP) phases for the development of the system, and by doing so, they created a great RPIMTS. By exploring the functionalities of the AIRCoDe, the researchers created a process flow that serves as a guide for every user that will use the system. After the development of the system, it undergoes testing, such as Use Case Testing, Performance Testing, and Security Testing, to show its level of functionality for use case testing, its level of vulnerability for security testing, and its level of response for performance testing. By those tests, it gives the results of passing those tests. The findings of this study may serve as a fundamental basis for the researchers to use the system in managing and tracking the research project and its progress.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clarify the specific scope of your project to avoid overlap with the archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 75, \"differences\": \"Scope differs slightly: one manages physical infrastructure, the other academic research.\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"Integrated monitoring and automated notification for infrastructure projects; web-based system for managing research projects\", \"academic_year\": \"2023\"}, {\"score\": 70, \"title\": \"OptiCCS: AN INTEGRATED SYSTEM FOR MONITORING AND MANAGING COMPUTER AND LABORATORY EQUIPMENT FOR THE COLLEGE OF COMPUTER STUDIES\", \"reason\": \"Both focus on integrated monitoring and management systems for computer equipment, targeting the same institution and users.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The College of Computer Studies (CCS) at Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges struggles with inefficient paper-based laboratory management that lacks real-time monitoring for student activity and equipment. To address this, the researchers developed OptiCCS, an integrated web- based system for laboratory and equipment management. The system, built using Agile Scrum methodology, integrates a web application with a real-time monitoring application. The web application, developed on the CodeIgniter PHP framework with a MySQL database, manages inventory, class creation, role-based access, and report generation. The real-time monitoring service uses a Python client agent on each computer unit, connecting to a server built with React HTTP for API requests and the Ratchet WebSocket library for bi-directional communication, enabling live status reporting, screenshot feeds, violation detection, and remote command execution. The system uses Google OAuth for authentication. System validation involved black box testing for functionality, usability, and performance. Administrators, faculty, technicians, and students participated using a questionnaire, and the results were assessed based on the ISO 25010 software quality standard. Findings demonstrated a strong readiness for daily operation: Unit Testing yielded a mean score of 1.00, confirming components function as intended. User Acceptance Testing produced a mean score of 0.99, indicating the system meets end-user requirements. Stress Testing also achieved a mean score of 0.99, proving the system remains stable and responsive under load conditions. The study concludes that OptiCCS is a reliable and accepted solution capable of replacing the college’s manual methods with a centralized, efficient system that provides reliable real-time data for administrative decisions.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 13, \"differences\": \"Specific features differ slightly: OptiCCS uses real-time monitoring with a web application; PROJ-TRACK focuses on automated notifications and AI intelligence engine\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"Integrated monitoring and management system for computer equipment\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 34, \"title\": \"SPHERE: CSPC SPACE FACILITY AND EQUIPMENT RENTAL AND EVENT MANAGEMENT SYSTEM\", \"reason\": \"Not assessed - this one was outside the set the checker examined.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"This study developed SPHERE: CSPC Space Facility and Equipment Rental and Event Management System, a centralized web-based platform designed to address the inefficiencies of the manual, paper-based booking process used by the Supply and Property Management Office (SPMO) of Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges. The study specifically aimed to identify existing facility and equipment reservation procedures, develop a digital system that automates booking, documentation, and event management, and evaluate the system using Black-Box testing to assess functionality, security, performance, and compatibility. The system was developed through requirements analysis, system design, iterative development, and testing, incorporating features such as real-time availability monitoring, centralized booking management, automated document generation, billing computation, inventory tracking, booking status monitoring, and a QR code–based attendance mechanism. Evaluation results showed that SPHERE met the required quality standards, demonstrating reliable performance, secure data handling, high usability, and cross-device compatibility, while significantly reducing administrative workload and scheduling conflicts and improving transparency and operational efficiency. It is therefore recommended that SPHERE be fully adopted by CSPC and further enhanced through the integration of advanced reporting, expanded attendance analytics, and dynamic facility management to support scalability and continuous institutional digital transformation.\", \"assessed\": false, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"\", \"archived_id\": 44, \"differences\": \"\", \"is_relevant\": true, \"similarities\": \"\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 23, \"title\": \"GIS- INTEGRATED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR EVANGELICAL CEMETERY IN SANTIAGO, IRIGA CITY\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages infrastructure projects, the other cemetery records.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The Evangelical Cemetery in Santiago, Iriga City had experienced disadvantages that come along with the traditional way of keeping records, inefficient plot tracking, and limited access to burial information which led to data inaccuracies and service delays. In an attempt to solve the problem, a GIS-Integrated Management System was launched that would be helpful in the modernization of cemetery operations while also taking into consideration the local cultural and religious practices. The aim of the research was to devise, create a web-based system that includes functions for managing burial records, allocating and tracking plots, managing deceased profiles, providing notification services, and visualization of plots based on GIS technology. A black-box testing approach was taken to evaluate the system, wherein different testing methods like functional, integration, security, compatibility, and usability were applied. The total average score of 0.99 was achieved for both functional and integration testing, where integration got the highest rating of 1.00 meaning there was 100% module interaction. Secured, compatible, and usability testing then reported their average scores of 4.50, 4.46, and 4.48, respectively, which were all seen as Highly Functional. It can thus be concluded that the system is able to significantly enhance efficiency, accuracy, data security, and accessibility. Overall, the research work establishes the claim that GIS and web technologies can be easily and effectively combined to create a record management system and service delivery solution that works in a local context.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define the specific scope and target users for your system to avoid overlap with this archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 48, \"differences\": \"One focuses on physical infrastructure, the other on burial plots.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage records for monitoring and notifications.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 20, \"title\": \"ELEVATEGS: A PROGRESSIVE WEB APPLICATION LEARNING MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR GRADUATE SCHOOL OF USANT\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages infrastructure projects, the other learning management systems.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"This study developed ElevateGS a Progressive Web Application (PWA) Learning Management System, to address critical operational inefficiencies at the University of Saint Anthony (USANT) Graduate School, specifically the heavy reliance on manual grading, decentralized announcement channels, and scattered course management that complicates resource retrieval. Utilizing the Adapted Agile Scrum Framework, the system features a decoupled architecture with a PHP Laravel backend and Vue.js frontend, incorporating Service Workers and IndexedDB to enable offline synchronization and centralize academic materials. A mixed-method evaluation involving 60 respondents including faculty, students, and IT experts revealed that the system is \\\"Highly Functional\\\" (composite mean of 0.99), with a 100% success rate for offline capabilities. Usability was rated as \\\"High\\\" (weighted mean of 3.82) and user satisfaction as \\\"Good\\\" (System Usability Scale score of 78.76), confirming that ElevateGS successfully bridges the gap between fragmented, manual processes and digital demands by providing a centralized, and offline- capable platform for the graduate school.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define your specific problem and target users for a more distinct proposal.\", \"archived_id\": 19, \"differences\": \"Different subjects (infrastructure vs. learning management) and users\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage centralization of records/delays\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 20, \"title\": \"BJMP (Bureau of Jail Management and Penology) Record Management System with Electronic Head Counting\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages infrastructure projects, the other records inmates\' presence.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"In today\'s landscape, technology is pivotal, reshaping how we interact, work, and navigate our world. A streamlined Record Management System is vital for organized, accessible, and meticulous record-keeping, promoting accountability and informed decision-making. This study focuses on automating record management for Persons Deprived of Liberty (PDLs), ensuring accurate tracking. Using a Mixed-method approach, Iriga City District Jails Officers were interviewed for data collection, which underwent arithmetic mean analysis. Black box testing showed use case and requirement-based testing achieving a Completely Functional level with a 100 overall average. The application significantly addresses challenges in manual recording and counting of PDLs, justifying the BJMP Record Management System with Electronic Head Counting implementation. This system revolutionizes inmate record-keeping, ensuring accuracy and efficiency. It streamlines data entry, facilitates seamless retrieval and analysis, aiding decision-making and resource allocation. This technological advancement enhances correctional facility operations, showcasing BJMP\'s commitment to modernizing record management, fostering transparency, accountability, and optimal resource utilization.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define your target users and specific problem being solved to avoid overlap with this archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 89, \"differences\": \"One focuses on PPDs and infrastructure monitoring; the other on inmate presence tracking.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both involve automated record-keeping systems.\", \"academic_year\": \"2024\"}, {\"score\": 20, \"title\": \"WEB-BASED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM FOR CSPC’S PRODUCTION AND AUXILIARY SERVICES WITH INVETORY AND SALES TRACKING\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages infrastructure projects, the other production and auxiliary services.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"In an institution like the Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges, where operational efficiency and controlled use of resources is required, manual processes within the Production and Auxiliary Services (PAxS) office created a critical bottleneck. This resulted in records supposedly prone to errors and a significant lack of real-time visibility in inventory and sales. The Web-Based Management System for CSPC Production and Auxiliary Services with Inventory and Sales Tracking thus emerges as a transformational solution to revolutionize basic PAxS operations. This new web-based system specifically provides the accuracy required by setting up automated and centralized tracking of sales, inventory, and vehicle pass applications, thus improving overall accountability and administrative control. Automating these key workflows substantially reduces the administrative load on personnel and significantly increases the quality and expedience of service delivery. Developed using the Agile Scrum Methodology, the iterative, user-friendly process ensured the final system architecture—includin g User Account Management, User Ordering, Digital Vehicle Pass Application, Integrated Sales and Inventory Tracking, Payment Processing, and Comprehensive Report Generation modules—met all stakeholder requirements. To determine the system\'s quality and institutional readiness, comprehensive black-box testing was conducted in three important dimensions. The strict quantitative findings reveal the system to be viable: Functional Testing scored an outstanding 0.97 (High Functionality), proving all modules acted as per specifications. Performance Testing scored 0.88 (High Performance), indicating system stability and efficiency under full transaction load. Security Testing yielded 0.89 (Low Risk), which confirms strong controls were established to keep sensitive institutional information safe. The study\'s aims were achieved with the development of this web-based system, which provides PAxS with a stable, productive, and secure solution that significantly improves accountability, increases operational speed, and enables data-driven decision-making, making the platform applicable for large-scale institutional adoption.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define your specific institution and scope to avoid overlap with this archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 2, \"differences\": \"One focuses on infrastructure projects (PPFMS), the other on production and auxiliary services.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage project/asset monitoring and automated notifications.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 20, \"title\": \"WEB-BASED MANAGEMENT SYSTEM WITH SMS NOTIFICATION FOR BULA MUNICIPAL WATERWORKS\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages infrastructure projects, the other municipal waterworks.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"In Water utility services, effective operations are crucial to provide the consumers with good services. However, traditional methods of record management and information delivery may affect the timeliness and accuracy of daily operations. To address these, this study focused on developing a Web-Based Management System with SMS Notification to enhance the processes in Bula Municipal Waterworks System (BMWS), which currently serves over 3,000 consumers from 22 barangays. The web-based platform includes several key features, such as consumer management, bill generation, meter reading, consumer support, SMS notification, and reports generation, designed to ensure that billing cycles, service updates, and information control and retrieval are secure, timely and accurate. To guarantee a continuous improvement throughout the system development, the Agile Scrum framework was utilized, allowing flexibility in handling requirements. To evaluate the system, black box testing was conducted to assess both the functional and non-functional aspects of the system, particularly focusing on the functionality, complete workflow, performance, and security. The functionality tests using test cases and end-to-end tests using Selenium IDE showed perfect 1.0 scores, performance achieved 0. 85 (Good Performance) in a load test with Apache JMeter, and security scans using OWASP ZAP found no high risks out of the total 12 findings. The test results reflect the system\'s capability in handling management operations and speeding up processes, which will significantly decrease the workloads of the staff, while gaining consumer trust through transparency. Currently implemented at BMWS, the system helps the local water service transform in terms of modernization, paving the way for future improvements in scalability and community engagement.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Specify a more unique problem or target users to differentiate from the archived document.\", \"archived_id\": 5, \"differences\": \"One focuses on infrastructure projects (PROJ-TRACK) and the other on municipal waterworks.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage records and notifications for utility services.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 15, \"title\": \"IBARYO: GOVERNANCE AUTOMATED AND KPI MONITORING SYSTEM FOR PALOYON ORIENTAL, NABUA, CAMARINES SUR\", \"reason\": \"Different core domains: one manages infrastructure projects, the other barangay governance.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"This study developed iBaryo, a web-based governance system designed to help Barangay Paloyon Oriental manage tasks and services more efficiently. Before the system, the barangay relied on manual paperwork that caused delays, missing records, and difficulty in tracking responsibilities and officials’ performance. With iBaryo, barangay operations are centralized in one platform, including role-based task assignments, online document requests, complaint submissions, event scheduling, census records, real-time notifications, and analytics for monitoring performance. It also uses Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) to check how well officials complete their tasks and respond to residents. The system was created using the Agile method and tested for functionality, usability, efficiency, and security, and results showed that it works well, is easy to use, fast, and secure. Overall, iBaryo makes barangay management more organized, transparent, and convenient for both officials and residents, while reducing paperwork and improving accountability. Future upgrades may include national database integration, predictive features, and a mobile app for better accessibility.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define your specific problem and target users to avoid overlap with iBaryo.\", \"archived_id\": 24, \"differences\": \"One focuses on project monitoring; the other on governance and KPI monitoring.\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"Both manage automated systems for monitoring and notification.\", \"academic_year\": \"2025\"}, {\"score\": 12, \"title\": \"BATO FARMLAND GEOLOCATION AND MAPPING SYSTEM\", \"reason\": \"Different core domain: one manages infrastructure projects, the other farmland mapping.\", \"authors\": null, \"program\": \"BSIT\", \"abstract\": \"The \\\"Bato Farmland Geolocation and Mapping System\\\" is a functional and user-friendly system when it comes to management and land mapping. This addresses the issues associated with manual recording and tracking of registered and insured farmers specifically in the Municipality of Bato. The system, which was specifically built for the Municipal Agriculture Office of Bato, aims to enhance efficiency, and reduce errors in farmers\' registration and tracking of farmland. It is primarily aimed at the office admin and staff that provides real-time monitoring and tracking of every farmland of registered farmers. The system provides accurate data on the location of the land area that serves as a guide to staff during the field visit for data collection. To ensure the level of functionality of the system, the system undergoes several test methods using black-box testing, where the use case and requirement-based testing were applied. The geolocation and mapping solution, developed in response to recognized concerns with manual tracking, of the registered farm and eliminates the need for manual data entry, offering a more efficient digital interface for users. The results of use case testing show a high degree of functionality, with an average mean of 0.98 (Highly Functional). Requirements-based testing confirms its efficacy, with a mean score of 0.98 (Highly Functional). The system\'s performance and alignment with objectives are supported by Local Government of Bato, input from administrators, and staff. “Bato Farmland Geolocation and Mapping System \\\" is set to transform municipal agricultural office administration by offering efficiency, accuracy and user-friendly system.\", \"assessed\": true, \"matched_on\": [], \"suggestion\": \"Clearly define your specific problem and target users to avoid confusion with unrelated systems.\", \"archived_id\": 72, \"differences\": \"Different subjects (infrastructure vs. farmland) and users (students vs. farmers)\", \"is_relevant\": false, \"similarities\": \"No genuine overlap beyond generic wording\", \"academic_year\": \"2023\"}]', '[{\"id\": 91, \"name\": \"Grom Hellscream\", \"role\": \"adviser\", \"reason\": \"Holds the adviser role, with expertise in General.\", \"expertise\": \"General\", \"role_label\": \"Adviser\"}]', '2026-09-13 01:54:59', '2026-09-13 01:54:59'),
